<node id="Yellow mealworms (Tenebrio molitor larvae)">
  <data key="d0">Yellow mealworms (Tenebrio molitor larvae)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Yellow mealworms are larvae of the darkling beetle Tenebrio molitor, capable of consuming and degrading various plastics including PS, LDPE, PP, PVC, and PLA. They are also used commercially as animal feed and as a sustainable protein source.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms, the larvae of Tenebrio molitor, are studied for their ability to biodegrade polylactic acid (PLA) as part of sustainable waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms, scientifically known as Tenebrio molitor larvae, were used in experiments to isolate new PS-degrading bacterial strains from their intestines.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381965</data>
</node>
<node id="Superworms (Zophobas atratus larvae)">
  <data key="d0">Superworms (Zophobas atratus larvae)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Superworms are larvae of Zophobas atratus, identified as plastic-consuming species that can ingest recalcitrant plastics such as PE and PS.&lt;SEP&gt;Larvae of Zophobas atratus, from which Pseudomonas sp. was isolated for polystyrene biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms, the larvae of Zophobas atratus (Coleoptera: Tenebrionidae), are studied for their ability to depolymerize polyethylene and polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms are insects studied for their ability to degrade polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms, specifically Zophobas atratus larvae, are reported to have the ability to eat plastics such as polystyrene and polyethylene, with their gut microbes playing an essential role in plastic digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms (Zophobas atratus larvae) were studied for their ability to degrade polystyrene in their gut.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e</data>
