<node id="Enterobacter sp.">
  <data key="d0">Enterobacter sp.</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Enterobacter sp. is a bacterial species isolated from the gut of greater wax moth larvae, possibly involved in polyethylene (PE) degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. is a bacterial genus isolated from the gut of Indian mealmoth larvae, capable of LDPE degradation, and associated with PP degradation in Z. atratus larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. is a bacterium isolated from the gut of the greater wax moth, contributing to polyethylene (PE) degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. is a bacterial genus associated with PP diets in the gut microbiome of Zophobas atratus larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a</data>
