<node id="Incubators">
  <data key="d0">Incubators</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Incubators maintained at 25 °C and 70% humidity were used to store polypropylene containers with mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Incubators were used to house mealworms during the experiment, with three incubators for each incubation time.&lt;SEP&gt;Incubators maintained at 25°C and 70% humidity were used to store the mealworm containers during the experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Controlled experimental environments used to maintain mealworms at specific temperatures and humidity levels during biodegradation tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Incubators housed the mealworms during the experiments and showed visible differences in PS residue depending on feed type.&lt;SEP&gt;Incubators housed the larvae during the antibiotic suppression test, from which samples were randomly chosen.</data>
