<node id="Tetrahydrofuran (THF)">
  <data key="d0">Tetrahydrofuran (THF)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is an organic solvent and chemical reagent widely employed in experimental and analytical studies, particularly those involving polymer degradation and extraction. In the referenced research, THF of high purity (anhydrous or GC grade, ≥99.9%) was used to ensure reliable and uncontaminated results. It served multiple roles, including functioning as a solvent in Soxhlet extraction of plastic fragments from frass and as an eluent in gel permeation chromatography (GPC) analysis. THF was specifically applied to extract polystyrene (PS) and polyvinyl chloride (PVC), as well as degraded polystyrene products from fecula, enabling subsequent molecular weight determination and characterization of polymer residues. Additionally, THF was introduced into experimental samples to halt biological activity prior to analysis, thereby preserving the chemical integrity of the samples. Overall, Tetrahydrofuran (THF) was a critical reagent in the study, valued for its high purity, versatility, and effectiveness in polymer extraction, sample preparation, and analytical procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Tetrahydrofuran (THF) was used as a solvent for PS extraction in the biodegradation assays.&lt;SEP&gt;Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent with GC grade purity &gt; 99.9% used for PS extraction in the biodegradation study.&lt;SEP&gt;Tetrahydrofuran was the extraction solvent used for PS and PVC polymers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-838d20fb5f3709d303402ea916d8172f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387408</data>
</node>
