<node id="Germany">
  <data key="d0">Germany</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">Germany is a European country that serves as a significant hub for scientific research, technology, and industrial innovation, particularly in the fields of life sciences, analytical instrumentation, and laboratory equipment. It is home to several globally recognized companies that supply reagents, instruments, and advanced technologies for research and industry. Among these are Sigma-Aldrich and Carl Zeiss AG, both of which are key suppliers of reagents and precision equipment. Germany is also the headquarters of Qiagen, a leading provider of sample and assay technologies, and Brock Instruments, a manufacturer specializing in ATR-FTIR equipment.  

The country hosts Walldorf, a notable location where Thermo Scientific operates, further emphasizing Germany’s role as a base for major scientific enterprises. Additionally, Bruker and Leica, both headquartered in Germany, are internationally renowned for their contributions to analytical and imaging technologies, with their equipment frequently used in experimental research. The Agilent 6540 UHD Accurate-Mass mass spectrometer is also identified as originating from Germany, highlighting the nation’s role in the development and distribution of high-precision analytical tools.  

Germany is further associated with Heilna Trade GmbH and Bruker Corporation, reinforcing its position as a center for companies engaged in scientific trade and instrumentation. Beyond its industrial and technological contributions, Germany has also been noted in scientific studies as one of the European countries where mealworms were observed consuming polystyrene (PS) foam, reflecting its involvement in environmental and biological research.  

Overall, Germany stands out as a central location for leading scientific companies, advanced instrumentation, and innovative research, making it a cornerstone of global progress in science and technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Germany is mentioned as the location of Bruker Corporation.&lt;SEP&gt;Germany is the country where Bruker Corporation is located.&lt;SEP&gt;Germany is the country where Elementar and Bruker are based.&lt;SEP&gt;Germany is the country where Qiagen is based.</data>
