<node id="35-Day Feeding Experiment">
  <data key="d0">35-Day Feeding Experiment</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A 35-day feeding experiment was conducted to study mealworm survival, microbial community analysis, and foam degradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756370611</data>
</node>
<node id="Thermo Scientific">
  <data key="d0">Thermo Scientific</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermo Scientific is a global company specializing in the development and manufacture of scientific instruments, laboratory equipment, and analytical technologies. The company is associated with multiple international operations, including facilities in Walldorf, Germany, where it produces instruments such as the Microm HM340E rotary microtome, and in Warsaw, Poland, where it provides laboratory kits and consumables, including the Pierce™ LDH Cytotoxicity Assay Kit.  

Thermo Scientific is widely recognized for its advanced spectroscopy and surface analysis systems that support research across chemistry, materials science, and life sciences. Its portfolio includes the K-Alpha X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy (XPS) system, which is used for surface chemical component analysis, as well as a range of Fourier Transform Infrared (FTIR) spectrometers. These include the Nicolet iS5 FTIR Spectrometer, applied in polymer functional group analysis; the Nicolet iS20 FTIR Spectrometer, designed for chemical analysis; and the Nicolet Magna IR-8700 FTIR system, used in advanced spectroscopic studies. Additionally, Thermo Scientific’s Attenuated Total Reflectance FTIR (ATR-FTIR) equipment has been employed in the characterization of polyethylene (PE) mulching films, demonstrating its role in agricultural and environmental research.  

Through its diverse instrumentation and laboratory solutions, Thermo Scientific supports a wide range of scientific applications, from cytotoxicity assays in biomedical research to structural and compositional analysis in materials science. The company’s global presence and comprehensive product portfolio make it a key provider of technologies that enable precise measurement, analysis, and innovation across multiple scientific disciplines.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermo Scientific is mentioned as the manufacturer of the X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy (XPS) equipment, located in Waltham, MA.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermo Scientific, USA, manufactured the Dionex ICS-6000 ion chromatographic system used for cation analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermo Scientific is a company based in the USA that provided the ion chromatographic system used in the analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermo Scientific is the provider of the GeneJET Gel Extraction Kit used for gel purification of PCR products.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermo Scientific is a company mentioned as the manufacturer of several laboratory kits and instruments used in the study, including the GeneJET Gel Extraction Kit, NanoDrop One Microvolume UV-Vis Spectrophotometer, CloneJET PCR Cloning Kit, and RapidOut DNA Removal Kit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37da2fbe64f85c50c36da45006f4c23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92b1e432ea4bee0f332d7303188e6de7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb1c38c1c6dc6fea84d8f51b9f706cd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512840a413df7ae3d881389c5cf1feb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385975</data>
</node>
<node id="Agilent">
  <data key="d0">Agilent</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Agilent is a global scientific instrumentation and technology company recognized for manufacturing a wide range of analytical instruments and laboratory solutions used across diverse fields of research and industry. In the context of polymer and chemical analysis, Agilent is the producer of several gel permeation chromatography (GPC) systems, including the PL-GPC 220, the 1260 GPC, and the 1100 series, which are widely employed for molecular weight determination and polymer characterization. These instruments are integral to gel permeation chromatography experiments, particularly in the study of polymers such as polyurethane (PU).  

In addition to GPC systems, Agilent manufactures the Cary 630 Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy (FTIR) instrument, which is used for molecular and structural analysis of chemical compounds. The company also provides solutions for bioanalytical applications, such as the RNA 6000 Nano LabChip Kit, designed for use with the Agilent Bioanalyzer 2100, enabling high-precision RNA quality and quantity assessments.  

Agilent’s expertise extends into chromatography and mass spectrometry. The company is the manufacturer of the Agilent 5975 gas chromatograph/mass spectrometer (GC/MS), a widely used system for chemical identification and quantification, as well as the Agilent 6890 N gas chromatograph, which has been applied in fatty acid analysis and other chemical studies.  

Overall, Agilent is consistently referenced as a key provider of high-performance analytical instruments, spanning applications in polymer science, spectroscopy, chromatography, mass spectrometry, and bioanalysis. Its instruments are recognized for their reliability and precision, making Agilent a central contributor to advanced scientific research and laboratory practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Agilent is a company based in Germany that provided the UHPLC system (Agilent 1290) and the quadrupole Time-Of-Flight mass spectrometer (Agilent 6540 UHD Accurate-Mass).&lt;SEP&gt;A company providing the GC-MS system (Agilent 7890A/5975C, USA) used for analyzing intermediates and products from plastic biodegradation.</data>
