<node id="TGA (Thermogravimetric Analysis)">
  <data key="d0">TGA (Thermogravimetric Analysis)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">TGA is a thermal analysis method measuring mass changes of a sample over time as temperature changes, used to study thermal stability and composition of materials.&lt;SEP&gt;TGA is an analytical technique used to measure weight loss and thermal stability changes in polyether-PU foam after digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;TGA is the analytical method used to detect thermal modification of Styrofoam after larval digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;TGA was used to detect thermal modification of larvae from Styrofoam to frass, analyzing decomposition patterns.</data>
