  <data key="d2">Carbon is an element detected on the surface of polyether-PU foam, with its proportion increasing after mealworm ingestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon was detected in LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads after biodegradation through elemental analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon content in LDPE, HDPE, and PS was measured before and after degradation by PM S1, showing significant loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon is described as a major component of PE polymers and a nutrient source for larvae.</data>
