<node id="Nitrogen">
  <data key="d0">Nitrogen</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitrogen is an element detected on the surface of polyether-PU foam, with its proportion decreasing after mealworm ingestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen was monitored in LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads after biodegradation using a Thermal Conductivity detection system.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen was identified as a key biochemical element in the digestive system, associated with intensive biochemical changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen is described as an essential element for protein and nucleic acid synthesis, and a limiting factor in PE-fed larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen concentration in frass was measured as part of the biodegradation study.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen levels were measured in frass and biomass, showing retention due to oxidative stress conditions during PS biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen is a compound with a covalent triple bond, referenced in the context of nitrogen fixation.</data>
