<node id="Simpson Index">
  <data key="d0">Simpson Index</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Simpson index is a diversity measure used to evaluate the evenness of microbial communities in the gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Simpson index is a diversity estimator used to measure bacterial richness in gut microbiomes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Simpson index was used to measure bacterial richness, which decreased in superworms and yellow mealworms fed with plastic diets.&lt;SEP&gt;The Simpson index is an ecological metric used to quantify dominance and evenness in gut microbiome studies of T. molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;The Simpson Index was used to measure alpha diversity of microbial communities, showing no significant differences among diets.&lt;SEP&gt;The Simpson index is a diversity estimator used to measure gut fungal community diversity in yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;The Simpson index is a diversity measure used to estimate species richness, with values indicating differences between PS and CT samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
