  <data key="d2">PCoA is a statistical method used to analyze differences in gut microbiome composition between bran-fed and PU-fed mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;A method used to analyze microbial community composition, showing distinct clustering of PS and CS groups from CB group.&lt;SEP&gt;PCoA is a statistical method used to visualize microbial community clustering based on Bray–Curtis dissimilarity.&lt;SEP&gt;PCoA was applied to analyze differences in gut microbiome composition under different feeding conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Principal Coordinate Analysis (PCoA) was performed to compare gut microbial communities across different diet groups.</data>
