<node id="Z. atratus larvae">
  <data key="d0">Z. atratus larvae</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Z. atratus larvae show increased abundance of Enterobacter sp. associated with PP degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of larvae (superworms) used in the biodegradation experiments, subjected to different feeding treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;Z. atratus larvae are large-sized mature larvae studied for their cannibalism behavior under nutritional limitation and their ability to consume and biodegrade polypropylene (PP).&lt;SEP&gt;Z. atratus larvae (Coleoptera: Tenebrionidae) are insects studied for their ability to biodegrade commercial PS products.</data>
