  <data key="d2">The gut microbial community refers to the microorganisms present in the digestive systems of larvae such as T. molitor, which change in composition when fed polyether-PU foam.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbial community refers to the bacterial populations within T. molitor larvae, analyzed to understand their role in PP biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microbial community refers to the microorganisms present in the digestive system of Tenebrio larvae, studied for diversity and shifts under different diets.</data>
