<node id="Tian, R.">
  <data key="d0">Tian, R.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Tian, R. is a researcher recognized for significant contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, with a particular focus on the role of mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor* larvae) in breaking down synthetic polymers. As both an author and co-author, Tian, R. has participated in multiple studies that investigate the ability of mealworms to ingest and metabolize plastics such as polystyrene, polyethylene, and mixtures of different polymer types. This body of work has provided important experimental evidence demonstrating that mealworms can consume and partially degrade these persistent materials, thereby offering a potential biological pathway for mitigating the global challenge of plastic waste accumulation.  

Much of Tian, R.’s research, particularly studies published around 2018, has been widely cited in the scientific literature. These studies have been instrumental in advancing understanding of insect-mediated plastic degradation, documenting not only the capacity of mealworms to process plastics but also exploring the biochemical and microbial mechanisms that facilitate this process. By examining both the efficiency and underlying factors of plastic biodegradation in mealworms, Tian, R. has contributed to shaping scientific discourse on sustainable and innovative waste management strategies.  

Overall, Tian, R.’s work positions mealworms as a promising model organism for developing eco-friendly approaches to reducing synthetic polymer pollution. Through co-authored and referenced studies on polyethylene and plastic mixtures, Tian, R. has played a key role in building the foundation for insect-based solutions to environmental plastic pollution and in highlighting the potential of biological systems to address one of the most pressing ecological challenges of modern times.&lt;SEP&gt;Tian, R. is a co-author of the 2018 study on biodegradation of polyethylene and plastic mixtures in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Tian, R. is an author of a study on biodegradation of polyethylene in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of a study on biodegradation of polystyrene and plastic mixtures in mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f3828bbe45c2c38004a29d55dcbf40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33180d5b7e1ebfedf8de59ba1a2a2d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20bc31ca22e33a7b244779745e9eeb73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602bba09eb2c308c400b412f39f4adb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ee089593160e720e507848fa8c917a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48</data>
