<node id="Ning, D.">
  <data key="d0">Ning, D.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ning, D. is a researcher recognized for significant contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, with a particular focus on the role of mealworms in breaking down synthetic polymers. Their work has centered on investigating the ability of yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) to ingest, metabolize, and degrade persistent plastics, including polystyrene, polyethylene, and mixtures of different plastic types. Through a series of co-authored studies, Ning, D. has provided experimental evidence that mealworms are capable of consuming and processing these materials, thereby presenting a potential biological pathway for addressing the environmental challenges posed by plastic waste.  

A key contribution from Ning, D. is a 2018 publication in *Chemosphere*, which examined the biodegradation of polystyrene wastes in yellow mealworms. This study demonstrated that mealworms could not only ingest but also metabolize polystyrene, supporting the concept that insect-mediated degradation may serve as a sustainable waste management strategy. Building upon this foundation, Ning, D. has co-authored additional research extending these findings to polyethylene and plastic mixtures, thereby broadening the scientific understanding of the scope and mechanisms underlying mealworm-driven plastic degradation.  

Collectively, Ning, D.’s research has been instrumental in advancing knowledge of insect-based biodegradation processes. By documenting both the occurrence and mechanisms of plastic digestion in mealworms, their work has highlighted the potential of biological systems as innovative and sustainable solutions to the global problem of plastic pollution. Through these contributions, Ning, D. has helped establish a foundation for further exploration of insect-mediated biodegradation as a viable strategy for mitigating the environmental impacts of synthetic polymer waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of a referenced study on biodegradation of polystyrene by yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Ning, D. is a co-author of the 2018 study on biodegradation of polyethylene and plastic mixtures in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the polystyrene biodegradation study.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of a study on enhancing bioenergy production with carbon capture of microalgae.&lt;SEP&gt;Ning, D. is one of the authors of a 2018 study (details truncated in text).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33180d5b7e1ebfedf8de59ba1a2a2d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-352650a946ab941cec3f7b9813faeee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20bc31ca22e33a7b244779745e9eeb73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602bba09eb2c308c400b412f39f4adb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72a9944bcd114b6a3be55ad9b596c77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90</data>
