<node id="Achatina fulica">
  <data key="d0">Achatina fulica</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Achatina fulica, commonly known as the giant African land snail, is a terrestrial gastropod species that has attracted scientific interest for its potential role in plastic biodegradation. Research has demonstrated that this species is capable of ingesting and disintegrating various synthetic polymers, including expanded polystyrene (PS) and expanded polyethylene, highlighting its relevance in studies of plastic waste management. Notably, Achatina fulica has been shown to degrade polystyrene plastics independently of its intestinal microflora, suggesting that the snail itself possesses intrinsic mechanisms for breaking down these materials.  

Beyond its role in polystyrene degradation, Achatina fulica has also been investigated in relation to other plastics. A 2019 study examined the uptake and potential adverse effects of polyethylene terephthalate (PET) microplastics in this species following soil exposure, underscoring its importance as a model organism for assessing environmental impacts of microplastic pollution. Collectively, these findings position Achatina fulica as a significant subject in biodegradation and ecotoxicological research, with implications for both waste reduction strategies and understanding the ecological consequences of plastic contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;Land snails studied for their ability to biodegrade expanded polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Achatina fulica, a species of land snail, is studied for its uptake, adverse effects, and biodegradation of microplastics and expanded polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Achatina fulica is a species of land snail studied for its ability to biodegrade and disintegrate expanded polystyrene.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173</data>
