<node id="Song, Y.">
  <data key="d0">Song, Y.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Song, Y. is a researcher whose work centers on the biodegradation of plastics and the environmental and biological impacts of micro- and nanoplastics. Their research has been instrumental in advancing scientific understanding of how synthetic polymers, including polystyrene, polyethylene, and polyethylene terephthalate (PET), interact with living organisms and ecosystems.  

Song, Y. is best known as a co-author of a landmark 2015 study published in *Environmental Science &amp; Technology* that demonstrated the ability of mealworms to consume and metabolize polystyrene. This study provided the first clear evidence that certain invertebrates can biologically degrade and mineralize persistent plastic materials, offering a potential biological pathway for mitigating plastic waste. Building on this work, Song, Y. has co-authored additional studies that expanded the range of organisms identified as capable of plastic degradation, including research on the biodegradation of expanded polystyrene by land snails. Their investigations have also extended to microbial contributions, such as identifying bacterial strains from waxworm guts that can degrade polyethylene, highlighting the role of microorganisms in plastic breakdown.  

In addition to biodegradation, Song, Y. has conducted extensive research on the ecological and toxicological effects of microplastics and nanoplastics. Their studies have examined the impacts of PET microplastics on snails, intestinal damage caused by microplastic ingestion in zebrafish and nematodes, and cellular-level effects of nanoplastics, including mitochondrial damage in human cells. These findings underscore the potential risks of plastic pollution to terrestrial and aquatic organisms, as well as to human health.  

Overall, Song, Y.’s research profile is defined by two interconnected themes: the potential for biological systems—including invertebrates and microorganisms—to degrade plastics, and the ecological and physiological consequences of micro- and nanoplastic exposure. Through this dual focus, Song, Y. has made significant contributions to the fields of biodegradation research and environmental toxicology, shaping current understanding of both the opportunities for biological plastic remediation and the risks posed by plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Song, Y. is a co-author of multiple studies on nanoplastics, including effects on human cells, terrestrial snails, and biodegradation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Description not available in text.&lt;SEP&gt;Song, Y. is an author of a study on biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Song, Y. is one of the authors of the study on breast cancer mice and polybrominated diphenyl ether-47, and also co-authored a study on biodegradation of expanded polystyrene by land snails.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of studies on biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene by plastic-eating mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb2c1ef38dbbafa838f87d5f4d6fd6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce368b44455642f4b9a1dacc4cdf0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1684575ed5f73a2ebe1adc7fbbb3b942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48</data>
