<node id="He, D.">
  <data key="d0">He, D.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">He, D. is a researcher and author whose work primarily focuses on the environmental impacts of plastics, particularly microplastics, and their biodegradation. He, D. has co-authored several studies investigating the potential of biological organisms to degrade synthetic polymers. Notably, this includes research on the biodegradation and disintegration of expanded polystyrene and polyethylene by land snails, highlighting the role of terrestrial invertebrates in addressing plastic pollution. In addition to biodegradation studies, He, D. has contributed to research on the occurrence and effects of microplastics. This includes a 2018 study demonstrating that microplastic particles can cause intestinal damage in zebrafish and nematodes, providing important insights into the toxicological impacts of microplastics on aquatic and soil organisms. Furthermore, He, D. co-authored a 2020 study examining the presence of microplastics in traditional medicinal materials, expanding the scope of microplastic research to human-related products and potential exposure pathways. Collectively, He, D.’s body of work integrates ecological, toxicological, and biodegradation perspectives, contributing to a broader understanding of how plastics interact with biological systems and exploring potential biological solutions to plastic pollution.</data>
