<node id="Wei, R.">
  <data key="d0">Wei, R.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Wei, R. is a researcher and author recognized for significant contributions to the field of plastic biodegradation and recycling, with a particular focus on enzymatic and microbial approaches. Their work spans multiple studies addressing the environmental challenge of synthetic polymer waste, especially petroleum-based plastics such as polyethylene terephthalate (PET) and polyurethane.  

Wei, R. has authored and co-authored several influential studies on biotechnological plastic degradation and recycling. This includes research on microbial enzymes capable of breaking down petroleum-derived plastics, with a notable 2017 study that advanced understanding of enzymatic recycling strategies. Their work also extends to the biodegradation of polyurethane, where they investigated the role of Tenebrio molitor larvae in breaking down this widely used but environmentally persistent material.  

In the area of enzymatic plastic degradation, Wei, R. has contributed to the development and characterization of thermostable PETase variants and thermostable polyester hydrolases, enzymes engineered to withstand higher temperatures and thereby improve the efficiency of PET hydrolysis. Additionally, they co-authored a study on thermophilic whole-cell degradation of polystyrene terephthalate using engineered *Clostridium thermocellum*, highlighting innovative microbial engineering approaches for plastic recycling.  

Beyond research articles, Wei, R. has also served as editor of the book *Enzymatic Plastic Degradation*, which consolidates knowledge in the field and provides a comprehensive resource on the use of enzymes for addressing plastic pollution.  

Overall, Wei, R.’s body of work reflects a sustained focus on advancing biotechnological solutions to plastic waste, combining enzyme engineering, microbial systems, and applied biodegradation studies to contribute to the development of sustainable recycling technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of a study on biodegradation and up-cycling of polyurethanes.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of a study on biodegradation of polyurethane foam in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Wei, R. is one of the authors of a 2019 study on biocatalytic degradation efficiency of polyethylene terephthalate packaging.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of a 2017 study on microbial enzymes for recycling petroleum-based plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Description not available in text.&lt;SEP&gt;Wei, R. is an author of a study on the biodegradation of polyether-polyurethane foam in Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
