<node id="Yellow mealworms (Tenebrio molitor)">
  <data key="d0">Yellow mealworms (Tenebrio molitor)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Larvae shown to biodegrade polystyrene and polypropylene, with studies on their life cycle and gut microbes.&lt;SEP&gt;Larvae used in the study to test biodegradation of polystyrene under different feeding strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms studied for their ability to biodegrade polypropylene and polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms (T. molitor) are larvae studied for their ability to ingest and degrade disposable surgical masks and plastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f</data>
