  <data key="d5">1756386557</data>
</node>
<node id="Andrew Flanagan, J.C.">
  <data key="d0">Andrew Flanagan, J.C.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Andrew Flanagan, J.C. is a researcher and author recognized for his contributions to studies on environmental sustainability and biodegradation. He is notably a co-author of a 2018 study published in *Chemosphere* that investigated the biodegradation of polystyrene wastes by yellow mealworms. This research explored the capacity of mealworms to consume and break down polystyrene, a persistent plastic pollutant, thereby contributing to the growing body of knowledge on biological solutions for plastic waste management. In addition to this work, Andrew Flanagan, J.C. has also co-authored research focused on enhancing bioenergy production through the integration of carbon capture in microalgae systems. His scholarly contributions reflect an interest in innovative, biologically driven approaches to addressing environmental challenges, particularly in the areas of plastic degradation and sustainable energy production.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-352650a946ab941cec3f7b9813faeee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
