<node id="Cai, S.Y.">
  <data key="d0">Cai, S.Y.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cai, S.Y. is a researcher recognized for contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly focusing on the role of yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) in breaking down synthetic polymers. Cai, S.Y. has co-authored multiple scientific studies investigating the capacity of mealworms to digest and degrade plastics, with a particular emphasis on polystyrene. Among these works, Cai, S.Y. is listed as an author of a notable 2018 study published in *Chemosphere* that examined the biodegradation of polystyrene wastes in yellow mealworms. This research provided important insights into the potential of insect-based systems for mitigating plastic pollution by demonstrating that mealworms can consume and metabolize polystyrene, a widely used but environmentally persistent plastic. Through these contributions, Cai, S.Y. has helped advance understanding of biological pathways for plastic degradation and the potential applications of insect-mediated processes in addressing global plastic waste challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the polystyrene biodegradation study.&lt;SEP&gt;Cai, S.Y. is an author of a study on biodegradation of plastics in Tenebrio genus.&lt;SEP&gt;Cai, S.Y. is a co-author of studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Cai, S.Y. is one of the authors of a 2018 study (details truncated in text).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-352650a946ab941cec3f7b9813faeee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
