</node>
<node id="Fan, H.Q.">
  <data key="d0">Fan, H.Q.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Fan, H.Q. is a researcher recognized for contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly focusing on the role of yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) in the digestion and breakdown of polystyrene waste. As a co-author of multiple scientific studies, including a 2018 publication, Fan, H.Q. has investigated the capacity of mealworms to consume and metabolize polystyrene, a widely used synthetic polymer that poses significant environmental challenges due to its persistence and resistance to natural degradation. The research emphasizes both the biodegradation process and the ubiquity of polystyrene digestion within yellow mealworms, highlighting their potential as a biological agent for mitigating plastic pollution. Through this body of work, Fan, H.Q. has contributed to advancing understanding of insect-mediated plastic degradation and its implications for sustainable waste management and environmental remediation.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the polystyrene biodegradation study.&lt;SEP&gt;Fan, H.Q. is an author of a study on biodegradation of plastics in Tenebrio genus.&lt;SEP&gt;Fan, H.Q. is a co-author of studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c0c246e98a503a16ace92f28394b584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c</data>
