<node id="Wang, Z.Y.">
  <data key="d0">Wang, Z.Y.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Wang, Z.Y. is a researcher recognized for contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly focusing on the role of yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) in the digestion and breakdown of polystyrene waste. As a co-author of multiple studies, including a 2018 publication, Wang, Z.Y. has investigated the capacity of mealworms to consume and metabolize polystyrene, a widely used but environmentally persistent plastic. This body of work has explored both the biodegradation process itself and the broader ubiquity of polystyrene digestion within yellow mealworms, providing evidence that these insects can serve as a biological agent for reducing plastic waste. Through these studies, Wang, Z.Y. has contributed to advancing scientific understanding of insect-mediated plastic degradation and its potential applications in addressing global plastic pollution challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the polystyrene biodegradation study.&lt;SEP&gt;Wang, Z.Y. is an author of a study on biodegradation of plastics in Tenebrio genus.&lt;SEP&gt;Wang, Z.Y. is a co-author of studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c0c246e98a503a16ace92f28394b584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c</data>
