<node id="Ren, N.Q.">
  <data key="d0">Ren, N.Q.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ren, N.Q. is a researcher and author recognized for extensive contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly through the use of insect larvae. Their work focuses on the capacity of species such as yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) and superworms (*Zophobas atratus*) to degrade synthetic polymers, including polystyrene, polypropylene, and polyethylene. Ren, N.Q. has co-authored multiple studies in this field, with notable publications spanning from at least 2018 through 2021.  

In 2018, Ren, N.Q. co-authored a study that investigated the biodegradation of polystyrene waste by yellow mealworms, providing early evidence of the potential of insect larvae to contribute to plastic waste management. Building on this foundation, subsequent studies in 2020 and 2021 expanded the scope of research to include other common plastics such as polypropylene and polyethylene, as well as additional insect species like superworms. These studies collectively examined the mechanisms, efficiency, and environmental implications of insect-mediated plastic degradation.  

Through this body of work, Ren, N.Q. has contributed to advancing scientific understanding of biological solutions to plastic pollution. Their research highlights the potential role of insect larvae in mitigating the environmental impact of persistent plastic waste, offering insights into sustainable waste management strategies and the broader field of biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of multiple studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of studies on biodegradation of polypropylene and polyethylene by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the 2020 study on biodegradation of polyethylene and polystyrene by greater wax moth larva.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of multiple studies on plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Ren, N.Q. is a co-author of multiple studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms and superworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb2c1ef38dbbafa838f87d5f4d6fd6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
