<node id="Receveur, J.P.">
  <data key="d0">Receveur, J.P.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Receveur, J.P. is a researcher and co-author recognized for contributions to studies on the biodegradation and digestion of polystyrene by yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*). His work focuses on investigating the capacity of mealworms to consume and metabolize polystyrene, a common plastic waste material, and on demonstrating the ubiquity of this biodegradation process across mealworm populations. Through these studies, Receveur, J.P. has contributed to advancing scientific understanding of insect-mediated plastic degradation, highlighting the potential role of mealworms in addressing environmental challenges associated with polystyrene waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of a 2018 study on ubiquity of polystyrene digestion and biodegradation within yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Receveur, J.P. is a co-author of studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c0c246e98a503a16ace92f28394b584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90</data>
