<node id="McClellan, R.L.">
  <data key="d0">McClellan, R.L.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">McClellan, R.L. is a researcher recognized for co-authoring scientific studies on the biodegradation of polystyrene by yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*). Their work focuses on the ubiquity of polystyrene digestion in mealworms, contributing to research that demonstrates the capacity of these insects to ingest and break down polystyrene, a common plastic pollutant. As a co-author, McClellan, R.L. has been involved in studies that highlight both the digestion and biodegradation processes of polystyrene within mealworms, providing evidence of the insects’ potential role in mitigating plastic waste. This body of research emphasizes the ecological and environmental significance of mealworms as a biological agent for plastic degradation and underscores McClellan, R.L.’s contributions to advancing knowledge in the field of plastic biodegradation and sustainable waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of a 2018 study on ubiquity of polystyrene digestion and biodegradation within yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;McClellan, R.L. is a co-author of studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c0c246e98a503a16ace92f28394b584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90</data>
