<node id="Zheng, M.">
  <data key="d0">Zheng, M.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zheng, M. is a researcher and co-author whose work primarily focuses on biodegradation processes, particularly involving plastic and organic pollutants. Zheng, M. is notably recognized for contributions to studies on the biodegradation of polystyrene by yellow mealworms (Tenebrio molitor). These studies, including a 2018 investigation, demonstrated the ubiquity and effectiveness of polystyrene digestion within mealworms, highlighting their potential role in mitigating plastic waste through biological processes. In addition to research on plastic degradation, Zheng, M. has also co-authored work on the enhanced biodegradation of quinoline and indole using a symbiotic system, indicating a broader interest in microbial and organism-assisted breakdown of persistent pollutants. Collectively, Zheng, M.’s research contributions emphasize the exploration of natural and symbiotic systems for addressing environmental challenges related to plastic and organic contaminant degradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90</data>
