<node id="Zhang, Y.L.">
  <data key="d0">Zhang, Y.L.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zhang, Y.L. is a researcher recognized for contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation by insects, particularly mealworms and superworms. Zhang has co-authored multiple scientific studies investigating the capacity of insect larvae to consume and degrade synthetic polymers such as polystyrene and low-density polyethylene. This body of work includes research on the ubiquity of polystyrene digestion in yellow mealworms (Tenebrio molitor larvae), as well as studies examining the biodegradation potential of superworms (Zophobas atratus or Zophobas morio larvae). In these studies, Zhang, Y.L. and collaborators have explored both the feeding behaviors of the larvae and the subsequent degradation effects on plastics, providing evidence that insect-based biodegradation could represent a promising avenue for addressing plastic waste. Through this research, Zhang, Y.L. has contributed to advancing scientific understanding of insect-mediated plastic degradation and its potential applications in environmental sustainability.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of a referenced study on biodegradation of polystyrene by dark mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Zhang, Y.L. is an author of a study on the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the 2010 study on Zophobas morio and 2019 study on polystyrene biodegradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Zhang, Y.L. is a co-author of studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f</data>
