<node id="Benbow, M.E.">
  <data key="d0">Benbow, M.E.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Benbow, M.E. is a researcher recognized for significant contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, with a particular emphasis on the role of mealworms in breaking down polystyrene. Polystyrene, a synthetic polymer extensively used in packaging and consumer products, poses a major environmental challenge due to its persistence and resistance to natural degradation. Benbow’s work has focused on investigating the capacity of mealworms, specifically yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) and dark mealworms (*Tenebrio obscurus*), to ingest, metabolize, and degrade this material.  

Through a series of studies, including notable publications in 2018 and 2019, Benbow and collaborators provided evidence that both *T. molitor* and *T. obscurus* are capable of digesting polystyrene and contributing to its biodegradation. These investigations examined not only the ability of mealworms to consume polystyrene but also the ubiquity and effectiveness of this process, demonstrating that the insects can break down the polymer into smaller, less persistent components. The findings have been widely cited in the scientific discourse on biological solutions to plastic waste, underscoring the potential of insect-mediated biodegradation as a sustainable strategy for addressing plastic pollution.  

By documenting and analyzing the mechanisms through which mealworms process polystyrene, Benbow, M.E. has advanced scientific understanding of insect-based biodegradation and its implications for environmental sustainability. This body of research has contributed to the exploration of innovative, biologically driven approaches to waste reduction and has highlighted the promise of alternative methods for mitigating the global accumulation of plastics in ecosystems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f3828bbe45c2c38004a29d55dcbf40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713</data>
