<node id="Ding, M.Q.">
  <data key="d0">Ding, M.Q.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ding, M.Q. is a researcher and author whose work focuses on the biodegradation of synthetic plastics, particularly polypropylene and polyethylene, through insect-mediated processes. Ding has co-authored multiple studies investigating the capacity of yellow mealworms (Tenebrio molitor larvae) and superworms (Zophobas atratus larvae) to degrade these persistent polymers. This research explores both the direct consumption of plastics by the larvae and the role of their gut microbiomes in facilitating biodegradation.  

In particular, Ding has contributed to studies examining the biodegradation of polypropylene by yellow mealworms and superworms, highlighting the potential of these insects as biological agents for reducing plastic waste. Additionally, Ding has been involved in research assessing how the physical and chemical properties of polyethylene influence its breakdown when ingested by insects. Another area of contribution includes investigations into the gut microbiome of Tenebrio larvae, which provide insights into the microbial processes that support polyethylene degradation.  

Overall, Ding, M.Q. is recognized for advancing knowledge on insect-based plastic biodegradation, with a focus on the interactions between mealworms, superworms, and their gut microbiota in the degradation of polyethylene and polypropylene. This body of work contributes to the broader field of sustainable waste management and the search for biological solutions to plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of multiple studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of studies on biodegradation of polypropylene and polyethylene by mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of multiple studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Ding, M.Q. is a co-author of studies on biodegradation of polypropylene by mealworms and superworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
