<node id="Zhang, C.H.">
  <data key="d0">Zhang, C.H.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zhang, C.H. is a researcher and author recognized for contributions to studies on the biodegradation of polypropylene, a widely used plastic, through the activity of insects such as mealworms and superworms. Specifically, Zhang, C.H. is listed as a co-author of a 2021 study that investigated the capacity of yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) and superworms (*Zophobas atratus*) to degrade polypropylene. This research explored the potential of these insect species to contribute to sustainable waste management and plastic biodegradation solutions. Through this work, Zhang, C.H. has contributed to advancing scientific understanding of biological pathways for mitigating plastic pollution and the role of insect-based systems in addressing environmental challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;Zhang, C.H. is a co-author of studies on biodegradation of polypropylene by mealworms and superworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
