<node id="Li, Q.X.">
  <data key="d0">Li, Q.X.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Li, Q.X. is a researcher and author recognized for contributions to studies on the biodegradation of polypropylene, a widely used plastic, by insect larvae. Specifically, Li, Q.X. served as a co-author of research investigating the ability of yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) and superworms (*Zophobas atratus*) to degrade polypropylene. This work, published in 2021, examined the potential of these organisms to consume and break down plastic waste, offering insights into biological pathways for mitigating plastic pollution. Through co-authorship of this study, Li, Q.X. contributed to advancing scientific understanding of insect-mediated plastic biodegradation and its implications for sustainable waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Li, Q.X. is a co-author of studies on biodegradation of polypropylene by mealworms and superworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
