<node id="Cao, G.L.">
  <data key="d0">Cao, G.L.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cao, G.L. is a researcher and author recognized for contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly focusing on the role of insects such as mealworms and superworms. Their work has examined the capacity of these organisms to degrade synthetic polymers, including polypropylene and polyethylene, two of the most widely used and environmentally persistent plastics. Cao, G.L. has co-authored and authored multiple studies that investigate the mechanisms and effectiveness of biodegradation processes facilitated by these insects, with an emphasis on understanding how yellow mealworms and superworms can break down and metabolize plastic materials. Through this research, Cao, G.L. has contributed to advancing knowledge in the field of plastic waste management and environmental sustainability, highlighting the potential of biological systems as innovative solutions for mitigating plastic pollution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
