<node id="Ding, J.">
  <data key="d0">Ding, J.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ding, J. is a researcher whose work is primarily focused on environmental science, with particular expertise in the biodegradation of plastics and other waste materials through biological processes. A central theme of Ding, J.’s research is the investigation of insect-mediated plastic degradation, especially using larvae of mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) and superworms (*Zophobas atratus*). These studies have demonstrated that such larvae are capable of ingesting and partially degrading persistent synthetic polymers, including polystyrene, polypropylene, polyethylene, and polyethylene terephthalate. By highlighting the potential of insect-based systems to reduce plastic waste, this body of work contributes to the development of sustainable waste management strategies and pollution mitigation approaches.  

In addition to documenting the direct degradation of plastics, Ding, J. has co-authored research examining the gut microbiome of *Tenebrio molitor* larvae, with a focus on its role in carbon and nitrogen metabolism during polyethylene biodegradation. This line of inquiry provides valuable insights into the microbial mechanisms that facilitate plastic breakdown, thereby advancing understanding of the ecological and biological processes underlying insect-based biodegradation. Ding, J. has also contributed to studies on the biodegradation of low-density polyethylene and explored the use of insect larvae for the reduction of lignocellulosic crop residues, extending the applicability of insect-based bioconversion to agricultural waste management and resource recovery.  

Beyond insect-related biodegradation, Ding, J. has participated in broader environmental research, including studies on wastewater treatment and the role of chloride ions in wastewater systems. This reflects a wider engagement with pollution control and environmental remediation beyond plastics. Furthermore, Ding, J. co-authored a 2023 bibliometric analysis of publications on plastic biodegradation, providing a systematic evaluation of research trends and developments in this rapidly growing field.  

Ding, J.’s contributions also encompass toxicological research, including co-authorship of a 2021 study on the effects of polystyrene microplastics in inducing male reproductive toxicity in mice, thereby linking plastic pollution not only to environmental but also to health-related concerns.  

Overall, Ding, J.’s research portfolio demonstrates a strong and multifaceted commitment to biodegradation, waste reduction, and environmental sustainability. By integrating studies on insect-mediated plastic degradation, microbial ecology, agricultural waste conversion, wastewater treatment, and the health impacts of microplastics, Ding, J. has significantly advanced the scientific understanding of biological solutions to global challenges in waste management, pollution control, and ecological resilience.&lt;SEP&gt;Ding, J. is a co-author of studies on biodegradation of polypropylene by mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Ding, J. is a co-author of a study on confirmation of polystyrene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Description not available in text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f3828bbe45c2c38004a29d55dcbf40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90</data>
