<node id="Shaoze Xiao">
  <data key="d0">Shaoze Xiao</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Shaoze Xiao is a researcher affiliated with the State Key Laboratory of Pollution Control and Resource Reuse at the College of Environmental Science and Engineering, Tongji University in Shanghai, China. Xiao is recognized as one of the authors of several studies investigating the biodegradation of plastics, particularly polyethylene and polystyrene microplastics, by mealworm larvae. These studies contribute to the growing body of research on biological approaches to mitigating plastic pollution.  

Within these research projects, Shaoze Xiao played a significant role in the conceptualization and design of the studies, as well as in the development of methodologies used to assess plastic degradation. In addition, Xiao contributed to formal analysis and validation, ensuring the reliability and accuracy of the experimental results. Through these contributions, Xiao has helped advance scientific understanding of how insect larvae can be utilized as a potential solution for reducing the environmental impact of persistent plastic waste.  

Overall, Shaoze Xiao’s work reflects a focus on environmental science and engineering, with particular emphasis on innovative strategies for pollution control and resource reuse. By combining expertise in experimental design, methodological development, and data validation, Xiao has contributed to research that explores sustainable pathways for addressing the global challenge of plastic pollution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb491e686c96e54f8ea43a9f1ba97eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0881f766e34a5d97ee711cd2edd793f</data>
