<node id="Jiabin Chen">
  <data key="d0">Jiabin Chen</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Jiabin Chen is a researcher affiliated with the State Key Laboratory of Pollution Control and Resource Reuse, College of Environmental Science and Engineering at Tongji University in Shanghai, China. He is recognized as one of the authors of multiple studies investigating the biodegradation of plastics, particularly polyethylene microplastics, by mealworm larvae (Tenebrio molitor). His work contributes to advancing understanding of how biological systems, such as insects, can play a role in addressing the global challenge of plastic pollution.  

In these studies, Jiabin Chen is identified as an author with the ORCID iD 0000-0002-4790-5873. His specific contributions to the research include validation of experimental results and securing funding to support the investigations. The research in which he participated explores the potential of mealworms to degrade microplastics, providing insights into sustainable waste management and resource reuse strategies.  

Through his authorship and institutional affiliation, Jiabin Chen is positioned as an active contributor to environmental science research, particularly in the field of plastic biodegradation and pollution control. His role highlights both scientific and practical aspects of the research process, combining technical validation with the acquisition of resources necessary to advance this line of inquiry.&lt;SEP&gt;Jiabin Chen is one of the authors of the study on polystyrene biodegradation in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Author affiliated with the State Key Laboratory of Pollution Control and Resource Reuse, Tongji University.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb491e686c96e54f8ea43a9f1ba97eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0881f766e34a5d97ee711cd2edd793f</data>
