<node id="Xuefei Zhou">
  <data key="d0">Xuefei Zhou</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Xuefei Zhou is a researcher affiliated with the State Key Laboratory of Pollution Control and Resource Reuse, within the College of Environmental Science and Engineering at Tongji University in Shanghai, China. Zhou has made significant contributions to the field of environmental science, particularly in the study of plastic biodegradation. As an author and corresponding author on multiple research papers, Zhou has focused on the biodegradation of various types of microplastics, including polyethylene and polystyrene, by mealworm larvae (Tenebrio molitor). These studies explore the potential of biological systems, specifically insect larvae, to degrade persistent plastic pollutants, offering insights into sustainable waste management and pollution control strategies.  

In the course of this research, Zhou has contributed to several key aspects of the scientific process, including methodology development, validation of experimental results, acquisition of funding to support the studies, and the critical tasks of reviewing and editing manuscripts. Through this work, Zhou has played a central role in advancing understanding of how mealworms can metabolize and break down synthetic polymers, thereby addressing one of the pressing environmental challenges of plastic pollution.  

Overall, Xuefei Zhou is recognized as an active scholar in environmental science and engineering, with a research focus on innovative approaches to pollution control and resource reuse, particularly through the biological degradation of microplastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0881f766e34a5d97ee711cd2edd793f</data>
