<node id="Oxidative stress">
  <data key="d0">Oxidative stress</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxidative stress refers to the physiological condition observed in mealworm larvae when fed polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is induced in mealworm larvae during PE ingestion and biodegradation, leading to tissue damage and reduced physiological performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is a physiological condition suggested for assessment to determine toxic effects of oxo-degradable polyethylene on insects.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is a physiological response observed in macroinvertebrates exposed to micro(nano)plastics, involving reactive oxygen species and metabolic dysbiosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is a biochemical condition investigated after larvae were fed PE-MPs for 21 days.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress conditions were linked to nitrogen retention and metabolic changes in mealworms during PS biodegradation.</data>
