<node id="Yang, S.-S.">
  <data key="d0">Yang, S.-S.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Yang, S.-S. is a researcher and author whose work is centered on the biodegradation of plastics, with a particular emphasis on insect-mediated, microbial, and enzymatic processes. Since at least 2018, Yang has co-authored multiple studies that provide experimental evidence for the ability of insect larvae—such as yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*), superworms (*Zophobas atratus*), and wax moth larvae (*Galleria mellonella*)—to consume and degrade synthetic polymers including polystyrene, polyethylene, polypropylene, and mixed plastic waste. These studies have demonstrated that larvae not only ingest and fragment plastics but also metabolize them, thereby highlighting their potential as a biological solution to the growing problem of plastic pollution.  

Yang’s research has been instrumental in establishing insect larvae as a viable biological model for plastic degradation. Specific contributions include studies on the biodegradation of polystyrene and low-density polyethylene in mealworms, the breakdown of polypropylene in both mealworms and superworms, and the digestion of polystyrene by yellow mealworms. In addition, Yang has co-authored investigations into the gut microbiome of larvae, examining its role in carbon and nitrogen metabolism during polyethylene degradation. This work has clarified the link between microbial activity within insect digestive systems and the overall biodegradation process, thereby advancing understanding of the mechanisms underlying insect-mediated plastic breakdown.  

Beyond insect-based approaches, Yang has also contributed to broader research on biological strategies for plastic degradation. This includes collaborative work on enzymatic and microbial pathways capable of breaking down plastics, as well as participation in a 2023 bibliometric analysis of global research on plastic biodegradation. The bibliometric study provided insights into publication trends, knowledge gaps, and future directions in the field, situating Yang’s work within the wider scientific landscape of sustainable waste management.  

In addition to plastics research, Yang has engaged in environmental studies related to wastewater treatment, including investigations into the role of chloride ions in wastewater systems. This reflects a broader commitment to pollution control and environmental sustainability beyond plastics alone.  

Overall, Yang, S.-S. is recognized for significant contributions to the scientific understanding of plastic biodegradation. By integrating research on insect physiology, gut microbiomes, enzymatic processes, and microbial pathways, Yang has helped build a comprehensive foundation for the development of biologically based solutions to plastic pollution, while also contributing to related areas of environmental chemistry and wastewater management.&lt;SEP&gt;Yang, S.-S. is a co-author of the 2018 study on biodegradation of polyethylene and plastic mixtures in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Yang, S.-S. is an author of a 2021 study on Tenebrio molitor gut microbiome response to diet shifts during plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Yang, S.-S. is an author of multiple studies on polystyrene digestion and biodegradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of a study on enhancing bioenergy production with carbon capture of microalgae.&lt;SEP&gt;Yang, S.-S. is one of the authors of a 2018 study (details truncated in text).&lt;SEP&gt;Description not available in text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f3828bbe45c2c38004a29d55dcbf40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-352650a946ab941cec3f7b9813faeee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20bc31ca22e33a7b244779745e9eeb73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713</data>
