<node id="Yellow Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor)">
  <data key="d0">Yellow Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Yellow mealworms are the larvae of Tenebrio molitor, belonging to the Coleoptera: Tenebrionidae family. They are widely studied as a model organism for plastic biodegradation due to their rapid growth, commercial availability, and ability to degrade plastics such as LDPE and PE. They are also commercially reared for sustainable food proteins and animal fats for livestock and human consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms are insects studied for their ability to biodegrade plastics such as polypropylene and polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Larvae of Tenebrio molitor, shown to biodegrade polypropylene and polystyrene via gut-microbe interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) are insects studied for their ability to biodegrade polypropylene and polyethylene through gut-microbe-dependent and independent depolymerization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ac276660dd76d0ef97a8a0b1a59664c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59</data>
