<node id="Agilent Technologies Inc.">
  <data key="d0">Agilent Technologies Inc.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Agilent Technologies Inc. is a U.S.-based company that provided the HT-GPC instrument (1260 Infinity II HT GPC) used in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Agilent Technologies Inc. is mentioned as the manufacturer of the Agilent 1260 system used for gel permeation chromatography (GPC) analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Agilent Technologies Inc., U.S.A., is the manufacturer of the Agilent 1260 GPC system used for analyzing polymer molecular weight changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Agilent Technologies Inc., a U.S.-based company, provided the GPC and HT-GPC instruments used to analyze molecular weight changes in polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Agilent Technologies Inc., based in the U.S.A., provided the Py-GCMS equipment (7890B-S977B GC/MS) and standard substances for PS and PE polymers used in the experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Agilent Technologies Inc., based in the U.S.A. and California, provided analytical instruments such as the 1260 Infinity II GPC/SEC, 1260 Infinity II HT GPC, and Agilent 8700 LDIR used in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3</data>
