<node id="HT-GPC Analysis">
  <data key="d0">HT-GPC Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">High-temperature gel permeation chromatography (HT-GPC) analysis was conducted to verify depolymerization and biodegradation of ingested PE microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;HT-GPC analysis was used to measure molecular weight reductions in residual polymers from mealworms fed PE and PS, indicating depolymerization.&lt;SEP&gt;HT-GPC (High-Temperature Gel Permeation Chromatography) analysis was used to study the molecular weight distribution of residual polymers after biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;HT-GPC analysis refers to the method used to analyze frass samples from gentamicin suppression groups to assess depolymerization ability of larvae.</data>
