<node id="UK">
  <data key="d0">UK</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">The United Kingdom (UK) is a country in Europe that serves as the location for several notable institutions and research activities. It is the home of Malvern Panalytical, a scientific instrumentation company specializing in materials analysis, and also the base of Cambridge University Press, the academic publisher of Roberson’s book. The UK is further recognized as the location of Queen’s University Belfast, a leading research-intensive university.  

In addition to its institutional significance, the UK has played a role in scientific studies on environmental sustainability. It was one of the countries where research on mealworm (Tenebrio molitor) polystyrene (PS) degradation was conducted, specifically examining the ability of larvae to consume and break down PS foam. The UK was also one of the sites where T. molitor larvae were collected for comparative analysis of PS consumption rates, contributing to broader international studies on biodegradation and plastic waste management.  

Overall, the UK is notable in this context both as a hub for prominent academic and scientific organizations and as a site of experimental research into biological solutions for plastic degradation.</data>
