<node id="PLA (Polylactic Acid)">
  <data key="d0">PLA (Polylactic Acid)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PLA (Polylactic Acid) is a bio-based degradable plastic used in previous studies as feedstock for mealworm larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;category&lt;SEP&gt;PLA is a polymer extracted using DCM for residual content analysis in frass.&lt;SEP&gt;PLA is a hydrolyzable bioplastic that can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;PLA is a biodegradable polyester tested as a food source for mealworms. It showed the lowest mass loss among tested plastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261</data>
