  <data key="d2">Lipid peroxidation occurs in mealworm larvae as a result of oxidative stress during PE ingestion and biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipid peroxidation is a biochemical indicator measured to evaluate oxidative stress in Tenebrio molitor larvae during plastic biodegradation.</data>
