  <data key="d2">Water content is one of the biomass components reduced in mealworm larvae after continuous PE feeding.&lt;SEP&gt;Water content was measured in mealworms supplemented with PET agar gel and agar gel alone, showing values of 58.3 ± 0.98% and 62.1 ± 1.04%, respectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Water content was measured in larvae and was lower in PS-fed and PVC-fed groups compared to PLA-fed and bran-fed groups.</data>
