<node id="Yalei Zhang">
  <data key="d0">Yalei Zhang</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Yalei Zhang is a researcher affiliated with the State Key Laboratory of Pollution Control and Resource Reuse, College of Environmental Science and Engineering at Tongji University in Shanghai, China. Identified with ORCID 0000-0002-3254-8965, Zhang has served as a corresponding author on multiple scientific studies, particularly in the field of plastic biodegradation. Their research contributions include investigations into the biodegradation of polyethylene terephthalate (PET) as well as studies on the degradation of polystyrene and microplastics by mealworms, reflecting a strong focus on environmental science and sustainable waste management.  

In these works, Yalei Zhang has played a central role in both scientific and administrative aspects of research. Their contributions span conceptualization, methodology development, validation of results, project administration, and the critical process of writing, reviewing, and editing manuscripts. Additionally, Zhang has been responsible for securing funding to support these research initiatives, underscoring their leadership in advancing studies on plastic pollution and biodegradation.  

Through their position as a corresponding author, Yalei Zhang has acted as a primary point of contact for collaborative research efforts and scholarly communication, further highlighting their role in coordinating and disseminating scientific knowledge. Their work at Tongji University and within the State Key Laboratory emphasizes the integration of innovative scientific inquiry with practical applications aimed at addressing pressing environmental challenges related to plastic waste.  

Overall, Yalei Zhang is recognized as a key contributor and leader in the study of plastic biodegradation, with a research portfolio that combines fundamental scientific exploration with applied environmental solutions.</data>
