<node id="Bombelli, P.">
  <data key="d0">Bombelli, P.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Bombelli, P. is a researcher recognized for his contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly through investigations involving the caterpillars of the wax moth *Galleria mellonella*. He is best known as a co-author of a widely cited 2017 study that demonstrated the ability of these caterpillars to degrade polyethylene, one of the most persistent and extensively used synthetic plastics. This work provided important evidence that biological systems, either through enzymatic activity or microbial symbiosis, could play a role in breaking down otherwise resistant polymers, offering potential pathways for innovative waste management and environmental remediation strategies.  

In addition to the 2017 publication, Bombelli, P. co-authored a 2019 study that expanded on this research by examining polyethylene biodegradation within the framework of holobiont metabolism. This study explored the interactions between the caterpillars and their associated microbial communities, emphasizing the ecological and metabolic complexity underlying the biodegradation process. His work has also been referenced in relation to research on the biodegradation of other plastics, including polystyrene, further underscoring his involvement in advancing knowledge of biological mechanisms for addressing plastic pollution.  

Through these contributions, Bombelli, P. has established himself as an important figure in the emerging field of plastic biodegradation research. His studies highlight the potential of leveraging biological and ecological processes to mitigate the environmental challenges posed by synthetic polymers, positioning his work at the intersection of microbiology, ecology, and sustainability science.&lt;SEP&gt;Description not available in text.&lt;SEP&gt;Bombelli, P. is an author of a referenced study on polyethylene biodegradation by caterpillars of the wax moth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df24ea37743c236d369911024fc20bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33180d5b7e1ebfedf8de59ba1a2a2d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16328c3c685f35501c3639525e997d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602bba09eb2c308c400b412f39f4adb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5338aa2127367c868a3e7331e1f66225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262</data>
