<node id="Hexabromocyclododecane (HBCD)">
  <data key="d0">Hexabromocyclododecane (HBCD)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">HBCD is a common flame retardant studied in the context of polystyrene-degrading mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;HBCD is a flame retardant consumed by mealworms and excreted via frass within 24 hours.&lt;SEP&gt;A flame retardant studied for its fate in polystyrene-degrading mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;HBCD is a common flame retardant studied in relation to polystyrene-degrading mealworms, where elevated levels were found in egested polymer but no bioaccumulation occurred.</data>
