<node id="Antarctic krill">
  <data key="d0">Antarctic krill</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Antarctic krill are capable of fragmenting microplastics into nanoplastics through digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Antarctic krill are macroinvertebrates without plastic-degrading abilities, studied for physiological stress responses to micro(nano)plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Antarctic krill are macroinvertebrates with poor or no plastic-degrading ability, referenced for comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;Antarctic krill is a macroinvertebrate mentioned as lacking plastic-degrading ability but still studied for digestive fragmentation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Antarctic krill are macroinvertebrates with poor plastic-degrading ability, leading to biofragmentation of ingested plastics into nanoparticles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1</data>
