  <data key="d2">Earthworms are studied for the effects of microplastic digestion and toxicity.&lt;SEP&gt;Eisenia fetida are macroinvertebrates with poor plastic-degrading ability, used in the experiment to observe ROS increase when exposed to PS MPs.&lt;SEP&gt;Earthworms (Eisenia fetida) were studied for defense responses when exposed to polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Earthworms (Eisenia fetida) are organisms that disintegrate bio-based PLA microplastics into sub-micron microplastics in their digestive tracts.</data>
