<node id="Lou, Y.">
  <data key="d0">Lou, Y.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lou, Y. is a researcher and author whose work centers on the biodegradation of synthetic plastics by insect larvae and the role of gut microbiomes in enabling this process. Their research has been particularly focused on the capacity of organisms such as the greater wax moth (*Galleria mellonella*) and the yellow mealworm (*Tenebrio molitor*) to degrade persistent plastics, including polyethylene and polystyrene, which are otherwise highly resistant to natural breakdown.  

In a series of studies published in 2020 and 2021, Lou, Y. co-authored influential research demonstrating that *Galleria mellonella* larvae are capable of degrading both polyethylene and polystyrene. These findings provided important evidence that insect larvae, together with their gut-associated microbial communities, play a significant role in the decomposition of recalcitrant polymers. This work has been widely recognized for highlighting the potential of biological systems as a novel approach to mitigating plastic pollution.  

Beyond the wax moth, Lou, Y. has also investigated the gut microbiome of *Tenebrio molitor* larvae, with a particular emphasis on how microbial communities respond to dietary shifts when the larvae are fed plastics. Their co-authored studies revealed that changes in gut microbiota composition are closely linked to the larvae’s ability to metabolize synthetic polymers, offering insights into the microbial mechanisms that support plastic degradation.  

Through this body of research, Lou, Y. has advanced knowledge in the emerging field of insect-mediated plastic biodegradation. Their contributions underscore both the biological capacity of insect larvae to degrade plastics and the ecological and microbiological processes that facilitate this phenomenon. By integrating entomology, microbiology, and environmental science, Lou, Y.’s work provides a foundation for exploring sustainable, biologically based strategies to address the global challenge of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Description not available in text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb2c1ef38dbbafa838f87d5f4d6fd6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c0c246e98a503a16ace92f28394b584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48</data>
