<node id="Ekaterina, P.">
  <data key="d0">Ekaterina, P.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ekaterina, P. is a researcher and co-author recognized for her contributions to studies on the biodegradation of synthetic plastics by insect larvae. Her work has primarily focused on the capacity of *Galleria mellonella* larvae, commonly known as wax moth larvae, to degrade persistent polymers such as polyethylene and polystyrene. These studies, including a notable publication in 2020, have explored the biological mechanisms by which these larvae can break down plastics, offering insights into potential biotechnological applications for addressing plastic waste. Through her authorship and co-authorship of multiple research papers, Ekaterina, P. has contributed to advancing scientific understanding of insect-mediated biodegradation processes and their implications for sustainable waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of the 2020 study on biodegradation of polyethylene and polystyrene by greater wax moth larva.&lt;SEP&gt;Ekaterina, P. is a co-author of a study on biodegradation of polyethylene and polystyrene by greater wax moth larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Ekaterina, P. is a co-author of a 2020 study on biodegradation of polystyrene by greater wax moth larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Description not available in text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb2c1ef38dbbafa838f87d5f4d6fd6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713</data>
