<node id="Lu, B.">
  <data key="d0">Lu, B.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lu, B. is a researcher and co-author whose work primarily focuses on the biodegradation of synthetic plastics by insect larvae and the associated microbial processes. Their contributions span multiple studies investigating the ability of insects such as yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) and wax moth larvae (*Galleria mellonella*) to degrade common plastics, including polyethylene and polystyrene.  

In this body of research, Lu, B. has co-authored studies examining how insect larvae can ingest and break down plastics, highlighting the potential of biological systems as alternatives to conventional plastic waste management methods. A significant aspect of this work involves the role of the gut microbiome in facilitating plastic degradation. For example, Lu, B. has contributed to studies analyzing the gut microbial community of yellow mealworms during polystyrene biodegradation, with particular attention to how dietary shifts influence microbial composition and metabolic activity.  

Additionally, Lu, B. has co-authored research on the biodegradation of polyethylene and polystyrene by wax moth larvae, specifically *Galleria mellonella*. These studies demonstrate that the larvae, along with their gut microbiota, can contribute to the breakdown of otherwise persistent plastic polymers. The findings suggest that insect–microbe interactions may play a crucial role in initiating and sustaining the degradation process.  

Overall, Lu, B.’s research contributions provide valuable insights into the biological and microbial mechanisms underlying plastic biodegradation. By focusing on insect larvae such as yellow mealworms and wax moths, as well as their gut microbiomes, Lu, B. has helped advance understanding of potential biotechnological approaches to mitigating plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Lu, B. is an author of a 2021 study on Tenebrio molitor gut microbiome response to diet shifts during plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of a study on gut microbiome response to diet shifts during plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Lu, B. is a co-author of a study on biodegradation of polyethylene and polystyrene by greater wax moth larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Lu, B. is a co-author of a 2021 study on the response of yellow mealworm gut microbiome to diet shifts during polystyrene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Description not available in text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48</data>
