<node id="Su, Y.">
  <data key="d0">Su, Y.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Su, Y. is a researcher recognized for contributions to studies on the biodegradation of polystyrene, particularly through the activity of mealworms. Su, Y. is listed as an author and co-author of research examining the capacity of both dark mealworms (*Tenebrio obscura*) and yellow mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) to degrade polystyrene, a widely used plastic known for its environmental persistence. This body of work, including a study published in 2019, highlights the potential role of these insect species in plastic waste management and environmental remediation. Through these investigations, Su, Y. has contributed to advancing scientific understanding of biological approaches to mitigating plastic pollution, with a focus on the mechanisms and effectiveness of polystyrene degradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of a study on biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Su, Y. is listed as an author of a study on biodegradation of polystyrene by dark and yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Su, Y. is an author of a study on biodegradation of polystyrene by dark and yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of a study on biodegradation of polystyrene by dark and yellow mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48</data>
