<node id="Cao, G.-L.">
  <data key="d0">Cao, G.-L.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cao, G.-L. is a researcher and co-author whose work primarily focuses on the biodegradation of synthetic polymers and organic waste by insect larvae. Their contributions span multiple studies investigating the capacity of insects, particularly mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) and superworms (*Zophobas atratus*), to degrade persistent plastic materials such as polyethylene, polypropylene, polystyrene, and low-density polyethylene. Cao, G.-L. has co-authored research that confirmed the biodegradation of polystyrene and low-density polyethylene in mealworms, providing experimental evidence that these larvae can ingest and metabolize plastics that are otherwise resistant to natural decomposition.  

In addition to plastics, Cao, G.-L. has contributed to studies on the reduction of lignocellulosic crop waste using *Tenebrio molitor*, highlighting the broader potential of insect larvae in bioconversion and waste management. Their work includes a 2021 study that specifically examined the biodegradation of polypropylene by both mealworms and superworms, further expanding the understanding of insect-mediated plastic degradation across different species.  

Overall, Cao, G.-L.’s research emphasizes the role of insect larvae as biological agents capable of breaking down recalcitrant polymers and agricultural residues, offering insights into sustainable waste reduction strategies and potential applications in environmental remediation.&lt;SEP&gt;Description not available in text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90</data>
