<node id="Pang, J.-W.">
  <data key="d0">Pang, J.-W.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Pang, J.-W. is a researcher and co-author whose work primarily focuses on the biodegradation of plastics, particularly through the activity of insect larvae such as *Tenebrio molitor* (commonly known as mealworms). Pang has contributed to multiple studies confirming the ability of mealworms to degrade various types of plastics, including low-density polyethylene (LDPE), polystyrene, and polyethylene terephthalate (PET). These studies have provided experimental evidence supporting the role of insect larvae in breaking down synthetic polymers, thereby offering potential biological solutions to plastic waste management.  

In addition to experimental research, Pang, J.-W. has co-authored a bibliometric analysis published in 2023 that examined global trends and developments in the field of plastic biodegradation. This work highlights the growing scientific interest in sustainable approaches to mitigating plastic pollution and situates Pang’s contributions within a broader research landscape.  

Beyond plastics research, Pang has also co-authored studies addressing environmental challenges in wastewater treatment, including investigations into the role and behavior of chloride ions. This indicates a broader interest in environmental science and pollution control.  

Overall, Pang, J.-W. is recognized for significant contributions to advancing knowledge on plastic biodegradation by insect larvae, with research spanning experimental validation of degradation processes, analysis of specific polymer types, and bibliometric assessments of the field, alongside related work in wastewater studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Description not available in text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f3828bbe45c2c38004a29d55dcbf40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90</data>
