  <data key="d0">Dark Mealworms (Tenebrio obscurus)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Dark mealworms are insects studied for their ability to biodegrade polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Dark mealworms, larvae of Tenebrio obscurus, are studied for their ability to biodegrade polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Dark mealworms (Tenebrio obscurus) are insects studied for their ability to biodegrade low-density polyethylene through gut microbe-independent depolymerization.</data>
