<node id="Zebrafish">
  <data key="d0">Zebrafish</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Zebrafish are aquatic organisms studied for developmental toxicity effects of microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Zebrafish are non-plastic-degrading organisms reported to show lipid homeostasis disruption when exposed to plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Zebrafish are referenced as organisms that can suffer biological toxicity and inflammatory responses from long-term exposure to microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Zebrafish are studied for the adverse effects of polyethylene microplastics on their heart at molecular and individual levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Zebrafish are mentioned as another species where metabolic pathways involved in oxidative stress defense have been studied.</data>
