<node id="Environmental Pollution">
  <data key="d0">Environmental Pollution</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">**Environmental Pollution** refers both to a significant real-world environmental issue and to a leading scientific journal dedicated to its study.  

As a global problem, environmental pollution denotes the contamination of natural ecosystems by harmful substances, particularly plastics, chemicals, and other persistent wastes. It encompasses the degradation of air, water, and soil quality, often resulting from excessive use and disposal of materials such as polystyrene and polyethylene. These pollutants accumulate in landfills, waterways, and oceans, where they generate toxic byproducts, release microplastics, and disrupt ecological balance. The consequences include harm to wildlife, marine organisms, and human health, as well as long-term damage to ecosystems. Examples include microplastic pollution in aquatic environments, the release of hazardous compounds from expanded polystyrene (EPS), and the broader ecological risks associated with plastic persistence. In response, sustainable alternatives such as papercrete bricks and other innovative building materials have been explored as strategies to reduce environmental pollution and mitigate its impacts.  

In the academic context, *Environmental Pollution* is a peer-reviewed scientific journal that provides a platform for research on the sources, effects, and mitigation of environmental contaminants. The journal has published influential studies that have advanced understanding of pollution, particularly in relation to plastics and microplastics. Notable contributions include a 2013 review on microplastics, a 2014 analysis of microplastic pollution, and investigations into the ecological consequences of textile fibers and synthetic particles in natural environments. More recent studies published in the journal include research on microbiome diversity in *Tenebrio molitor* when fed with polystyrene waste, examinations of gut microbiome changes in insects exposed to plastics, and work on the biodegradation potential of *Zophobas atratus* (2020). Additionally, the journal has featured studies on coral responses to microplastic exposure, highlighting the far-reaching ecological effects of pollution.  

Together, the dual meanings of *Environmental Pollution* underscore both the urgency of addressing environmental contamination in practice and the critical role of scientific research in informing solutions. The journal serves as a central venue for disseminating knowledge on pollution’s causes and consequences, while the broader concept of environmental pollution represents one of the most pressing global challenges of the modern era.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental pollution is a concern caused by synthetic debris such as plastics and microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Pollution is the name of the scientific journal in which this article was published.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a603837ad5b989bafd614f5eeb8504c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678bd592bfdda3f6dd8f2a6659de7fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f830cfd93570c7a9762518aa356ab69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d9491734042920c5911740665415835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387937</data>
</node>
<node id="ScienceDirect">
  <data key="d0">ScienceDirect</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">ScienceDirect is the online platform where the journal Environmental Pollution is hosted.&lt;SEP&gt;ScienceDirect is an online platform where the Journal of Environmental Chemical Engineering is hosted.&lt;SEP&gt;ScienceDirect is the platform where the journal Chemosphere and its contents are available.&lt;SEP&gt;ScienceDirect is the platform where the Journal of Hazardous Materials content is available.&lt;SEP&gt;ScienceDirect is the platform where the Journal of Environmental Management contents are available.&lt;SEP&gt;ScienceDirect is the platform where the Journal of Environmental Chemical Engineering contents are available.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a603837ad5b989bafd614f5eeb8504c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90</data>
