<node id="Pantoea">
  <data key="d0">Pantoea</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Pantoea is a bacterial genus belonging to the family Erwiniaceae and is recognized for its presence in the digestive systems of insects, particularly the mealworm *Tenebrio molitor*. It has been consistently identified in both larvae and adult stages of *T. molitor*, including in groups fed on specialized diets such as polyethylene and bran. Within these contexts, Pantoea has been noted as a characteristic and enriched genus, suggesting its adaptability to diverse nutritional environments. Importantly, strains of Pantoea, including *Pantoea agglomerans*, have been isolated from adult gut samples, with some evidence indicating their potential role in the degradation of plastics such as low-density polyethylene. This association highlights the genus as a candidate of interest in studies of insect-microbe interactions and biodegradation processes. Taxonomically, Pantoea is one of 14 genera within Erwiniaceae, and its classification has undergone refinement, with four species formerly placed in Pantoea reclassified to establish the separate genus *Mixta*. Overall, Pantoea represents a versatile bacterial genus with ecological significance in insect gut microbiota and potential biotechnological applications in plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Pantoea is a bacterial genus characteristic of polyethylene diets in Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Pantoea is a bacterial genus identified in larvae fed polyethylene diets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a603837ad5b989bafd614f5eeb8504c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
