  <data key="d2">Esterases are enzymes with high activity in Tenebrio molitor larvae digestive systems and are involved in polyethylene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Esterases are enzymes identified as predominant during the biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Esterases are enzymes acting during the biodegradation of plastics, identified in the gut microbiome of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Esterases are enzymes measured in the gut of mealworms that can break down specific bonds in polyurethane molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Esterases are enzymes measured in the mealworm gut, associated with PU hydrolysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Esterases are extracellular enzymes tested for activity against NPS-grown bacteria using Tween 20 as substrate.&lt;SEP&gt;Esterases are enzymes produced by Achromobacter species, involved in the hydrolysis of ester bonds and degradation of pollutants.</data>
