<node id="Thermo Fisher Scientific">
  <data key="d0">Thermo Fisher Scientific</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermo Fisher Scientific is a leading scientific instrumentation and biotechnology company headquartered in Waltham, Massachusetts, USA. The company is widely recognized for providing advanced laboratory equipment, analytical instruments, and reagents that support research across diverse scientific disciplines. In various studies, Thermo Fisher Scientific has been identified as the supplier of key technologies and systems essential for molecular biology, genomics, metabolomics, and materials characterization.  

Among its contributions, Thermo Fisher Scientific provided the **Maxima Probe Real-time PCR Master Mix**, a reagent critical for quantitative PCR applications, and the **Nanodrop spectrophotometer**, an instrument used for assessing RNA quality and quantity. In metabolomics research, the company supplied the **UPLC-Q Exactive system**, which enables high-resolution metabolomic profiling, as well as the **Vanquish Flex UHPLC system**, designed for advanced chromatographic separation.  

For spectroscopy and materials analysis, Thermo Fisher Scientific manufactured the **Nicolet iS50 FTIR Spectrometer**, which has been used in both Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy and polymer characterization. In the field of sequencing, the company provided the **Ion SS XL System**, a platform supporting next-generation sequencing applications.  

Thermo Fisher Scientific is also associated with **Invitrogen**, one of its well-known brands, which further expands its portfolio of molecular biology reagents and tools. Collectively, the company’s technologies play a central role in enabling high-precision scientific research, from molecular diagnostics and genomics to metabolomics and materials science.  

In summary, Thermo Fisher Scientific, based in Waltham, MA, USA, is a global provider of scientific instruments, reagents, and systems, including PCR reagents, spectrophotometers, chromatography platforms, sequencing systems, and spectrometers, supporting a wide range of research and analytical applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermo Fisher Scientific, U.S.A., is the manufacturer of the Nicolet iS5 FTIR Spectrometer used for characterizing functional groups of PS and frass.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermo Fisher Scientific is a U.S.-based company whose Nicolet iS50 FTIR spectrometer was used to obtain FTIR spectra of PP foam and frass samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermo Fisher Scientific, based in Sunnyvale, CA, USA, produced the Thermo-Nicolet 6700 Series FTIR spectrometer used in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermo Fisher Scientific is a U.S.-based company providing the Nicolet iS50 FTIR Spectrometer used for Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermo Fisher Scientific is the company based in the U.S.A. that manufactures the Nicolet iS50 FTIR Spectrometer.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermo Fisher Scientific is a company based in Waltham, USA, that provided the Maxima Probe Real-time PCR Master Mix used in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4c5fc4d4324334254706d6d5f9312276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6ccf223c8c62d59ba994731f546ad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e69c793c3b67aed7a68bf864c2c7a309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee</data>
