<node id="Illumina MiSeq">
  <data key="d0">Illumina MiSeq</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Illumina MiSeq is a next-generation sequencing platform developed by Illumina that is widely used for high-throughput DNA sequencing, particularly in microbial ecology and microbiome research. It is frequently operated in paired-end sequencing mode, such as 2×250 base pair reads, which allows for improved accuracy, greater sequence coverage, and more reliable assembly of DNA fragments. This capability makes the platform especially well-suited for amplicon sequencing, where targeted regions of DNA, such as the 16S rRNA gene, are amplified and sequenced to characterize microbial community composition.  

In research applications, the Illumina MiSeq is commonly employed to study bacterial and fungal communities across diverse environments. It is a standard tool for profiling bacterial taxa through 16S rRNA gene sequencing and is also applied to fungal community analysis using other marker genes. The platform supports detailed taxonomic and functional profiling, enabling researchers to assess microbial diversity, structure, and dynamics with high resolution.  

The Illumina MiSeq has been extensively used in experimental studies of host-associated microbiomes, including investigations of gut bacterial and fungal communities in insect larvae such as mealworms. For example, it has been applied to analyze PCR-amplified 16S rRNA fragments from the mealworm gut microbiome and to evaluate how dietary factors, including plastic- or mask-based diets, influence microbial composition. These applications highlight its role in advancing understanding of how environmental and dietary variables shape host-associated microbial ecosystems.  

Overall, the Illumina MiSeq is a versatile and reliable sequencing platform that underpins a wide range of microbiological and ecological studies. By enabling precise, efficient, and high-quality sequencing of bacterial and fungal communities, it has become an essential tool for microbiome research, environmental microbiology, and studies of host–microbe interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used in the study to assess gut bacterial and fungal microbiomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used for paired-end sequencing of purified amplicons in microbial community analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used for paired-end sequencing of the V3-V4 region of the 16S rRNA gene.&lt;SEP&gt;Illumina MiSeq is the sequencing platform used in paired-end mode (2x250) to analyze microbial communities in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Illumina MiSeq is a sequencing platform used in paired-end mode for DNA sequencing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f8516b10110f884279870c2ef887f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512840a413df7ae3d881389c5cf1feb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee</data>
