<node id="Tenericutes">
  <data key="d0">Tenericutes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Tenericutes is a bacterial phylum that plays a significant role in the gut microbiome of mealworms, particularly under varying dietary conditions. It has been consistently identified as one of the dominant phyla in mealworm gut microbial communities, with its relative abundance strongly influenced by the type of substrate consumed. Studies have shown that Tenericutes is especially prevalent in yellow mealworms fed on synthetic polymers such as polyethylene (PE), polystyrene (PS), polypropylene (PP), and polyurethane (PU), as well as in those fed on conventional bran diets. Its abundance often increases in groups fed with PS, PP, and corn starch (CS), and it has been reported in higher proportions in PE-oxo feeding variants compared to other diets. These findings highlight the phylum’s adaptability and importance in microbial responses to both natural and synthetic feeding substrates.  

Within Tenericutes, taxonomic groups such as Mollicutes and Entomoplasmatales have been detected, reflecting the diversity encompassed by this phylum in mealworm gut ecosystems. The consistent representation of Tenericutes across experimental datasets, with measurable abundance values under different dietary treatments, underscores its ecological relevance. Its presence and fluctuations in abundance suggest that Tenericutes contributes to the digestion processes and microbial adaptation mechanisms that enable mealworms to utilize a wide range of substrates, including plastics. Overall, Tenericutes is recognized as a key bacterial phylum shaping the structure and function of mealworm gut microbiomes across diverse feeding conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304c1b42a6d3f439e83f380d2d64420a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73db2a18ccd822d0da3ef61e68d3a6f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc</data>
