  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Clostridia is a bacterial class with higher proportions in OAT and lower in PE-oxo and PS variants.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridia is a bacterial class included in the dataset with measured abundance across substrates.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridia are anaerobic bacteria within the Firmicutes phylum, mentioned as spore formers in the mealworm gut microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridia is a group of Gram-positive bacteria associated with PS degradation under anaerobic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridia is a bacterial class within the phylum Firmicutes, represented in the study by Clostridiales.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridia is one of the bacterial classes found abundantly in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor.</data>
