  <data key="d2">Bacilli is a bacterial class widely distributed across feeding variants, with highest proportions in PE-oxo and PS.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacilli is a bacterial class listed in the dataset with measured abundance across substrates.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacilli are aerobic bacteria within the Firmicutes phylum, mentioned as spore formers in the mealworm gut microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacilli is a bacterial class within Firmicutes, associated with PS degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacilli is one of the bacterial classes found abundantly in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacilli is a bacterial class more abundant in PS samples (13%) compared to CT samples (7%).&lt;SEP&gt;Bacilli is a bacterial class mentioned in the table, including Virgibacillus sp. and Pseudogracilbacillus.</data>
