<node id="Termites">
  <data key="d0">Termites</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Termites are insects whose digestive tracts host microbial communities capable of cellulose degradation and nitrogen cycling.&lt;SEP&gt;Termites are insects studied by Butler and Buckerfield for their ability to digest synthetic lignin hydrocarbons, converting part of it into CO2.&lt;SEP&gt;Termites are referenced as insects with diets based on lignocellulose, practically devoid of nitrogen compounds, used as a comparison to mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Termites are insects whose diet is based on lignocellulose, which is practically devoid of nitrogen compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Termites are insects that rely on nitrogen-fixing bacteria to supplement their nitrogen supply when feeding on low-nitrogen diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Termites are lignocellulose-feeding insects with gut microbial communities that act as lignin degraders.&lt;SEP&gt;Insects studied for lignocellulose-degrading enzymes and their symbiotic microbiota.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db579d338d8f90574e3ac67a3ae9938d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
