<node id="Rhodococcus sp.">
  <data key="d0">Rhodococcus sp.</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Rhodococcus sp. is a bacterial taxon within the phylum Actinobacteria that has been studied for its diverse ecological roles and metabolic capabilities. This group of bacteria is notable for its association with insects, particularly as part of the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor (mealworm) larvae, where it contributes to the degradation of complex substrates such as polystyrene and corn straw. In this symbiotic context, Rhodococcus sp. not only aids in the breakdown of otherwise recalcitrant polymers but also provides essential amino acids to its insect hosts, thereby supporting their nutrition and metabolic needs.  

Beyond insect-associated environments, Rhodococcus sp. has also been isolated from mangrove sediments, where it has been investigated for its role in the biodeterioration of synthetic polymers, including polypropylene microplastics. This highlights its potential importance in environmental biodegradation processes, particularly in the context of plastic pollution. Studies have further proposed Rhodococcus sp. as a candidate organism involved in the biological mechanisms underlying styrene degradation, underscoring its relevance in the breakdown of aromatic hydrocarbons and related compounds.  

Overall, Rhodococcus sp. represents a versatile bacterial group with significant ecological and biotechnological importance. Its ability to degrade synthetic polymers such as polystyrene and polypropylene, coupled with its role in nutrient provision within insect microbiomes, positions it as a key organism of interest in both environmental sustainability research and the study of insect-microbe interactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
