<node id="Appl. Environ. Microbiol.">
  <data key="d0">Appl. Environ. Microbiol.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">*Applied and Environmental Microbiology* (Appl. Environ. Microbiol.) is a peer-reviewed scientific journal that serves as a leading platform for research in applied microbiology and environmental microbiology. The journal publishes studies that explore microbial processes, microbial ecology, and the interactions between microorganisms and their environments, with a particular emphasis on biodegradation and microbial community dynamics.  

Since its inception, *Applied and Environmental Microbiology* has been recognized for disseminating influential research on the microbial degradation of both natural and synthetic polymers. A landmark 1979 study published in the journal investigated the biodegradation of polystyrene, poly(methyl methacrylate), and phenol formaldehyde, providing early insights into microbial pathways for breaking down synthetic materials. In 1991, the journal featured important work on the biodegradation of polyethylene glycols by *Pseudomonas stutzeri*, as well as studies advancing microbial community classification and characterization methods. In 1992, it published research on the degradation of starch-polyethylene plastics in compost environments, contributing to the understanding of biodegradable plastics and their environmental fate.  

The journal has continued to play a central role in advancing knowledge on plastic biodegradation. It has published studies on the microbial degradation of polystyrene and other plastics, including research on the gut microbial flora of *Plesiophthalmus davidis* larvae and investigations by Kaplan, Hartenstein, and Sutter into the biodegradation of synthetic polymers. More recently, a 2019 study in *Applied and Environmental Microbiology* addressed microbial degradation of plastics, underscoring the journal’s ongoing relevance to contemporary environmental challenges.  

Beyond plastics, the journal has been a venue for broader ecological and methodological contributions. It has published studies on bacterial diversity, the coevolution of termite gut microbiota, and the development of computational tools such as the Naive Bayesian classifier for rRNA taxonomy assignment, which has become a widely used method in microbial ecology.  

Overall, *Applied and Environmental Microbiology* (Appl. Environ. Microbiol.) is recognized as a prominent and authoritative journal in the life sciences. It has consistently provided a platform for foundational and innovative research in biodegradation, microbial ecology, and environmental microbiology, shaping scientific understanding of microbial processes and their applications in addressing environmental and industrial challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;Appl. Environ. Microbiol. is a scientific journal where a study on biodegradation of polystyrene, poly(methyl methacrylate), and phenol formaldehyde was published.&lt;SEP&gt;Appl. Environ. Microbiol. is the journal in which the 2020 study on biodegradation of polystyrene by gut microbial flora of Plesiophthalmus davidis larvae was published.&lt;SEP&gt;Applied and Environmental Microbiology is the journal where the study on polystyrene biodegradation by Plesiophthalmus davidi larvae was published.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal where the termite gut microbiota diversity study was published.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-866df96ed7f051acf60ebd0e82d9a19e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68a8917166a3e45f4bf51e2e04949f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41af774fc28352c7dd95d8c3cb43f855&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56425bd62513be46b9165bfd84f0dd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57e056cd3b06b37d22117fc75e3a4df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2</data>
