<node id="Priestia megaterium S1">
  <data key="d0">Priestia megaterium S1</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Priestia megaterium S1 is a microbial isolate obtained from the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae fed on Styrofoam. It has the ability to degrade polyethylene (PE) and polystyrene (PS) beads, showing significant biodegradation capacity proven by weight loss studies, FTIR, and SEM analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Priestia megaterium S1 is a microorganism isolated from Tenebrio molitor, tested on PS beads for 180 days, studied in microbiome context.&lt;SEP&gt;Priestia megaterium S1 is a polymer degrading gut microbe isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae fed on Styrofoam.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2961e2aad708e7b78a585260097b4d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381155</data>
</node>
