<node id="Scanning Electron Microscope (SEM)">
  <data key="d0">Scanning Electron Microscope (SEM)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">SEM is an analytical technique used in the study to observe surface biodegradation of plastics by Priestia megaterium S1.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM is used to characterize morphological and functional changes in plastics during biodegradation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;The scanning electron microscope (SEM) was used to observe colonies on agar and PS sheet surfaces at various magnifications to evaluate microbial growth effects.&lt;SEP&gt;SEM was used to observe bacterial growth and modifications on PS sheets, revealing tunnels, cracks, grooves, and aggregates formed by bacterial isolates.&lt;SEP&gt;The scanning electron microscope was used to observe morphology and micro-area composition of frass from larvae fed with mask layers.&lt;SEP&gt;The scanning electron microscope was used to analyze surface changes in polystyrene films caused by bacterial activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2e818c436fabed80b9d3d720ebf491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386809</data>
</node>
