<node id="Insects">
  <data key="d0">Insects</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Insects are mentioned as organisms that, in combination with microorganisms, can break down plastics and natural polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Organisms studied for metabolic impacts when exposed to plastic feed substrates.&lt;SEP&gt;Insects are the largest group within the animal kingdom arthropod phylum, abundant and diverse, some capable of degrading plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Insects are mentioned as organisms that can convert natural polymers into smaller fragments to facilitate enzymatic reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Insects, including beetles and larvae, have been investigated since the 1950s for their ability to eat plastics and damage packaging materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Insects are organisms that rely on fat, carbohydrates, and proteins as energy sources, with specific metabolic responses during starvation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e2601f950d62c093ceb86612b2374f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2e818c436fabed80b9d3d720ebf491</data>
