<node id="Ethanol">
  <data key="d0">Ethanol</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">70% ethanol was used to disinfect beads and clean them after experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Absolute ethanol (&gt;99.5% purity) is used to kill larvae for gut microbiome analysis and preserve specimens.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethanol is used as a solvent to extract ethanol-extractable fractions from frass samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethanol was used to submerge and kill mealworms in order to avoid contamination of non-metabolized or partially metabolized 13C-labeled products.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethanol was used to wash samples after completion of the reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethanol is used for surface sterilization, stain extraction, and preparation of crystal violet solutions in biofilm and PS film assays.&lt;SEP&gt;Ethanol of analytical grade was used as part of the solvent extraction process in the biodegradation study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a478461d1471ca083f90b3f8e7456e</data>
