  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">FTIR spectroscopy was performed to analyze LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads before and after treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR Spectroscopy was used to analyze LDPE beads in the biodegradation study.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR Spectroscopy was used to analyze PS beads, showing chemical structure changes after treatment with PM S1.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR spectroscopy is used in the study to determine the appearance or removal of functional groups in polymer molecules, helping to identify degradation products and chemical changes in LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR Spectroscopy is an analytical method used to examine chemical alterations at the surface of PVC fragments.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR spectroscopy is an analytical method used to study gaseous compounds produced during thermal decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR spectroscopy is a technique studied for reading and interpreting organic material structures.</data>
