<node id="PM S1">
  <data key="d0">PM S1</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">PM S1 refers to a microbial strain or isolate studied for colonization and degradation of LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads.&lt;SEP&gt;PM S1 is a bacterial isolate from the gut microbiome of mealworms, identified through 16S rRNA sequencing. It showed 99% homology with Bacillus-related genera and demonstrated the ability to degrade PE and PS as a sole carbon source.&lt;SEP&gt;PM S1 is a microbial strain used in the study that consumes dissolved oxygen and demonstrates biodegradation capabilities over LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads.</data>
