<node id="Plastic Waste Accumulation">
  <data key="d0">Plastic Waste Accumulation</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Plastic waste accumulation is described as an environmental issue requiring biodegradation strategies for sustainable waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;The accumulation of plastic waste in the environment due to low recycling rates and resistance to degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste accumulation refers to the buildup of polyurethane and other plastics in landfills and aquatic systems, creating environmental problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste accumulation refers to the global issue of increasing plastic production and waste exceeding recycling and biodegradation rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756380843</data>
</node>
<node id="Biodegradation Strategy">
  <data key="d0">Biodegradation Strategy</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Biodegradation strategy refers to the approach of using microbial strains like PM S1 to degrade plastics such as LDPE, HDPE, and PS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756371421</data>
</node>
<node id="Biological Oxygen Demand">
  <data key="d0">Biological Oxygen Demand</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Biological Oxygen Demand (BOD) is mentioned as a parameter supporting the evidence of biodegradation of plastics by PM S1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756371421</data>
</node>
<node id="Control Beads">
  <data key="d0">Control Beads</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Control beads are untreated LDPE, HDPE, and PS samples used for comparison in FTIR and SEM studies, showing no degradation or surface cracks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756371421</data>
</node>
<node id="Study">
  <data key="d0">Study</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The study investigates the biodegradation of LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads by the microbial strain PM S1, using methods such as FTIR, SEM, Sturm test, and CO2 evolution analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;The study investigated the effects of PS foam as feed for mealworms, comparing productivity with standard diets, and explored biodegradation potential with microbes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382410</data>
</node>
