<node id="Brandon AM">
  <data key="d0">Brandon AM</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Brandon AM is a researcher and author whose work primarily focuses on the biodegradation of synthetic polymers, particularly polystyrene and polyethylene, through biological processes involving mealworms. He has contributed to multiple studies investigating the capacity of yellow mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) to digest and degrade polystyrene waste, providing insights into the potential of insect-mediated biodegradation as a solution to plastic pollution. His research includes detailed examinations of polystyrene digestion pathways in mealworms, the fate of associated chemical additives such as the flame retardant hexabromocyclododecane (HBCD) during the degradation process, and the broader implications of these findings for environmental remediation.  

In addition to polystyrene, Brandon AM has co-authored studies exploring the biodegradation of polyethylene and plastic mixtures in mealworms, expanding the scope of inquiry beyond a single polymer type. His work emphasizes both the biological mechanisms underlying plastic degradation and the practical applications of these processes in addressing global plastic waste challenges. By contributing to research on the progress and potential of polystyrene biodegradation, Brandon AM has helped advance scientific understanding of insect-based plastic waste management strategies and their role in mitigating environmental pollution.  

Overall, Brandon AM’s body of work highlights the intersection of environmental science, microbiology, and waste management, with a particular emphasis on developing innovative, biologically driven solutions to the persistent problem of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of studies on biodegradation of plastics in mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Brandon AM is an author of referenced studies on biodegradation of polyethylene and polystyrene in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of multiple studies on biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Brandon AM is an author of a 2018 study on biodegradation of polyethylene and plastic mixtures in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Brandon AM is an author of research on microbial degradation and valorization of plastic wastes.&lt;SEP&gt;Brandon AM is an author of a study on polystyrene digestion and biodegradation within yellow mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4ff228c7711f94fb27152b187b1fa3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa27760a0a889fe7b58360dbb150cdf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a882603f777986db9d8fc65cea91dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-372aa232f6e8aad1d8e0a93f16a42b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa884bb7540491e8ab975e29c46d1f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aac53ba8b358857c4dcd3b6cd9e8991</data>
