<node id="Criddle CS">
  <data key="d0">Criddle CS</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Criddle CS is a researcher and author recognized for extensive contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly through the role of insect larvae as biological agents of degradation. Their work has focused on the capacity of organisms such as mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) and wax moth larvae to break down synthetic polymers, including polystyrene, polyethylene, poly mixtures, and polyvinyl chloride (PVC).  

Criddle CS has co-authored multiple studies that investigate the mechanisms and outcomes of plastic biodegradation in these larvae, with a particular emphasis on polystyrene. This includes a 2019 study examining the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms, as well as research on the degradation of polystyrene wastes in yellow mealworms. Beyond polystyrene, Criddle CS has contributed to studies exploring the biodegradation of polyethylene and mixed plastic polymers, highlighting the potential of insect larvae to process diverse plastic types.  

In addition to experimental work on specific polymers, Criddle CS has also engaged in broader research on microplastics pollution, situating the biodegradation studies within the larger environmental context of plastic waste accumulation and its ecological impacts. By examining both the degradation pathways and the environmental implications, their work contributes to advancing knowledge on biological solutions to plastic pollution.  

Overall, Criddle CS is recognized as a significant contributor to the field of plastic biodegradation research, with a body of work that spans multiple polymer types, insect species, and environmental considerations, positioning them as an important figure in the exploration of sustainable strategies for mitigating plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Criddle CS is an author of referenced studies on biodegradation of plastics in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Criddle CS is an author of multiple studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of multiple studies on biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Criddle CS is a co-author of a 2018 study on biodegradation of plastics in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Criddle CS is an author of research on biodegradation of PVC in Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Criddle CS is an author of a study on polystyrene digestion and biodegradation within yellow mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4ff228c7711f94fb27152b187b1fa3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa27760a0a889fe7b58360dbb150cdf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-372aa232f6e8aad1d8e0a93f16a42b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6464a2f3ca18442f70e254b9341a3e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa884bb7540491e8ab975e29c46d1f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fe36521680f0d09a603eab04706561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aac53ba8b358857c4dcd3b6cd9e8991</data>
