<node id="Biodegradation of Plastics">
  <data key="d0">Biodegradation of Plastics</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Biodegradation of plastics refers to the microbial, fungal, and insect-mediated breakdown of synthetic polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation of plastics refers to the process of breaking down plastic polymers by biological, chemical, or physical means, often studied through various analytical methods.&lt;SEP&gt;A research topic discussed in a cited article, described as a state-of-the-art review.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation of plastics refers to the process studied since the 1970s, involving microbial and enzymatic approaches to break down polymers such as PE and PET.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation of plastics is a research focus mentioned in the text, studied in various insect species including Tenebrio molitor.</data>
