<node id="High Impact Polystyrene (HIPS)">
  <data key="d0">High Impact Polystyrene (HIPS)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">High Impact Polystyrene (HIPS) is a type of polystyrene plastic widely used in production and manufacturing, particularly in electronic applications, where it is often classified as an e-plastic. In this context, HIPS may contain additives such as decabromodiphenyl oxide and antimony trioxide, which are flame retardants but also considered hazardous materials. Due to its extensive use and persistence in the environment, HIPS has been the subject of research focused on its degradation and potential recycling pathways.  

Studies have shown that HIPS can undergo microbial-assisted degradation, making it a candidate for biotechnological approaches to plastic waste management. Certain microorganisms, including species of *Pseudomonas* and *Bacillus*, produce esterases capable of breaking down HIPS polymers. In addition to microbial activity, biological degradation has also been observed in invertebrates. For example, larvae of *Tenebrio molitor* (commonly known as mealworms) have demonstrated the ability to ingest and depolymerize HIPS, suggesting a potential role for insect-based biodegradation in addressing plastic pollution.  

Overall, High Impact Polystyrene (HIPS) is both an important industrial material and a focus of environmental research. Its durability and widespread use in electronics contribute to waste management challenges, while its susceptibility to microbial and insect-mediated degradation highlights emerging opportunities for sustainable disposal and recycling strategies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56425bd62513be46b9165bfd84f0dd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826</data>
