<node id="Chemosphere">
  <data key="d0">Chemosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">**Chemosphere** is a peer-reviewed international scientific journal published by Elsevier that specializes in environmental science, with a strong focus on pollution, toxicology, ecological sustainability, and innovative approaches to environmental remediation. It serves as a leading platform for disseminating research that addresses pressing global environmental challenges, including microplastic contamination, plastic pollution, and the development of sustainable bioremediation strategies.  

The journal has played a pivotal role in advancing scientific understanding of plastic biodegradation, particularly through its publication of landmark studies on insect- and microbe-mediated polymer digestion. Among its most influential contributions are investigations into the ability of *Tenebrio molitor* larvae (yellow mealworms) to ingest and metabolize synthetic polymers such as polystyrene, polyethylene, and polyurethane foams. These studies have provided molecular-level insights into insect-mediated plastic digestion, including transcriptomic responses to plastic-based diets, and have highlighted the potential of mealworms as biological agents for mitigating plastic waste. Notable publications include the 2018 studies “Biodegradation of Polystyrene Wastes in Yellow Mealworms” and “Ubiquity of Polystyrene Digestion and Biodegradation within Yellow Mealworms,” as well as subsequent research in 2020 on polystyrene and low-density polyethylene degradation.  

Chemosphere has also expanded knowledge of insect-based plastic degradation pathways by publishing studies on foam plastic biodegradation by *Zophobas atratus* larvae and on the breakdown of expanded polystyrene and low-density polyethylene foams. Beyond insect-focused research, the journal has featured important microbial studies, such as the 2017 work by Eyheraguibel and colleagues on polyethylene biodegradation by *Rhodococcus rhodochrous*, as well as investigations into bacterial colonization of micro-polyethylene particles. These contributions have broadened the understanding of microbial mechanisms for addressing plastic pollution.  

In addition to biodegradation research, Chemosphere has published influential studies on the environmental impacts of microplastic pollution in aquatic ecosystems, including case studies in Chinese seas and Gorgan Bay. It has also examined the ecological effects of pollutants such as phenanthrene on soil organisms like earthworms and has addressed the broader consequences of hydrocarbon-based plastics in natural environments.  

Through this diverse body of work, Chemosphere has established itself as a leading venue for research on plastic biodegradation, insect- and microbe-mediated polymer digestion, and comprehensive strategies for environmental sustainability. By fostering interdisciplinary research and promoting innovative solutions, the journal continues to shape international approaches to environmental protection, pollution mitigation, and sustainable resource management.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemosphere is a scientific journal where studies on biodegradation of plastics and environmental toxicology are published.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal where a study on polystyrene biodegradation by mealworms was published.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f3828bbe45c2c38004a29d55dcbf40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f830cfd93570c7a9762518aa356ab69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fe36521680f0d09a603eab04706561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-908b8bfa7e446694958cf9bd0cfbc583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68a8917166a3e45f4bf51e2e04949f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39598f698094d1663ca3438bc143bc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7768b61a3d166f2cd01d4e87ac88cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4da90774e2e5cb1fea30fd5aa390760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77298fbeb95f87269261b74c2158d5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c2