<node id="Springer Nature">
  <data key="d0">Springer Nature</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Springer Nature is a global academic publishing company that serves as the publisher of numerous scientific journals, books, and research outputs. It is the parent organization of Springer-Verlag GmbH Germany and Springer Science+Business Media, LLC, both of which are responsible for publishing scholarly studies across a wide range of disciplines. Among its portfolio of journals, Springer Nature publishes *Chemosphere*, a prominent journal in the field of environmental science.  

In its publishing practices, Springer Nature consistently issues a formal note of neutrality regarding jurisdictional claims in published maps and institutional affiliations. This statement underscores the company’s commitment to maintaining impartiality and avoiding the endorsement of any territorial or political claims that may be represented in the materials it disseminates. The neutrality note is applied across its publications, including cited works, referenced studies, and journal articles, ensuring a standardized approach to sensitive geopolitical issues.  

Through its role as both a publisher and parent organization, Springer Nature plays a central part in advancing global research dissemination while upholding principles of neutrality and academic integrity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4ff228c7711f94fb27152b187b1fa3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa5755e6c9a5eeae3f595d901dff422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8f385513fcff2125529486530ad5a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2359b10600f30376fe077f5e942cc999</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
