  <data key="d0">Kluyvera</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Kluyvera is a bacterial genus associated with polypropylene diet in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Kluyvera is a bacterial genus associated with mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;A bacterial genus predominant in the gut microbiota of larvae across all diet groups, with high abundance in CS-fed larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Kluyvera is a bacterial genus enriched in the gut microbiome of superworm after PS feeding.&lt;SEP&gt;Kluyvera is a bacterial genus predominant in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae during PP degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Kluyvera is a bacterial genus identified as a nitrogen-fixing gut bacterium in mealworms.</data>
