<node id="Global Plastic Production">
  <data key="d0">Global Plastic Production</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">In 2019, global plastic production reached 368 million tons, marking an increase compared to 2018.&lt;SEP&gt;Global plastic production increased from 1.5 million tons in 1950 to 299 million tons in 2013, with continuous growth expected.&lt;SEP&gt;The worldwide production of plastics, which reached 390.7 million tons per year by 2021 and is projected to reach 800 million tons by 2035 and 1600 million tons by 2050.&lt;SEP&gt;Global plastic production has tripled in the last 25 years, reaching over 322 million tons in 2015, contributing to waste management challenges and environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Global plastic production reached approximately 430 million tons in 2023, with two-thirds being short-lived plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Global plastic production reached 370 million metric tons in 2021 and is projected to increase to 12,000 Mt by 2050.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387398</data>
</node>
