<node id="Aspergillus">
  <data key="d0">Aspergillus</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Aspergillus is a fungal genus widely recognized for its role in plastic biodegradation, particularly within insect gut microbiota. Multiple studies have reported Aspergillus in the digestive systems of mealworms, lesser mealworms (Alphitobius diaperinus), and wax moth larvae when these insects were fed on synthetic polymers such as polystyrene (PS), polyethylene (PE), and components of disposable masks. In these contexts, Aspergillus has been consistently identified as a dominant or overrepresented genus, suggesting a strong association with plastic degradation processes. For example, in yellow mealworms fed on plastics, Aspergillus accounted for approximately 8% of the gut fungal community, while in mask-fed diets it appeared in high abundance across all treatment groups.  

The genus includes species with confirmed plastic-degrading capacity, such as *Aspergillus flavus* strain PEDX3, which has been experimentally shown to degrade polyethylene. More broadly, Aspergillus species have been linked to the breakdown of several types of synthetic polymers, including PS and PE, and their frequent recovery in resampled PS-fed systems further supports their persistence and functional role in biodegradation.  

Overall, Aspergillus emerges as a key fungal genus in the context of insect-mediated plastic degradation. Its consistent presence across different insect hosts, diets, and experimental conditions highlights its ecological importance and potential utility in biotechnological applications aimed at mitigating plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Aspergillus is a fungal genus with reported plastic degradation ability, found in plastics-fed Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Aspergillus is a fungal genus observed in PU-fed groups, reported to have plastic degradation ability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbb6f13dbe3de759712fa3a0c9780470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
