  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Trichoderma is a fungal genus reported to be involved in PS plastic degradation in mealworm guts.&lt;SEP&gt;Trichoderma is a fungal genus reported in PS-fed lesser mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Trichoderma is a fungal genus identified in the gut microbiota of polystyrene-fed Alphitobius diaperinus and associated with plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Trichoderma is a fungal genus found to be overrepresented in PS samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Trichoderma is a fungal genus identified as overrepresented in PS samples compared to CT samples, though rarely recovered in resamples.&lt;SEP&gt;Trichoderma is a fungal genus with species such as Trichoderma viride capable of degrading LDPE.</data>
