<node id="Superworm (Z. atratus)">
  <data key="d0">Superworm (Z. atratus)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Superworm larvae (Z. atratus) were used in experiments to test plastic degradation with PE and PS diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworm (Z. atratus) is a larval species studied for its ability to consume plastics such as polystyrene (PS) and polyethylene (PE). In the experiment, superworms showed higher plastic consumption rates compared to yellow mealworms but experienced significant weight loss and reduced survival rates when fed solely on plastic diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworm (Z. atratus) is an insect species studied for its ability to consume plastics such as polystyrene (PS) and polyurethane (PU). Its life cycle includes egg, larva, pupa, and adult stages. In experiments, superworms showed higher PS consumption efficiency compared to yellow mealworms.</data>
