<node id="PU (Polyurethane)">
  <data key="d0">PU (Polyurethane)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PU (polyurethane) was associated with bacterial communities in superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;PU (Polyurethane) is a plastic material tested for biodegradation by insects such as T. molitor and Zophobas morio.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyurethane (PU) is a type of foam plastic studied for biodegradation by mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;PU refers to polyurethane, a type of plastic used as feed in the experiment to measure consumption and effects on larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;PU is a type of plastic foam used as a sole feedstock for yellow mealworms in one of the experimental groups.&lt;SEP&gt;PU is a type of plastic polymer tested in the study. It was consumed by yellow mealworms and showed broad depolymerization in their gut.</data>
