  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Yellow mealworm (T. molitor) is a larval species studied for its ability to consume plastics such as polystyrene (PS) and polyethylene (PE). In the experiment, yellow mealworms showed lower plastic consumption rates compared to superworms but maintained slight weight increases.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworm (T. molitor) is an insect species studied for its ability to consume plastics such as polystyrene (PS) and polyurethane (PU). Its life cycle includes egg, larva, pupa, and adult stages. In experiments, yellow mealworms showed lower PS consumption efficiency compared to superworms but similar PU consumption efficiency.</data>
