  <data key="d2">Foam plastics, including polystyrene (PS) and polyethylene (PE), were used as feedstocks in the experiment to test larval consumption and degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Foam plastics, including polystyrene (PS) and polyurethane (PU), were tested as diets for superworms and yellow mealworms, with consumption rates measured.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of plastic studied for biodegradation by Zophobas atratus larvae.</data>
