<node id="Superworms (Z. atratus)">
  <data key="d0">Superworms (Z. atratus)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Superworms (Z. atratus) are larvae studied for their ability to ingest and partially degrade plastics such as polyethylene (PE) and polystyrene (PS). Their frass pellets are larger due to their larger body size and mouthparts.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms (Z. atratus) are larvae studied for their ability to degrade plastics such as polyethylene (PE) and polystyrene (PS). Their frass showed reduced plastic degradation compared to yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms (Z. atratus) are plastic-degrading insects that did not produce NPs in frass when fed with PS and PE foams.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms (Z. atratus) are organisms reported to degrade PS polymers in a similar way to mealworms.</data>
