  <data key="d2">DSC-TGA (Differential Scanning Calorimetry - Thermogravimetric Analysis) is an analytical technique used to examine thermal stability and degradation of plastics and frass samples.&lt;SEP&gt;DSC-TGA is a thermal analysis technique used to assess the thermal stability and weight loss of plastics and frass samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Differential scanning calorimetry and thermogravimetric analysis were used to study thermal properties of degraded polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;DSC-TGA is an analytical technique used to analyze polymer degradation in the experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;DSC-TGA is an analytical method used to confirm differences in composition and thermal stability of plastics and frass after digestion by yellow mealworms.</data>
