<node id="Basidiomycota">
  <data key="d0">Basidiomycota</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Basidiomycota is a fungal phylum that increased in PS- and PE-fed yellow mealworm guts, associated with plastic diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Basidiomycota is a fungal phylum well represented in PS samples but rare in CT samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Basidiomycota is a fungal phylum found at high frequency in PS samples but almost absent in CT samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Basidiomycota is a phylum of fungi encountered at fairly high frequency in PS samples and nearly absent in CT samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Basidiomycota is a fungal phylum found in the gut fungal community of yellow mealworms, associated with polymer degradation.</data>
