<node id="Greater Wax Moth">
  <data key="d0">Greater Wax Moth</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Greater wax moth was mentioned in relation to Pseudomonas being associated with PS degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Greater wax moth is a type of larva included in the study. It consumed PS but showed lower PS degradation ability compared to superworms, with moderate survival and weight change results.&lt;SEP&gt;Greater wax moth is one of the insect larvae species studied for its ability to degrade polystyrene (PS), with distinct microbial diversity trends compared to other species.&lt;SEP&gt;Greater wax moth is one of the insect larvae species analyzed for gut microbial composition changes under polystyrene (PS) feeding.</data>
