<node id="Environ. Pollut.">
  <data key="d0">Environ. Pollut.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">*Environmental Pollution* (abbreviated as *Environ. Pollut.*) is a peer-reviewed scientific journal dedicated to advancing research in environmental science, with a strong emphasis on pollution and its ecological impacts. The journal provides a multidisciplinary platform for studies that address the sources, pathways, and consequences of environmental contaminants, particularly plastics and microplastics, and is widely recognized as a leading venue for research in this domain.  

A central focus of *Environmental Pollution* has been the biodegradation of plastics by biological agents. The journal has published influential studies on the ability of insect larvae, including *Tenebrio molitor* (mealworms) and *Zophobas atratus* (superworms), to degrade synthetic polymers such as polyethylene, polystyrene, and polyester polyurethane. These investigations have explored both the physical breakdown of plastics and the biological mechanisms underlying degradation, with particular attention to the role of the gut microbiome and enzymatic activity in facilitating depolymerization. Research articles have detailed the microbial diversity and enzymatic profiles associated with insect larvae when fed plastics, providing insights into the biochemical pathways that enable plastic degradation. Beyond insect-based systems, *Environmental Pollution* has also featured studies on fungal contributions, such as the capacity of *Aspergillus tubingensis* to degrade plastics, thereby expanding the scope of biological solutions to plastic pollution.  

The journal has also been instrumental in documenting the ecological distribution and impacts of microplastics. Published studies have reported the incorporation of microplastics into the burrows of earthworms (*Lumbricus terrestris*) and their ingestion by terrestrial invertebrates such as snails, highlighting the pervasive nature of microplastic contamination in soil ecosystems. These findings underscore the interactions between microplastics and soil organisms, contributing to a deeper understanding of how plastic pollution influences biodiversity, soil processes, and ecosystem health.  

In addition to empirical studies, *Environmental Pollution* has published reviews and evaluations of broader strategies to mitigate global plastic pollution. This includes assessments of biodegradable plastics as potential sustainable alternatives and analyses of microplastic formation and environmental persistence. By integrating research across microbiology, ecology, and environmental science, the journal provides a comprehensive perspective on pollution challenges and potential mitigation pathways.  

Overall, *Environmental Pollution* (*Environ. Pollut.*) is recognized as a leading scientific journal for research on plastic pollution, biodegradation processes, and the ecological consequences of microplastics. It serves as a critical resource for scientists, policymakers, and environmental practitioners seeking to understand and address the environmental impacts of pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Environ. Pollut. is a scientific journal where studies on the fate of plastic in the environment and nanoplastics in aquatic systems were published.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal where the study on regional distribution of styrene analogues from polystyrene degradation was published.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4da90774e2e5cb1fea30fd5aa390760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77298fbeb95f87269261b74c2158d5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af93e805daf3987d95ff99ab8e891d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582</data>
