<node id="Front. Microbiol.">
  <data key="d0">Front. Microbiol.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">**Front. Microbiol. (Frontiers in Microbiology)** is a peer-reviewed scientific journal that publishes research across the field of microbiology, with a particular emphasis on microbial processes, interactions, and their environmental and applied implications. The journal has served as a platform for a wide range of studies, including those addressing pressing global challenges such as plastic pollution and microbial ecology.  

Several notable publications in *Front. Microbiol.* have focused on the microbial degradation and valorization of plastic wastes, highlighting the potential of microorganisms and enzymes to break down synthetic polymers and contribute to sustainable waste management. This includes research on the microbial and enzymatic degradation of synthetic plastics, as well as studies specifically examining the biodegradation of polyurethane and xenobiotic additives. The journal has also published reviews, such as the work by Jacquin and colleagues on microbial ecotoxicology of marine plastic debris, which explored the interactions between microbial communities and plastic pollutants in marine environments.  

Beyond plastics, *Front. Microbiol.* has featured research on the environmental impacts of microplastics and nanoplastics, underscoring the journal’s role in advancing understanding of how these emerging contaminants affect ecosystems and microbial dynamics.  

In addition to its focus on environmental microbiology, the journal has published studies in diverse areas of microbial science. For example, a 2017 study on bacteria-specific primer pairs was published in *Front. Microbiol.*, contributing to methodological advancements in microbial community analysis. Similarly, a 2016 study on the intestinal microbiota of broiler chickens appeared in the journal, reflecting its coverage of host-microbe interactions and applications in animal health and agriculture.  

Overall, *Front. Microbiol.* (Frontiers in Microbiology) is a multidisciplinary journal that provides a venue for research spanning microbial ecology, biotechnology, environmental microbiology, and host-microbe interactions. Its publications demonstrate a strong commitment to addressing both fundamental scientific questions and applied challenges, particularly in relation to microbial roles in environmental sustainability and health.&lt;SEP&gt;Front. Microbiol. is the journal where the study on microbial and enzymatic degradation of synthetic plastics was published in 2020.&lt;SEP&gt;Front. Microbiol. (Frontiers in Microbiology) is the journal where the study on degradation of polyurethane and xenobiotic additives by a landfill microbial community was published.</data>
