  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Zophobas aratus, also known as superworm, is a beetle larva species studied for its ability to biodegrade low-density polyethylene and polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Zophobas aratus, also known as superworm, is studied for its ingestion preferences and biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Zophobas aratus is a beetle larvae species (Coleoptera: Tenebrionidae) studied for its ability to biodegrade foam plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Larvae of Zophobas aratus (superworms) studied for their ability to biodegrade polyethylene and polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Zophobas aratus, also referred to as superworms, is mentioned as larvae studied for their ability to biodegrade plastics and associated gut microbiome changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Larvae species studied for its ability to biodegrade polystyrene.</data>
