<node id="Enterobacter asburiae YT1">
  <data key="d0">Enterobacter asburiae YT1</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a bacterial strain isolated from waxworm gut shown to degrade PE films.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a bacterial strain reported to degrade LDPE.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a gut bacterium that removed approximately 6.1% of LDPE films after 60 days.&lt;SEP&gt;A PE-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the intestine of plodia interpunctella larvae by Yang et al.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of waxworms, capable of degrading PE.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae YT1 is a microbial strain capable of degrading commercial LDPE film.</data>
