  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Linear low-density polyethylene (LLDPE) is a form of polyethylene that mealworms were not capable of ingesting in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;LLDPE is a type of plastic that mealworms were not capable of ingesting.&lt;SEP&gt;LLDPE is a type of polyethylene with lower crystallinity due to branching, making it less resistant to biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;LLDPE is a type of polyethylene with medium crystallinity and more short chain branching than HDPE.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of polyethylene with middle crystallinity and higher short chain branching, tested for biodegradation in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;LLDPE is a type of polyethylene plastic that Tenebrio molitor larvae cannot degrade.</data>
