<node id="Polydispersity Index (PDI)">
  <data key="d0">Polydispersity Index (PDI)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PDI was measured for PP, LDPE, and LLDPE to assess polymer molecular weight distribution.&lt;SEP&gt;The Polydispersity Index (PDI) is a measure of the distribution of molecular mass in a given polymer sample. In the study, PDI values of HDPE, LLDPE, and LDPE were compared before and after biodegradation by Tenebrio larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Polydispersity index (PDI) is a measure of molecular weight distribution of polystyrene microplastics, which decreases after digestion by mealworms, indicating a narrower distribution.</data>
