<node id="Wheat Bran">
  <data key="d0">Wheat Bran</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Wheat bran is a widely utilized dietary substrate and experimental feed, particularly in entomological research involving the rearing of mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) and superworms (*Zophobas atratus*). It is recognized as the conventional and standard food source for these larvae, providing a nutritionally balanced diet rich in protein, carbohydrates, and fatty acids. This composition supports efficient digestion, rapid larval growth, low mortality, and successful development into adulthood, making wheat bran the benchmark feed for maintaining healthy darkling beetle cultures. Its effectiveness as a baseline diet has been confirmed in multiple studies, which highlight its role in ensuring optimal survival and reproductive outcomes.  

In experimental contexts, wheat bran is frequently employed as a control diet. By serving as the reference standard, it allows researchers to compare larval performance under normal nutritional conditions with outcomes observed when larvae are fed alternative or experimental diets, such as synthetic polymers. This control function is particularly important in studies evaluating growth rates, survival, and life cycle progression, where wheat bran provides the baseline against which dietary effects are measured.  

Beyond its role in insect rearing, wheat bran is central to biodegradation research, especially in investigations of insect-mediated breakdown of plastics such as polystyrene (PS) and micro-polystyrene (PS MPs). When used as a co-feeding material alongside plastics, wheat bran supplies essential nutrients that sustain larval health and stimulate higher levels of plastic ingestion. This co-diet approach has been shown to enhance the overall consumption of plastics by *T. molitor* and *Z. atratus*, thereby facilitating studies on the potential of insects to contribute to plastic waste degradation.  

However, the use of wheat bran in biodegradation experiments also presents methodological challenges. Because it contributes organic matter to larval frass, residual wheat bran can complicate the interpretation of analytical results. For example, during thermogravimetric analysis (TGA), remnants of wheat bran may be misidentified as degraded polymer, potentially leading to overestimation of plastic breakdown. These issues underscore the importance of careful experimental design, rigorous controls, and precise analytical methods when wheat bran is incorporated into feeding trials.  

In summary, wheat bran serves a dual role in insect research: it is both a reliable, nutritionally balanced rearing substrate that ensures optimal larval development and a versatile experimental diet that supports investigations into insect-driven biodegradation of synthetic materials. Its widespread use reflects its effectiveness as a standard feed, while its methodological implications highlight the need for precision and control in experimental applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-02a57c5d6ee92292f1b1bd3dbe76e612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b6629e8c030ab3162553d83aa6eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
