<node id="National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI)">
  <data key="d0">National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">NCBI is a database provider whose Nr protein database was used for gene annotation.&lt;SEP&gt;NCBI is mentioned as the source of the Nr database used for protein comparison in gene annotation.&lt;SEP&gt;NCBI is an institution that maintains GenBank and provides access to biological sequence data.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI), located in Bethesda, MD, created the Basic Local Alignment Search Tool (BLAST) used for sequence alignment.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) is the repository where the partial 16S rRNA sequence of Achromobacter xylosidans M9 was deposited.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI), USA, created the BLAST tool used for aligning the obtained sequences.&lt;SEP&gt;The National Center for Biotechnology Information provided the nucleotide database used for BLASTN homology search to identify bacterial strains.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5e9eb740edf53e540b468122b302cb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f545e57b1a2b3da8601b4d23e1260c94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3196d2d200ebf060e966a565b5eb26de</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
