<node id="Starvation Control">
  <data key="d0">Starvation Control</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Starvation control refers to the experimental group of worms that received no diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Starvation control refers to the group of mealworms deprived of food, used as a baseline for mortality and weight comparisons.&lt;SEP&gt;Starvation control refers to mealworms that were unfed during the experiment to serve as a control group.&lt;SEP&gt;Starvation control refers to the experimental group of mealworms deprived of food, used as a baseline for survival comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;Starvation control refers to mealworms deprived of food, used as a baseline to compare survival and mortality against MPS-fed groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Starvation control refers to the experimental group of mealworms deprived of food, used as a comparison to evaluate the effects of microplastic feeding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
