<node id="HT-GPC">
  <data key="d0">HT-GPC</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">HT-GPC is the method used to quantify molecular weight of LDPE.&lt;SEP&gt;HT-GPC refers to high-temperature gel permeation chromatography.&lt;SEP&gt;HT-GPC (High-Temperature Gel Permeation Chromatography) is a method used to determine molecular weights of residual polymers in frass compared to virgin polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;HT-GPC (High-Temperature Gel Permeation Chromatography) was used to analyze residual polymers in frass samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723</data>
