  <data key="d2">GPC analysis was used to measure molecular weight changes in plastics during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC (Gel Permeation Chromatography) analysis was used to measure molecular weight changes in PET polymers after biodegradation by T. molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis (Gel Permeation Chromatography) provides information on depolymerization and degradation of plastic materials by measuring molecular weights and distributions.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis was performed on frass samples to evaluate molecular weight changes.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis (Gel Permeation Chromatography) was used to determine the extent of depolymerization and biodegradation of mask layers.</data>
