<node id="Crystallinity">
  <data key="d0">Crystallinity</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystallinity is a structural property of plastics that negatively affects their consumption and degradability by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallinity refers to the degree of structural order in PET polymers, influencing degradation rates in larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallinity is a structural property of HDPE that was reduced during biodegradation by strain PELW2042.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallinity refers to the degree of long-range order in a polymer material. Higher crystallinity increases hardness and density, making biodegradation more difficult.</data>
