<node id="Pupation">
  <data key="d0">Pupation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pupation refers to the developmental process of larvae transforming into pupae, which was affected by plastic feeding in the experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;Pupation was used as an indicator of larval health and development under different diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Pupation refers to the transformation stage of larvae into pupae, observed in the study under different diet conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Pupation is a developmental stage in the life cycle of superworms and yellow mealworms, used as an indicator of larval health and development. The experiment measured pupation rates under different diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Pupation is the developmental process in T. molitor when larvae transform into pupae, triggered by reaching an energy threshold.&lt;SEP&gt;Pupation refers to the process of larvae transforming into pupae, observed in control and supplemented diet groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38f2f3673b813b3a817c014229c9565</data>
