<node id="G. mellonella">
  <data key="d0">G. mellonella</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">G. mellonella larvae were studied for their gut microbiota activity when fed on beeswax, showing gene expression changes related to wax degradation and fatty acid metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;G. mellonella larvae are mentioned as being associated with LDPE and PS biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae are referenced as organisms in which PS metabolism occurs, involving enzymes such as CYP4/6.&lt;SEP&gt;G. mellonella is an insect species mentioned in the context of plastic biodegradation, particularly PE, PS, and PVC.&lt;SEP&gt;G. mellonella is a species of larvae used in the feeding tests, reared on beeswax or Styrofoam.&lt;SEP&gt;G. mellonella refers to larvae species mentioned as capable of LDPE biodegradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c310f4f7adc3c5b8340e973a5af45e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee</data>
