<node id="Fatty Acids">
  <data key="d0">Fatty Acids</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Fatty acids are metabolites of CES catalytic reactions that can inhibit CES in humans and were produced in higher amounts in PS-fed mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Fatty acids are biomass components in which 13C incorporation can be measured during biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Fatty acids showed variation in levels during PS biodegradation, suggesting metabolic stress in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;A nutritional component analyzed in prior studies of mealworms, absent in plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Fatty acids were analyzed in Tenebrio molitor larvae to assess nutritional composition under different feeding conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Fatty acids are measured in larvae and excrement, with their profiles influenced by different feeds such as potatoes, whey, and polystyrene.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
