<node id="Styrene">
  <data key="d0">Styrene</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Styrene is an organic chemical compound that serves as the fundamental monomer of polystyrene (PS), one of the most widely produced plastics. It plays a dual role in the life cycle of PS: it is the essential building block during polymer synthesis and also the principal decomposition product when PS undergoes thermal, chemical, or biological degradation. In thermal degradation processes, such as those studied using thermogravimetric Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy (TG-FTIR), styrene consistently emerges as the dominant volatile product, including from materials like Styrofoam.  

In biological and ecological contexts, styrene has been identified as a key intermediate in the microbial and insect-mediated breakdown of polystyrene. Studies involving insects such as Tenebrio molitor (mealworms) and superworms have detected styrene in frass samples when the insects were fed PS, though its presence varies depending on species, diet, and experimental conditions. In some cases, styrene was found in control PS materials but not in insect frass or carcasses, indicating that its accumulation and further degradation are context-dependent. Within microbial systems, styrene degradation pathways have been reconstructed and analyzed, with styrene monooxygenase identified as the first enzyme initiating its breakdown. Microorganisms such as Pseudomonas species can transform styrene into phenylacetate, which is further metabolized into phenylacetyl-CoA and subsequently funneled into the tricarboxylic acid (TCA) cycle, ultimately leading to complete mineralization into carbon dioxide (CO₂) and water (H₂O). Styrene can also undergo oxidation to form acetophenone, highlighting its role as a transitional compound in diverse metabolic routes.  

Beyond its role as a chemical intermediate, styrene has been noted for potential biological effects, including bacteriostatic activity that may influence microbial communities, such as gut microbiota in insects involved in plastic degradation. This dual significance—as both a metabolic substrate and a biologically active compound—makes styrene an important focus in environmental and ecological studies of plastic persistence and biodegradation.  

Styrene is also widely used in laboratory and industrial applications. High-purity styrene (≥99%) is commercially available from suppliers such as Sigma Aldrich and is frequently employed as a standard in analytical studies for quantifying monomers and oligomers. Its availability and well-characterized properties make it a valuable reference compound in research on polymer chemistry, degradation mechanisms, and biotechnological applications.  

Overall, styrene is a pivotal compound in the environmental and industrial context of polystyrene. It is the indispensable monomer for PS synthesis, the major decomposition product during thermal and chemical breakdown, and a measurable intermediate in microbial and insect-driven biodegradation pathways. Its transformations, whether through abiotic or biological processes, provide critical insights into the persistence, recyclability, and potential biotechnological utilization of polystyrene in environmental systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-57edc76f6646a41c4845d94baa519950&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5134944e002326fa5ca136c470d99e2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3815960770483b9c0a1579ca8442e3a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de9904e6f38706256e15c7957f8f0527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7432cb0d6c74fd2dd80b065fbad26b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf</data>
