<node id="KEGG">
  <data key="d0">KEGG</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">KEGG stands for Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes.&lt;SEP&gt;KEGG is a pathway database used for enrichment analysis of DEGs in response to PS and CS.&lt;SEP&gt;KEGG is referenced as the source of pathway analysis for styrene degradation in the PS-fed group.&lt;SEP&gt;KEGG is a database used for pathway definition and enrichment analysis in the study of PET-fed larvae microbiomes.&lt;SEP&gt;KEGG (Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes) is a database used for pathway enrichment analysis to identify significantly enriched pathways in PET-fed groups.&lt;SEP&gt;KEGG is a mapping and classification system used to analyze metabolic pathways, identifying upregulated metabolites and enriched pathways in PET-fed larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
