<node id="W.-M. Wu">
  <data key="d0">W.-M. Wu</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">W.-M. Wu is a researcher affiliated with Stanford University who has made significant contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly through investigations involving insect larvae such as mealworms and superworms. Wu is recognized as an author and co-author of multiple scientific publications that focus on the biodegradation and mineralization of plastics, including polystyrene, by these organisms. His work has advanced understanding of how insect larvae can consume and break down synthetic polymers, offering potential solutions for plastic waste management.  

In addition to authoring numerous referenced articles on this subject, W.-M. Wu has also contributed to bibliometric analyses of biodegradation research, highlighting trends and developments in the field. He played a key role in organizing and supervising a worldwide survey on mealworm plastic consumption, underscoring his leadership in coordinating international research efforts. Wu is frequently listed as a corresponding author, with contact information provided through Stanford University, further emphasizing his central role in this area of study.  

Overall, W.-M. Wu is recognized as a leading figure in the scientific exploration of plastic biodegradation by insect larvae, with his research widely cited and referenced in the academic community.&lt;SEP&gt;W.-M. Wu is an author of multiple studies on biodegradation of polystyrene in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of a study on biodegradation of polyethylene and plastic mixtures in mealworms and effects on the gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;W.-M. Wu is an author of a study on biochar generation using frass of yellow mealworms fed with wheat straw.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-908b8bfa7e446694958cf9bd0cfbc583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57e056cd3b06b37d22117fc75e3a4df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44e006d8af33633a06dac6789334329d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278</data>
