<node id="Klebsiella oxytoca NBRC 102593">
  <data key="d0">Klebsiella oxytoca NBRC 102593</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Klebsiella oxytoca NBRC 102593 is a specific bacterial strain of *Klebsiella oxytoca* that has been identified and confirmed through molecular techniques, particularly polymerase chain reaction (PCR) and 16S ribosomal RNA (rRNA) gene sequencing. The strain was characterized by amplification of the 16S rRNA gene using NBRC-specific primers, yielding a product size of 247 base pairs. This molecular confirmation demonstrated a high degree of similarity, with 99.77% sequence identity, to isolates obtained from the gut microbiota of *Tenebrio molitor* (mealworm beetle).  

The strain was originally isolated as part of studies investigating the microbial community within the gut of *T. molitor*, where it was identified as isolate number 5. Its presence in this environment has been linked to potential roles in polystyrene biodegradation, suggesting that *Klebsiella oxytoca* NBRC 102593 may contribute to the breakdown of synthetic polymers within the insect gut. In addition to its ecological significance, the strain has been used for designing primers targeting the 16S rRNA gene, further supporting its role as a reference organism in microbial identification and genetic analysis.  

Overall, *Klebsiella oxytoca* NBRC 102593 is a well-characterized bacterial strain confirmed through PCR and 16S rRNA sequencing, isolated from the gut of *Tenebrio molitor*, and notable for its potential involvement in polystyrene degradation as well as its utility in molecular microbiology research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de</data>
