</node>
<node id="Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182">
  <data key="d0">Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182 is a well-characterized bacterial strain of the species *Klebsiella oxytoca*, confirmed through molecular techniques such as PCR amplification and 16S ribosomal RNA gene sequencing. The strain has been used in genetic studies, including the design of primers targeting the 16S rRNA gene, where amplification with ATCC-specific primers produced a product size of 337 base pairs. It has also been reported to successfully amplify the alkB gene, further supporting its molecular identification and characterization.  

This strain is notable for its ecological and applied significance. Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182 has been isolated from the gut of *Tenebrio molitor* (mealworm larvae), where it has been identified with 87.70% similarity among gut microbial isolates. Its presence in this environment is particularly important because it has been associated with the biodegradation of polystyrene, a persistent plastic pollutant. The strain’s ability to contribute to polystyrene degradation highlights its potential role in bioremediation and microbial ecology research.  

Overall, Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182 is a reference strain that serves both as a genetic resource for molecular studies and as a biologically relevant isolate with demonstrated potential in plastic biodegradation, particularly within the insect gut microbiome of *Tenebrio molitor*.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de</data>
