<node id="BLAST">
  <data key="d0">BLAST</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">BLAST is the sequence alignment tool used to compare the FASTA sequence against nucleotide sequences in NCBI GenBank.&lt;SEP&gt;BLAST is a sequence similarity search tool used to identify strains against the NCBI 16s rRNA database.&lt;SEP&gt;The Basic Local Alignment Search Tool (BLAST) is a database search tool used to compare nucleotide or protein sequences.&lt;SEP&gt;BLAST is referenced as a bioinformatics tool used for sequence search and clustering, against which faster methods were compared.&lt;SEP&gt;BLAST is a bioinformatics tool used to search and compare cox1 sequences of the lesser waxworm for genetic similarities.&lt;SEP&gt;BLAST is a sequence alignment tool created by the National Center for Biotechnology Information, USA, used to compare obtained sequences with organisms in the GenBank database.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e9eb740edf53e540b468122b302cb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99a98d885ec6495c4dc902866c4ab9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582</data>
