</node>
<node id="Sample 3">
  <data key="d0">Sample 3</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Sample 3 refers to one of the Klebsiella oxytoca colonies, described as whitish and the largest among the three isolates.&lt;SEP&gt;Sample 3 is the Klebsiella oxytoca strain identified as ATCC 13182, which successfully amplified the alkB gene.&lt;SEP&gt;Sample 3 showed the presence of the alkB gene with a band at 550 bp in gel electrophoresis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199</data>
