  <data key="d5">1756372040</data>
</node>
<node id="Touchdown PCR">
  <data key="d0">Touchdown PCR</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A PCR method applied to amplify the alkB gene due to degenerate bases in primer sequences.&lt;SEP&gt;Touchdown PCR was used to amplify genomic DNA extracted from larvae gut samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b964b1825429cad2c7d13c1ea8827e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756379490</data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 6">
  <data key="d0">Figure 6</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 6 presents the constructed phylogenetic tree and gel results showing amplification of the alkB gene.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure referenced in the study showing correlations between dominant bacteria and differential metabolites.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 6 shows the life cycle of Tenebrio molitor, where pupae collected from the three groups eventually turned into beetles.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 6 shows surfaces of cement mortar glued to EPS after larvae consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 6 shows the non-metrical multidimensional scaling (NMDs) of the gut microbial community for PU and bran diets at different sampling times.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 6 presents a phylogenetic tree of Lac640 protein, SDS-PAGE analysis, enzyme activity, kinetic analysis, FTIR spectra, and surface morphology of PS/CS treated with or without Lac640 enzyme.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 6 presents a global overview summary of positive and negative CCM correlations with various plastic substrates, including those with molasses supplement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756380876</data>
</node>
<node id="Polystyrene emulsion">
  <data key="d0">Polystyrene emulsion</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Polystyrene emulsion was used as the only carbon source in culturing gut microorganisms from Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene emulsion was prepared from EPS dissolved in dichloromethane and used for microbial degradation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene emulsion is a prepared solution used as the sole carbon source for microbial degradation experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bf67bf1b585ce1050569a2eb0000cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e</data>
