</node>
<node id="Gut microorganisms">
  <data key="d0">Gut microorganisms</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Microorganisms isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor that are capable of feeding on polystyrene and aiding in its degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Microorganisms in the gut of mealworms that play a role in polystyrene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microorganisms are studied in relation to their role in the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene by plastic-eating mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of microorganisms found in insect larvae guts, some of which are associated with PS biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Microorganisms in mealworms' digestive systems that play a role in polystyrene biodegradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db0003a7244c51697d0129eb84b8e28e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0</data>
