</node>
<node id="Homeostasis">
  <data key="d0">Homeostasis</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Homeostasis is mentioned as a biological function disrupted by endocrine-disrupting chemicals.&lt;SEP&gt;Homeostasis is the stable internal environment provided by the host, which supports symbiotic microorganisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Homeostasis refers to the self-regulating process in insects that influences mitochondrial activity and mineral balance under nutritional stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Homeostasis was mentioned as a biochemical process affected in mealworm larvae during PS biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Homeostasis refers to the physiological balance in mealworms, which is disrupted by toxic byproducts of PVC depolymerization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7734a37a076c4f934de059042daf10cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
