<node id="Hermetia illucens">
  <data key="d0">Hermetia illucens</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Hermetia illucens, also known as black soldier fly larvae, is studied as an insect larval meal for broiler chickens.&lt;SEP&gt;An edible insect species studied for nitrogen-protein conversion factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Hermetia illucens, also known as the black soldier fly, is studied for its potential use in entomoremediation and as a nutritional source.&lt;SEP&gt;Hermetia illucens is the scientific name of the Black Soldier Fly (BSF).&lt;SEP&gt;An edible insect species studied for nitrogen-to-protein conversion factors and recovery of proteins.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
