<node id="Mice">
  <data key="d0">Mice</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mice were used in a study on gender dimorphism in differential peripheral blood leukocyte counts.&lt;SEP&gt;Mice were used in studies where T. molitor was added to their diet, resulting in growth of beneficial intestinal bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Mice were used in a study where exposure to polystyrene microplastics altered gut microflora gene expression, especially fat and lipid metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Mice are referenced as organisms that can suffer biological toxicity and inflammatory responses from long-term exposure to microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Animal model used in a study to test reproductive toxicity caused by polystyrene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Mice are mentioned as another species where metabolic pathways involved in oxidative stress defense have been studied.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6c2706bd609f920aa61d5ef2310db6</data>
