<node id="Zhang Y">
  <data key="d0">Zhang Y</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zhang Y is a researcher recognized for extensive contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly focusing on insect-mediated processes. Zhang Y is the author of a 2019 study that investigated the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms (Tenebrio molitor larvae), a line of research that has been foundational in demonstrating the potential of insect larvae to break down synthetic polymers. Beyond this, Zhang Y has co-authored studies examining the biodegradation of polyvinyl chloride (PVC) in Tenebrio molitor larvae, further expanding the scope of plastic types shown to be susceptible to biological degradation.  

In addition to work with mealworms, Zhang Y has also conducted research on biodegradation processes involving superworms (Zophobas atratus larvae), highlighting the broader applicability of insect-based systems for plastic degradation. Zhang Y’s studies consistently emphasize the role of insect gut microbiota and enzymatic activity in facilitating the breakdown of otherwise persistent plastics.  

Complementing this insect-focused research, Zhang Y has also contributed to the identification and characterization of plastic-degrading microorganisms. Notably, Zhang Y is an author of a study reporting the isolation of a polystyrene-degrading Acinetobacter bacterium from the gut of Tribolium castaneum larvae, underscoring the microbial dimension of plastic biodegradation and its potential for biotechnological applications.  

Overall, Zhang Y’s body of work spans multiple plastic types, including polystyrene and PVC, and multiple biological systems, including mealworms, superworms, and associated microbial communities. This research collectively advances understanding of biological plastic degradation and highlights potential pathways for developing sustainable solutions to plastic waste management.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45bee9c7111e3b95e966d23c3a6223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6464a2f3ca18442f70e254b9341a3e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa884bb7540491e8ab975e29c46d1f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fe36521680f0d09a603eab04706561</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386034</data>
</node>
