<node id="Sci Total Environ">
  <data key="d0">Sci Total Environ</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Science of the Total Environment (abbreviated as *Sci Total Environ*) is a peer-reviewed scientific journal that publishes interdisciplinary research addressing environmental science and its interactions with human health, ecosystems, and technology. The journal serves as a platform for studies that explore pollution, ecological impacts, and innovative approaches to environmental sustainability.  

Over the years, *Sci Total Environ* has published a wide range of influential studies. In 1997, it featured research on reproductive health in humans and wildlife, highlighting early concerns about environmental contaminants and their biological effects. More recently, the journal has become a key outlet for studies on microplastics and biodegradation. For example, it has published investigations into the presence of microplastics in human food chains, the role of microorganisms in microplastics degradation (2022), and the combined effects of mulch film-derived microplastics and atrazine on earthworms.  

The journal has also been central to advancing knowledge on biological and microbial solutions for plastic waste management. It has published studies on the biodegradation of polypropylene by mealworms and superworms (2021), the biodegradative capacity of *Tenebrio molitor* larvae on vulcanized styrene-butadiene rubber (SBR) and tire crumb, and the ability of land snails to degrade polystyrene. Research on the marine fungus *Zalerion maritimum* and its potential role in plastic degradation has also appeared in its pages.  

Beyond plastics, *Sci Total Environ* has disseminated work on environmental technologies, such as a 2021 study on microbial electrolysis cells, and on pollutant interactions, including the adsorption of oxytetracycline on microplastics.  

Overall, *Science of the Total Environment* is recognized as a leading journal for comprehensive environmental research, bridging studies on pollution, ecological health, biodegradation, and sustainable technological innovations. Its broad scope and interdisciplinary focus make it a critical resource for scientists, policymakers, and practitioners addressing global environmental challenges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb491e686c96e54f8ea43a9f1ba97eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933de951613fc7eadfd14dde9bd18b2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6464a2f3ca18442f70e254b9341a3e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387439</data>
</node>
