<node id="Jiang L">
  <data key="d0">Jiang L</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Jiang L is a researcher and author recognized for contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly focusing on the role of insects such as mealworms and waxworms in breaking down synthetic polymers. Jiang L has co-authored multiple scientific studies investigating the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene, a widely used plastic, by mealworms. This body of work includes a notable 2015 study that provided evidence of mealworms’ ability to consume and metabolize polystyrene, leading to its partial mineralization. In addition to research on mealworms, Jiang L has also contributed to studies examining the biodegradation of plastics by waxworms, further expanding the understanding of insect-mediated plastic degradation. Collectively, Jiang L’s research has advanced knowledge in the field of environmental biotechnology and waste management by highlighting biological pathways for mitigating plastic pollution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-38a07d29ecfa06f82d97e69f5cd2c801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386046</data>
</node>
