  <data key="d2">Environmental estrogens were studied for their health implications in humans.&lt;SEP&gt;Humans are affected by ingestion of chemicals and microplastics, which can accumulate in the body and harm cells and tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Humans are indirectly mentioned as potentially affected by contamination of insect feed with plastic, since mealworms are an accepted food source for animals.&lt;SEP&gt;Humans are indirectly exposed to plastics through consumption of seafood and other means, making plastic pollution a human health problem.</data>
