<node id="Enterobacter asburiae YTI">
  <data key="d0">Enterobacter asburiae YTI</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Enterobacter asburiae YTI is a bacterial strain found in the gut of waxworms, capable of degrading polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae YTI is a bacterial strain that degraded about 6.5% of commercial LDPE film with a Mw of 88.2 kDa in more than two months.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef</data>
