  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Polylactide (PLA) is a type of plastic waste that some insects have been confirmed to degrade.&lt;SEP&gt;Polylactide (PLA) is a type of bioplastic capable of degradation under natural conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Polylactide is a biodegradable thermoplastic polyester derived from renewable resources such as corn, tapioca starch, or sugarcane, tested in the study.</data>
