<node id="Plastic pollution">
  <data key="d0">Plastic pollution</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Plastic pollution is the environmental problem caused by accumulation of plastic waste in ecosystems such as rivers, lakes, and oceans.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution is described as one of the biggest environmental concerns, alongside climate change and air quality.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution is the environmental issue caused by the accumulation of plastic debris, including polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the accumulation of plastics in ecosystems, leading to environmental and public health issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution is described as a significant environmental crisis caused by the widespread use and disposal of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to environmental contamination caused by plastic waste, including water and soil pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the environmental issue addressed by the study, focusing on PS and MPs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c6c5d405260e0a6f512a9504195dc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9</data>
