  <data key="d0">Mealworms (T. molitor)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mealworms (T. molitor) are insects studied for their nutrient composition when fed Styrofoam compared to a conventional diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms, the larvae of the T. molitor beetle, were used in the experiment to test the effects of feeding on EPS, XPS, and standard diet. Their survival, growth, development, and fecundity were measured.</data>
