<node id="One-way ANOVA">
  <data key="d0">One-way ANOVA</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">One-way ANOVA is a statistical test employed to evaluate differences among the means of three or more independent groups. In the referenced studies, One-way ANOVA was applied across a variety of contexts to determine whether observed variations between groups were statistically significant. Specifically, it was used in questionnaire analyses to assess differences related to gender and prior experience with eating insects. It was also applied in experimental research to analyze nutritional parameters, such as protein, sugar, and lipid content, in mealworms fed with different polystyrene (PS) species, thereby identifying whether diet influenced biochemical composition. Additionally, One-way ANOVA was utilized for multiple comparisons across co-diet groups, allowing researchers to test for significant differences when more than two dietary treatments were involved. In some cases, the method was used for pairwise analysis of data, highlighting its role in comparing group means systematically. Furthermore, One-way ANOVA was employed to test alpha diversity differences between diet groups, where results indicated no significant variation. Across these applications, statistical significance was denoted using conventional markers such as * and **. Overall, One-way ANOVA served as a central analytical tool for examining group-level differences in both biological and behavioral research contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;One-way ANOVA was used for statistical analysis of experimental data.&lt;SEP&gt;One-way ANOVA was used to analyze survival rates of mealworms under different treatments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e9eb740edf53e540b468122b302cb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c810740a381d4d9e829e28c01e62564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385994</data>
</node>
