<node id="Kosewska, O.">
  <data key="d0">Kosewska, O.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Kosewska, O. is a researcher and author whose work focuses on innovative biological approaches to waste management, particularly through the use of insects in the biodegradation of plastics and other materials. She has contributed to multiple studies investigating the potential of *Tenebrio molitor* (mealworm) larvae as agents for recycling and biodegradation. Her research explores the gut microbiome and enzymatic activity of these larvae when exposed to various waste substrates, including cellulose, polyethylene, and polystyrene.  

In a series of studies, including work published in 2019 and 2020, Kosewska, O. examined how the gut microbial community structure and enzymatic profiles of *Tenebrio molitor* larvae adapt during the biodegradation of different types of plastic waste. These studies provided insights into the biological mechanisms underlying the larvae’s ability to process synthetic polymers, highlighting the role of microbial symbionts and digestive enzymes in breaking down otherwise persistent materials.  

Additionally, Kosewska, O. has investigated alternative methods of recycling foamed polystyrene using insects, emphasizing the potential of insect-based biodegradation as a sustainable solution to plastic pollution. Her research contributes to the growing body of evidence that insect larvae, particularly mealworms, can serve as a biological tool for reducing plastic waste and recovering value from materials that are otherwise difficult to recycle.  

Through her authorship and co-authorship of these studies, Kosewska, O. has advanced scientific understanding of insect-mediated biodegradation processes, with a focus on the interplay between insect physiology, gut microbiota, and enzymatic activity in the context of environmental sustainability and waste recycling.&lt;SEP&gt;Kosewska, O. is an author of a study on gut microbiome and enzymatic profile of Tenebrio molitor larvae biodegrading cellulose, polyethylene, and polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of a study on gut microbiome and enzymatic profile of Tenebrio molitor larvae biodegrading waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Kosewska, O. is a co-author of research on gut microbiome and enzymatic profiles of Tenebrio molitor larvae degrading plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author in a study on gut microbiome and enzymatic profile of Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Kosewska, O. is an author of a study on gut microbiome and enzymatic profile of Tenebrio molitor larvae biodegrading waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af93e805daf3987d95ff99ab8e891d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f</data>
