<node id="Tenebrio molitor (Yellow Mealworm)">
  <data key="d0">Tenebrio molitor (Yellow Mealworm)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">An insect species studied for toxicity evaluation and as an environmentally friendly insect.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor, also known as the yellow mealworm, is an insect larva studied for its ability to biodegrade polystyrene (PS). It depolymerizes PS strongly by destroying the benzene ring.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor is a species of darkling beetle larvae capable of biodegrading plastics such as PS, LDPE, PVC, PP, and PLA.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568</data>
