</node>
<node id="Alphitobius diaperinus">
  <data key="d0">Alphitobius diaperinus</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">An edible insect species studied for nitrogen-protein conversion factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Alphitobius diaperinus is an insect species studied in relation to starvation and carbohydrate levels depending on temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;The beetle species studied for bacterial and fungal diversity in polystyrene-fed conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;An edible insect species studied for nitrogen-to-protein conversion factors and nutritional value.&lt;SEP&gt;Alphitobius diaperinus, also known as the lesser mealworm, is an insect species capable of feeding on and degrading polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Alphitobius diaperinus, also known as the lesser mealworm, is a pest of stored food grain products and has been shown to feed on and degrade polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Alphitobius diaperinus, also referred to as the lesser mealworm, was studied for survival rate and its ability to degrade polystyrene (PS).</data>
