<node id="Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor larvae)">
  <data key="d0">Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor larvae)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mealworms, specifically larvae of Tenebrio molitor, were the experimental organisms used to study microplastic consumption and degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Organisms whose gut microbiome was studied for responses to polystyrene and corn straw diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms, specifically Tenebrio molitor larvae, are studied for their gut microbiome and ability to biodegrade polystyrene and other materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms are macroinvertebrates studied for their ability to biodegrade polystyrene (PS) and polyethylene (PE) foams.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms, specifically Tenebrio molitor larvae, were used in the study to ingest and degrade PS and LDPE foams.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387070</data>
</node>
<node id="Rigid micro-PS (MPS)">
  <data key="d0">Rigid micro-PS (MPS)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Rigid micro-PS (MPS) is a type of microplastic material with specific density and hardness, used in experiments to study mealworm consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756372631</data>
