  <data key="d0">Residual Polymer</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Residual polymer refers to the incompletely digested MPS egested by mealworms, analyzed for molecular weight changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Residual polymer refers to undegraded polymer content in frass, extracted using solvents for analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Residual polymer is the remaining polymer extracted from frass after digestion by mealworms, analyzed for molecular weight and degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Residual polymer refers to the remaining plastic material after being processed in the gut of mealworms, analyzed for depolymerization and chemical modifications.</data>
