  <data key="d2">Feedstock refers to the original MPS material used as a baseline for comparison with residual polymer after digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedstock refers to the PS material provided to mealworms as a diet input, with different variations (A, B, C) used in the experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Feedstock is another intended end product of organic waste processing, which can be negatively impacted by plastic contamination.</data>
