</node>
<node id="Ji-Wei Pang">
  <data key="d0">Ji-Wei Pang</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ji-Wei Pang is a researcher affiliated with CECEP Digital Technology Co., Ltd., part of the China Energy Conservation and Environmental Protection Group in Beijing, China. He has contributed as an author to several scientific studies focused on the biodegradation of plastics, particularly investigating the role of Tenebrio molitor larvae (commonly known as mealworms) in breaking down synthetic polymers. His work includes research on the biodegradation of polyethylene terephthalate (PET) as well as studies examining how the molecular weight and other material properties of plastics, such as polyethylene, influence their degradation by mealworms. Within these studies, Ji-Wei Pang played a role in developing and contributing to the research methodology, supporting the design and execution of experiments that explore sustainable approaches to plastic waste management. Through his contributions, he has advanced understanding of insect-mediated plastic degradation and its potential applications in environmental protection and waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Ji-Wei Pang is listed as one of the authors of the study on biodegradation of low-density polyethylene in mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386459</data>
</node>
<node id="De-Feng Xing">
  <data key="d0">De-Feng Xing</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">De-Feng Xing is one of the authors of the study on PET biodegradation in Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;De-Feng Xing contributed to conceptualization and experimental design.&lt;SEP&gt;De-Feng Xing is one of the authors of the study on PET biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;De-Feng Xing is one of the authors of the research article, affiliated with Harbin Institute of Technology.&lt;SEP&gt;De-Feng Xing contributed to methodology in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Author of the study on impacts of polyethylene properties on biodegradation in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;De-Feng Xing is listed as one of the authors of the study on biodegradation of low-density polyethylene in mealworms.</data>
