<node id="Journal of Hazardous Materials">
  <data key="d0">Journal of Hazardous Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The **Journal of Hazardous Materials** is a peer-reviewed scientific journal that publishes research on topics related to hazardous substances, environmental contaminants, and their impacts, as well as strategies for their management, mitigation, and remediation. It serves as a platform for studies addressing the environmental and health risks associated with hazardous materials, including plastics and microplastics. The journal has featured a wide range of research articles and reviews, such as investigations into the biodegradation of synthetic polymers and plastics by biological organisms. Notable examples include studies on the biodegradation of polyethylene terephthalate (PET) and polylactic acid (PLA) by *Tenebrio molitor* larvae (commonly known as mealworms), microbial degradation of high-impact polystyrene, and the breakdown of polystyrene microplastics. Additionally, the journal has published critical reviews on the occurrence, behavior, and risks of microplastics in soil and groundwater environments. Through such publications, the Journal of Hazardous Materials contributes significantly to advancing scientific understanding of plastic pollution, biodegradation processes, and broader environmental hazards.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal of Hazardous Materials is a scientific journal referenced in the text, publishing research on nanoplastics, their environmental fate, toxicity, and risk management strategies.</data>
