<node id="Shenzhen">
  <data key="d0">Shenzhen</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">Shenzhen is a major city located in Guangdong Province, China, recognized both as an academic hub and as a site for scientific research on plastic degradation. It is home to the Harbin Institute of Technology (Shenzhen), a prominent institution contributing to advanced studies in engineering and environmental sciences. The city has also played a significant role in experimental research involving mealworms (Tenebrio molitor larvae) and their capacity to degrade and metabolize various plastics.  

In Shenzhen, multiple studies have been conducted to evaluate the ability of mealworms to ingest and break down different types of plastics, including polystyrene (PS), polyethylene (PE), low-density polyethylene (LDPE), and polyvinyl chloride (PVC). Research carried out in the region demonstrated that mealworm larvae collected locally were able to consume and metabolize these plastics, with one experiment reporting a 29.7% loss of polyethylene after feeding trials. Investigations in Shenzhen also examined the rates of plastic consumption, the metabolic pathways involved, and the potential for mealworms to process microplastics, highlighting their role as a biological model for plastic degradation.  

Overall, Shenzhen serves as both an educational center and a research site where pioneering studies on insect-mediated plastic degradation have been conducted, contributing valuable insights into sustainable approaches for addressing plastic pollution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c651f9305c4265540ed7deeb891eae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f4db8df75799fa6a0a07921158cf0</data>
