<node id="Microplastics and Nanoplastics">
  <data key="d0">Microplastics and Nanoplastics</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Microplastics and nanoplastics are formed from improper disposal and weathering of plastics, accumulating in the environment and causing toxic effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental contaminants largely comprised of polyethylene, resistant to biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastics and nanoplastics are environmental contaminants largely comprised of PE.</data>
