  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Recycling of PET into bottles, fibers, films, and sheets is mentioned as a countermeasure, though currently limited to 28.4%.&lt;SEP&gt;Recycling is a method of managing plastic waste by reusing materials to reduce pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Recycling is mentioned as a conventional method to tackle plastic pollution, though considered insufficient.&lt;SEP&gt;A conventional method mentioned in the text for tackling plastic pollution, though considered insufficient.&lt;SEP&gt;Recycling is one of the methods used for disposal of waste plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Recycling is a method of reprocessing plastic waste, though only about 9% of plastics are recycled.&lt;SEP&gt;Recycling, including bio-recycling, is mentioned as a critical sustainability practice.</data>
