<node id="Spiroplasma sp.">
  <data key="d0">Spiroplasma sp.</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Spiroplasma sp. is a bacterial genus commonly identified as a dominant member of the gut microbiota in *Tenebrio molitor* (mealworm) larvae. It has been consistently observed across different dietary conditions, including control groups and larvae fed on synthetic polymers such as polyethylene terephthalate (PET) and low-density polyethylene (LDPE), as well as natural substrates like polypropylene (PP) and lignocellulose. Within these contexts, Spiroplasma sp. has been associated with processes of plastic and lignocellulosic material biodegradation, suggesting a potential role in the microbial mechanisms that enable mealworms to metabolize otherwise recalcitrant substrates.  

Although Spiroplasma sp. is generally regarded in entomological research as a pathogenic or male-killing bacterium in insects, this pathogenic effect was not observed in the studies of *T. molitor* larvae where it appeared as a stable and abundant gut symbiont. Instead, it was consistently reported as one of the most prevalent genera in the mealworm gut microbiome, regardless of diet type, indicating its ecological importance in the host’s digestive system.  

Overall, Spiroplasma sp. represents a key bacterial genus in the gut microbiota of *Tenebrio molitor* larvae. It is notable both for its dominance across feeding conditions and for its potential functional contributions to the degradation of plastics and plant-derived polymers, highlighting its dual significance as a common insect-associated bacterium and as a microorganism of interest in biodegradation research.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681a7143730d41e569d0d76a926eb069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386527</data>
</node>
