  <data key="d0">Acinetobacter sp.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A bacterial genus found in PET-fed larvae with 12.28% abundance.&lt;SEP&gt;Acinetobacter sp. is a bacterial species associated with medium molecular weight polypropylene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Acinetobacter sp. was enriched in PP-M-fed larvae and is associated with LDPE and PS biodegradation in T. molitor and G. mellonella.&lt;SEP&gt;Acinetobacter sp. is a bacterial species associated with PS degradation in T. castaneum larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;A bacterial genus strongly associated with PS degradation in the gut microbiome of T. castaneum larvae.</data>
