<node id="Citrobacter sp.">
  <data key="d0">Citrobacter sp.</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Citrobacter sp. is a bacterial genus identified within the gut microbiome of *Tenebrio molitor* (yellow mealworm), particularly in individuals fed on plastic-based diets. It has been consistently associated with the biodegradation of synthetic polymers, most notably polyethylene (PE) and polystyrene (PS). Studies have shown that Citrobacter sp. becomes more abundant in mealworms maintained on plastic-only diets, with one report noting a relative abundance of 5.70% in larvae fed polyethylene terephthalate (PET). This enrichment suggests a strong ecological and functional link between the presence of Citrobacter sp. and the capacity of the mealworm gut microbiome to metabolize and degrade recalcitrant plastic substrates.  

The genus has been highlighted as a key microbial taxon contributing to the breakdown of PE and PS, two of the most widely used and environmentally persistent plastics. Its consistent detection across different studies of plastic-fed mealworms underscores its potential role in facilitating or enhancing plastic degradation processes within the insect gut environment. By associating with both polyethylene and polystyrene degradation, Citrobacter sp. represents an important microbial candidate for understanding the mechanisms of plastic biodegradation and for exploring potential biotechnological applications in plastic waste management.  

In summary, Citrobacter sp. is a bacterial genus within the mealworm gut microbiome that shows significant enrichment under plastic-fed conditions and is strongly linked to the degradation of polyethylene and polystyrene, highlighting its ecological importance and potential utility in bioremediation strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Citrobacter sp. is a bacterial genus associated with PP diets in the gut microbiome of Zophobas atratus larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a</data>
