  <data key="d2">A bacterial genus found in PET-fed larvae with 5.22% abundance, reported as a plastic-degrading genus.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterococcus sp. is a bacterial genus identified as a key microorganism in both PP and lignocellulose degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterococcus sp. is a bacterial strain studied in relation to polystyrene degradation in Tenebrio molitor, Galleria mellonella, and Zophobas atratus.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterococcus sp. is a bacterial genus identified as a majority member of the mealworm gut microbiome across all diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterococcus sp. is a bacterial genus found in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio larvae and strongly associated with LDPE biodegradation.</data>
