<node id="PET (Polyethylene terephthalate)">
  <data key="d0">PET (Polyethylene terephthalate)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PET is a type of plastic studied for biodegradation by larvae and gut microbiota, producing metabolites and degradation products.&lt;SEP&gt;PET is a commercial polyester resin polymer that undergoes biodegradation by Tenebrio molitor larvae and gut microbiota, producing various metabolic intermediates.&lt;SEP&gt;PET (Polyethylene terephthalate) is a plastic material consumed by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;A petroleum-based plastic studied for enzymatic hydrolysis and recycling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e</data>
