<node id="Figure 5">
  <data key="d0">Figure 5</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A figure referenced in the study showing metabolite classification and pathway analysis results.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 5 shows the relative abundance of PS-degrading bacterial species identified by 16S rRNA sequencing.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 5 shows the survival percentage rate of mealworms from three groups: control, polystyrene + carrots, and polystyrene only.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 5 shows specimens at the end of the experiment with white and grey EPS.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 5 illustrates the Shannon diversity index of the gut microbiome of mealworms under PU and bran diets across 3, 10, and 17 days.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 5 illustrates the proposed metabolic pathways of lignocellulose and PS plastic degradation in mealworms, including multiple stages of degradation and enzyme expression levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 5 shows the relative abundance of predominant phyla and genera in the gut of mealworms fed different diets.</data>
