<node id="Lipid metabolism">
  <data key="d0">Lipid metabolism</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipid metabolism pathways, including ether lipid metabolism and glycerophospholipid metabolism, were positively correlated with Dysgonomonas sp. and Hafnia-Obesumbacterium sp. during PET degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipid metabolism pathways of the host larvae were reprogrammed during PET degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;A metabolic pathway upregulated in mice exposed to polystyrene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipid metabolism includes pathways such as FA degradation, FA biosynthesis, FA elongation, steroid biosynthesis, sphingolipid metabolism, glycerolipid metabolism, and cutin, suberine, and wax biosynthesis, all expanded in PET-fed larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6c2706bd609f920aa61d5ef2310db6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22</data>
