</node>
<node id="Craig S. Criddle">
  <data key="d0">Craig S. Criddle</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Craig S. Criddle is a professor in the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at Stanford University, where he is actively engaged in research and academic scholarship. He is recognized as both an author and the corresponding author of a research article investigating the enhanced bioavailability and microbial biodegradation of polystyrene within mealworm gut microbiomes. In this capacity, he contributed not only through authorship but also by providing guidance, support, and critical suggestions that shaped the study. His role reflects his expertise in environmental engineering and his broader commitment to advancing scientific understanding of microbial processes and sustainable waste management. Through his academic position at Stanford University, Craig S. Criddle continues to contribute to research, mentorship, and the development of innovative approaches to environmental challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;Professor at Stanford University who provided suggestions during the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a8b07ee5dc7a7af59a93d03311efe60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16328c3c685f35501c3639525e997d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5338aa2127367c868a3e7331e1f66225</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387697</data>
</node>
