  <data key="d0">Plesiophthalmus davidis</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Plesiophthalmus davidis is a species of darkling beetle larvae mentioned as capable of biodegrading plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;A beetle species whose larvae host gut microbes capable of degrading polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Plesiophthalmus davidis is an insect species mentioned as capable of degrading plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Species of insect larvae within the darkling beetle family found to biodegrade plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Plesiophthalmus davidis is a species of darkling beetle confirmed to biodegrade PS plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Plesiophthalmus davidis is a macroinvertebrate species with plastic-degrading capacities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
