  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Lepidoptera: Pyralidae is the moth family that includes species such as Indian mealmoths and waxworms, which are capable of biodegrading plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;The pyralid moth family is noted for its ability to biodegrade plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Lepidoptera: Pyralidae is a moth family whose members chew and damage plastic packaging materials.</data>
