<node id="Darkling beetles">
  <data key="d0">Darkling beetles</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Darkling beetles are the common name for the Tenebrionidae family, which includes species capable of biodegrading plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Darkling beetles are insects whose gut microbes have been found to degrade plastics such as PS and LDPE.&lt;SEP&gt;Darkling beetles (family Tenebrionidae) are insect pests known to chew and damage plastic packaging materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Darkling beetles (Coleoptera: Tenebrionidae) are insects whose larvae and adults chew, ingest, and damage plastic packaging materials.</data>
