<node id="Gentamicin">
  <data key="d0">Gentamicin</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Gentamicin is an aminoglycoside antibiotic that has been widely employed in both clinical and experimental contexts, with particular importance in research on insect–microbe interactions and plastic biodegradation. In laboratory studies, gentamicin has been used extensively as a suppression agent to inhibit gut microbiota in mealworm larvae, especially *Tenebrio molitor* and *Tenebrio obscurus*. By incorporating gentamicin into the diet of larvae, researchers have been able to selectively suppress or eliminate bacterial activity in the gut, thereby clarifying the microbial contribution to the depolymerization and biodegradation of synthetic polymers.  

Among various antibiotics tested, gentamicin consistently demonstrated the strongest inhibitory effect on gut flora, making it a preferred tool in suppression assays. Its application has shown that gut bacteria play a critical role in the degradation of polystyrene (PS) and expanded polystyrene (EPS, commonly known as Styrofoam). When larvae were treated with gentamicin, their ability to degrade PS and EPS was significantly reduced or completely halted. This outcome provided strong evidence that microbial activity, rather than insect physiology alone, is essential for the breakdown of these plastics. One notable finding was that gentamicin inhibited the growth of *Exiguobacterium* sp. YT2, a bacterial strain associated with EPS degradation, thereby directly impairing the larvae’s capacity to metabolize this material.  

In contrast, gentamicin treatment had a less pronounced effect on the degradation of low-density polyethylene (LDPE) and other polyethylene variants (PE-1 and PE-2). While some reduction in LDPE depolymerization was observed, the suppression was not as complete as with PS and EPS. This suggests that LDPE degradation in mealworms may involve alternative mechanisms, potentially including non-microbial enzymatic pathways or host-driven processes that are less dependent on gut bacteria.  

Gentamicin has also been applied in suppression tests involving polypropylene (PP), where it served a similar role in evaluating microbial contributions to polymer breakdown. Across these studies, gentamicin has consistently functioned as a benchmark antibiotic for distinguishing microbial versus non-microbial pathways of plastic degradation in insect systems.  

Overall, gentamicin is not only a clinically important antibiotic but also a valuable experimental tool in biodegradation research. Its use in mealworm studies has provided critical insights into the ecological and biotechnological potential of insect–microbe symbioses for plastic waste management, highlighting the indispensable role of gut microbiota in the depolymerization of certain synthetic polymers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524</data>
