<node id="Sodium dodecyl sulfate (SDS)">
  <data key="d0">Sodium dodecyl sulfate (SDS)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">SDS is a chemical used in pretreatment to remove biofilm or biomass from plastic surfaces before biodegradation analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium dodecyl sulfate (SDS) is used at 2% concentration to clean plastic samples before WCA analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;SDS is a detergent solution used to wash PE films before weight measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;Sodium dodecyl sulfate (SDS) is a chemical solution used to treat PS films during biodegradation assays.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fca6acde6809ed3c727d7bffdbfd1ada&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5af82472112cbc9e76b1fd1ac6e8c54e</data>
