  <data key="d2">PS MPs (polystyrene microplastics) are used as feedstock in larval diet experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;PS MPs refer to polystyrene microplastics, which caused a remarkable ROS increase in earthworms (Eisenia fetida).&lt;SEP&gt;PS MPs (polystyrene microplastics) are the materials consumed by mealworms in the study, with varying molecular weights (PS-1 to PS-6).&lt;SEP&gt;PS MPs (polystyrene microplastics) are the subject of biodegradation experiments conducted with mealworms.</data>
