<node id="Survival Rate (SR)">
  <data key="d0">Survival Rate (SR)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Survival rate (SR) is a physiological parameter calculated based on the number of live larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Survival rate (SR) is a physiological parameter of larvae, calculated as the percentage of live larvae (including pupae and beetles if found) relative to the initial number of larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Survival rate (SR) was recorded in the biodegradation experiments based on the number of living larvae compared to the initial number.&lt;SEP&gt;Survival rate was measured over one month to compare Styrofoam-fed and bran-fed mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Survival rate (SR) was a measured outcome in the experiment, used to evaluate the effects of PS consumption, nutrition, and temperature on mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Survival rate (SR) is a measured outcome in the experiment, comparing fed and unfed mealworms under different conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Survival Rate (SR) is a measured parameter in the study, used to compare the survival of T. molitor and T. obscurus larvae under different feeding conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2</data>
