<node id="Thermal Gravimetric Analysis (TGA)">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Gravimetric Analysis (TGA)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">TGA is an analytical method used to characterize thermal changes in PS feedstock and frass samples.&lt;SEP&gt;TGA is an analytical method used in the study to assess the thermal properties of degraded polyurethane compared to virgin polyurethane.&lt;SEP&gt;TGA is an analytical method used to study thermal stability and degradation of fecula.&lt;SEP&gt;An analytical method used to study thermal changes and pyrolysis of PS and frass under nitrogen and air atmospheres.&lt;SEP&gt;TGA (TA, Q600, New Castle, DE, USA) was used to analyze thermal changes during conversion of Styrofoam to frass.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384505</data>
</node>
<node id="Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR)">
  <data key="d0">Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">NMR is an analytical method used to characterize chemical changes in the end groups of egested polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;NMR is an analytical method used in previous studies to characterize PS degradation and detect polymer residues.&lt;SEP&gt;1H-NMR (Bruker BioSpin, AVANCE III HD 400, Fällanden, Switzerland) was used to characterize changes in polymer end groups in frass.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384505</data>
</node>
<node id="PS Feedstock">
  <data key="d0">PS Feedstock</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PS feedstock refers to the polystyrene material provided to larvae as part of their diet and used in analytical tests.&lt;SEP&gt;PS feedstock refers to the original polystyrene foam material used as a control in degradation and ingestion experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;PS feedstock refers to the initial 1.8 g of polystyrene provided to mealworms for consumption and degradation testing.&lt;SEP&gt;PS feedstock refers to the original polystyrene material used as the baseline for comparison in degradation and depolymerization studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a</data>
