<node id="Mn">
  <data key="d0">Mn</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mn is a scientific term with dual significance, depending on the disciplinary context in which it is applied. In polymer science, Mn denotes the **number-average molecular weight**, a fundamental parameter used to characterize polymers and evaluate their structural integrity. This value is typically determined through gel permeation chromatography (GPC) and provides insight into the distribution of polymer chain lengths. Monitoring Mn is essential for assessing polymer degradation, depolymerization, and molecular changes during experimental or environmental processes. For example, Mn has been measured in polystyrene (PS), polyethylene (PE), polyvinyl chloride (PVC), and polyethylene terephthalate (PET) to track alterations in molecular weight during biodegradation studies, including those involving insect larvae such as *Tenebrio molitor*. Reductions in Mn values serve as indicators of polymer breakdown, whether in feedstock materials, frass extracts, or microplastic residues. Thus, Mn functions as a critical analytical variable in evaluating the extent and mechanisms of polymer degradation in both laboratory and environmental contexts.  

In addition to its role in polymer characterization, Mn is also the chemical symbol for the element **manganese**. In this context, manganese has been detected in trace amounts within polymer-related samples, including polystyrene, polyurethane, polyethylene, and frass. Although present only in minor concentrations, the detection of manganese contributes to the broader understanding of elemental composition in polymer degradation studies and environmental analyses.  

Overall, Mn embodies two distinct but complementary scientific meanings: as the number-average molecular weight, it is a central metric for analyzing polymer properties and degradation pathways; as the symbol for manganese, it represents a trace element of interest in material and environmental characterization. The dual usage of Mn underscores the importance of contextual interpretation in scientific research, ensuring clarity when distinguishing between its role as a polymer property and as a chemical element.&lt;SEP&gt;Mn represents the number-average molecular weight of LDPE, which was reduced after larval digestion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e69c793c3b67aed7a68bf864c2c7a309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
