<node id="Mz">
  <data key="d0">Mz</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mz refers to the z-average molecular weight, a parameter commonly used to characterize the molecular size distribution of polymers. In the context of polymer degradation studies, Mz is measured to evaluate the extent of depolymerization or molecular breakdown. It represents a size-averaged molecular weight that provides insight into changes in polymer chain length and structure during biodegradation processes.  

In experimental studies involving different types of plastics, including polystyrene (PS), polyethylene terephthalate (PET), and polyethylene (PE), Mz has been used as a key indicator of degradation. For polystyrene, Mz was observed to decrease in both depolymerization patterns, reflecting a reduction in molecular weight as the polymer chains were broken down. Similarly, in studies where PS residues were digested by larvae, a decrease in Mz was recorded, further confirming molecular degradation. For PET microplastics, Mz was measured to assess the degree of polymer breakdown during biodegradation experiments with *Tenebrio molitor* larvae. Likewise, in the case of PE polymers, Mz was analyzed to monitor molecular changes after biodegradation.  

Overall, Mz serves as an essential analytical measure in polymer science, particularly in biodegradation research. By tracking changes in the z-average molecular weight, researchers can quantify the extent of polymer depolymerization and assess the effectiveness of biological or chemical processes in breaking down synthetic plastics. This makes Mz a critical parameter for understanding polymer stability, environmental persistence, and the potential for biological treatment of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Mz represents the large molecular chains in polymers, which showed little or no breakdown in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Mz is a molecular weight parameter measured in GPC analysis of plastics and frass.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e69c793c3b67aed7a68bf864c2c7a309</data>
