<node id="Fig. 1">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 1</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 1 illustrates multiple aspects of the experiment, including larvae chewing PS foam, survival rates, PS consumption, digestion extent, and molecular weight changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure showing enzymatic activity and PS degradation rates.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure illustrating Tenebrio molitor larvae feeding on plastics and bran, survival rates, weight changes, and physiological responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 1 illustrates the physiological responses of T. molitor and T. obscurus larvae fed with LDPE, HDPE, and LLDPE versus wheat bran, including survival rates, weight changes, and carbonyl index of residual polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 1 refers to the figure showing characterization of nanopolystyrene using multiple analytical techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 1 presents experimental results on survival rates, pupation, and cumulative net weight changes of superworms and yellow mealworms under different diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 1 shows the average mass of larvae after 7, 14, and 21 days of the experiment.</data>
