<node id="Zhuang, G.">
  <data key="d0">Zhuang, G.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zhuang, G. is a researcher recognized for contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly focusing on the role of insects in breaking down synthetic polymers. Zhuang, G. is listed as an author and co-author of multiple studies investigating the biodegradation of expanded polystyrene (EPS) and polyethylene foams, including low-density polyethylene (LDPE), by larvae of *Tenebrio molitor* Linnaeus, commonly known as mealworms. These studies, published between 2020 and 2021, include a notable article in *Chemosphere* (2021) that examined the capacity of *T. molitor* larvae to degrade EPS and polyethylene foams. The research highlights the potential of insect-mediated biodegradation as a sustainable approach to addressing plastic waste, which is a significant environmental challenge. Through this body of work, Zhuang, G. has contributed to advancing scientific understanding of biological pathways for managing persistent plastic pollutants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387721</data>
</node>
<node id="Peng, X.">
  <data key="d0">Peng, X.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Peng, X. is a researcher recognized for contributions to studies on the biodegradation of synthetic polymer foams by insect larvae. Specifically, Peng, X. is listed as an author and co-author of multiple studies published around 2020 and 2021 that investigate the degradation of expanded polystyrene (EPS) and polyethylene foams, including low-density polyethylene (LDPE), by the larvae of *Tenebrio molitor* Linnaeus, commonly known as mealworms. These studies, including one published in *Chemosphere* in 2021, focus on the capacity of *T. molitor* larvae to consume and break down persistent plastic materials, offering insights into potential biological solutions for plastic waste management. Peng, X.’s work in this area contributes to the growing body of research exploring insect-mediated biodegradation as an environmentally sustainable approach to addressing the global challenge of plastic pollution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387720</data>
</node>
<node id="Song, Y.L.">
  <data key="d0">Song, Y.L.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Song, Y.L. is a researcher recognized for contributions to the study of plastic biodegradation, particularly focusing on the role of mealworms in breaking down synthetic polymers. As a co-author of multiple studies, including a notable publication in *Chemosphere* (2015), Song, Y.L. has investigated the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene, a widely used and environmentally persistent plastic. This body of work demonstrated that mealworms, often referred to as plastic-eating organisms, are capable of consuming and metabolizing polystyrene, leading to its partial degradation and conversion into simpler compounds. Through these studies, Song, Y.L. has contributed to advancing scientific understanding of biological pathways for plastic degradation, highlighting the potential of insect-based systems as a sustainable approach to mitigating plastic pollution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f</data>
