<node id="FTIR Analysis">
  <data key="d0">FTIR Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">FTIR analysis was performed on frass samples to detect chemical changes such as the appearance of carbonyl groups and hydroxyl groups, indicating biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR analysis was used to confirm biodegradation and oxidation of EPS and LDPE.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR analysis was used in the study to reveal chemical alterations in PVC after biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR analysis was used to detect chemical modifications in residual polymers, showing incorporation of oxygen and functional groups such as alcohols.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR (Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy) analysis was used to study chemical modifications in PE after digestion by lesser waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR analysis was used to detect chemical changes, oxidation, and depolymerization of PS in frass samples.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR (Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy) analysis was used to confirm depolymerization and degradation of MPs by larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386245</data>
</node>
