<node id="Harbin Institute of Technology">
  <data key="d0">Harbin Institute of Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Harbin Institute of Technology (HIT) is a prominent higher education institution located in Harbin, China. It is recognized for its strong academic and research affiliations, particularly in the fields of engineering, environmental science, and bioenergy. The university is home to several key research centers and laboratories, including the State Key Laboratory of Urban Water Resource and Environment and the National Engineering Research Center for Bioenergy, both of which play significant roles in advancing scientific innovation and applied research.  

HIT has been identified as the institutional affiliation of several researchers acknowledged in academic studies, including Dr. Shanshan Yang and Dr. Shangshang Yang, who have received support from the university in their scholarly work. Through its extensive network of laboratories, schools, and research centers, the institution fosters interdisciplinary collaboration and contributes to addressing critical challenges in urban water management, environmental sustainability, and renewable energy.  

As one of China’s leading universities, Harbin Institute of Technology combines advanced research infrastructure with a commitment to academic excellence, making it a central hub for scientific inquiry and technological development in the region. Its affiliations with national-level laboratories and engineering research centers underscore its role as a key contributor to China’s higher education and research landscape.</data>
