<node id="Northern Ireland">
  <data key="d0">Northern Ireland</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">One of the locations where mealworm polystyrene degradation was studied.&lt;SEP&gt;Northern Ireland is one of the countries where detailed assessments of mealworms' ability to digest polystyrene were carried out, with one source contributing.&lt;SEP&gt;Northern Ireland was mentioned as a region where mealworms were sourced and experiments were conducted.&lt;SEP&gt;Northern Ireland is a location where 200 mealworms were incubated in 600 mL containers as part of a study on plastic consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms from Northern Ireland were tested for PS consumption rates and degradation effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Northern Ireland is one of the geographic sources of mealworm samples studied.&lt;SEP&gt;Northern Ireland is one of the locations where yellow mealworms capable of digesting PS foam were sourced.</data>
