<node id="Plastic Wastes">
  <data key="d0">Plastic Wastes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Category mentioned in keywords, related to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic wastes are environmental pollutants that could potentially be biodegraded and recycled using enzymes derived from insect gut microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic wastes are synthetic polymer-based materials that accumulate in the environment, causing pollution and ecological harm.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic wastes are described as harmful to humans, marine creatures, and vegetation when buried in soil.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic wastes are described as a major environmental concern of global significance, with up to 6300 million metric tons generated to date.</data>
