<node id="PS Mass Balances">
  <data key="d0">PS Mass Balances</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PS mass balances were used to determine specific rates of PS degradation in mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756373322</data>
</node>
<node id="Exiguobacterium sp.">
  <data key="d0">Exiguobacterium sp.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Exiguobacterium sp. is a PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated from mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Exiguobacterium sp. is a bacterium from the digestive tract of Tenebrio molitor larvae with the ability to degrade polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Exiguobacterium sp. is a bacterial genus identified in insect guts with plastic-degrading ability.&lt;SEP&gt;Exiguobacterium sp. is identified as a microorganism capable of creating biofilms and degrading polystyrene (PS) in the gut of Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Exiguobacterium sp. is a bacterial species reported in previous studies as being capable of degrading polystyrene from the intestines of mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386794</data>
</node>
