<node id="Lactobacillaceae">
  <data key="d0">Lactobacillaceae</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Lactobacillaceae is one of the most abundant bacterial families in mealworm gut communities.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactobacillaceae is a family of bacteria whose growth in mice intestines increased when T. molitor was added to their diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactobacillaceae is a bacterial family within the order Lactobacillales, represented in the study by Lactobacillus species such as L. crispatus, L. graminis, L. johnsonii, and L. salivarius.&lt;SEP&gt;A bacterial family associated with inositol metabolism and abundant in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;A bacterial family dominant in the gut microbiome of bran-fed yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactobacillaceae is a bacterial family whose relative abundance was negatively affected by microplastic feeding in Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactobacillaceae are a family of bacteria whose abundance decreased in response to polymer additives.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73db2a18ccd822d0da3ef61e68d3a6f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
