<node id="Erwinia">
  <data key="d0">Erwinia</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Erwinia is the most prevalent bacterial genus in mealworm gut communities across different diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Erwinia is a bacterial genus detected in the gut microbiome of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Erwinia is a bacterial genus identified in the digestive tracts of adult T. molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Erwinia is a bacterial genus found in the digestive tracts of adult Tenebrio molitor. A strain identified was Erwinia persicina.&lt;SEP&gt;Erwinia is one of the 14 genera within the family Erwiniaeae.&lt;SEP&gt;Erwinia is a bacterial genus used for comparative genomic analysis with strain BIT-26T.</data>
