<node id="Streptococcus">
  <data key="d0">Streptococcus</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Streptococcus is a bacterial genus found in Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Streptococcus is a bacterial genus previously reported in T. molitor fed with PS.&lt;SEP&gt;Streptococcus is a bacterial genus detected in the gut microbiome of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Streptococcus is a bacterial genus isolated from termites, associated with lignocellulose degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Streptococcus is a bacterial genus found in high abundance in PS- and CS-fed larvae, associated with plastic or lignocellulose degradation.</data>
