<node id="Tenebrio Molitor">
  <data key="d0">Tenebrio Molitor</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Tenebrio Molitor, also known as mealworm larvae, is referenced as capable of biodegrading polystyrene and polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworm larvae studied for their ability to biodegrade cellulose, polyethylene, and polystyrene waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor is a beetle species studied for growth and development under different moisture conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio Molitor, also known as mealworms, are studied for their ability to digest and biodegrade plastics such as polystyrene and polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms studied for their role in polyethylene biodegradation.</data>
