<node id="Bhak, J.">
  <data key="d0">Bhak, J.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Bhak, J. is a researcher and co-author recognized for contributions to the study of the hologenome of *Galleria mellonella*, commonly known as the greater wax moth, with a particular focus on its ability to metabolize beeswax. In 2019, Bhak, J. co-authored a study that investigated the holobiont or hologenome of *Galleria mellonella*, examining the complex interactions between the insect host and its associated microbial community. This research explored how the combined genetic and metabolic capacities of the moth and its microbiota enable the breakdown of beeswax, a substance composed largely of long-chain hydrocarbons. The study provided insights into the metabolic pathways involved in beeswax degradation and highlighted the ecological and biological significance of the *Galleria mellonella* holobiont. Through this work, Bhak, J. contributed to advancing understanding of host-microbe interactions, insect metabolism, and the potential applications of such systems in biodegradation and biotechnology.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c</data>
