<node id="Przemieniecki, S.W.">
  <data key="d0">Przemieniecki, S.W.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Przemieniecki, S.W. is a researcher and author whose work focuses primarily on the gut microbiome and enzymatic activity of *Tenebrio molitor* (mealworm) larvae in the context of biodegradation processes. He has contributed to multiple studies examining how these larvae interact with and break down various waste materials, including cellulose, polyethylene, and polystyrene. His research highlights the role of the larvae’s gut microbiome and enzymatic profiles in enabling the degradation of both organic and synthetic substrates, thereby contributing to the understanding of insect-mediated biodegradation as a potential solution for waste management and plastic pollution.  

In addition to his studies on waste biodegradation, Przemieniecki, S.W. has co-authored research exploring the application of mealworm larvae meal as a fertilizer for wheat seedlings, indicating his broader interest in the agricultural and environmental applications of insect-based bioproducts. His publications span at least from 2019 to 2020, during which he has consistently investigated the microbiological and biochemical mechanisms underlying the larvae’s ability to process diverse materials.  

Overall, Przemieniecki, S.W. is recognized for his contributions to the fields of microbiology, entomology, and environmental biotechnology, with a particular emphasis on the symbiotic relationship between *Tenebrio molitor* larvae and their gut microbiota in the biodegradation of waste and plastics, as well as their potential role in sustainable agriculture.&lt;SEP&gt;Przemieniecki, S.W. is an author of a study on gut microbiome and enzymatic profile of Tenebrio molitor larvae biodegrading waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af93e805daf3987d95ff99ab8e891d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f</data>
