</node>
<node id="Ciesielski, S.">
  <data key="d0">Ciesielski, S.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Ciesielski, S. is a researcher and author whose work focuses on the gut microbiome and enzymatic activity of *Tenebrio molitor* larvae in the context of biodegradation. Their research contributions include studies published in 2019 and 2020 that investigate how the gut microbial community and enzymatic profiles of these larvae adapt when exposed to and degrade various types of waste materials. Specifically, Ciesielski, S. has co-authored studies examining the larvae’s ability to biodegrade plastics such as polyethylene and polystyrene, as well as cellulose and other organic waste substrates. These studies provide insights into the metabolic and microbial mechanisms that enable *Tenebrio molitor* larvae to process and break down otherwise persistent waste materials, highlighting the potential role of insect-based biodegradation in waste management and environmental sustainability. Through this body of work, Ciesielski, S. has contributed to advancing understanding of insect-microbe interactions and their applications in biodegradation research.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author in a study on gut microbiome and enzymatic profile of Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Ciesielski, S. is an author of a study on gut microbiome and enzymatic profile of Tenebrio molitor larvae biodegrading waste.</data>
