<node id="Mechanical Recycling">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Recycling</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mechanical recycling is a method of reintroducing plastic waste into the production cycle by reshaping thermoplastics under high temperature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756373799</data>
</node>
<node id="Chemical Recycling">
  <data key="d0">Chemical Recycling</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Chemical recycling involves converting plastic waste into valuable chemical substances or precursors of plastic, including methods such as pyrolysis and gasification.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical recycling is a traditional method of disposing of waste plastic, but it cannot fundamentally solve environmental pollution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384500</data>
</node>
<node id="Pyrolysis">
  <data key="d0">Pyrolysis</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pyrolysis is a chemical recycling method where plastics decompose under high temperatures and anaerobic conditions, producing biofuel.&lt;SEP&gt;Pyrolysis is a scientific journal that published a study on fluidised bed pyrolysis of low density polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Pyrolysis is a journal that published research on fluidised bed pyrolysis of low density polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Pyrolysis is the thermal decomposition process occurring during TGA analysis, producing combustible gases and biochar.&lt;SEP&gt;Pyrolysis is a process studied for its role in mitigating microplastics in sewage sludge, with temperature as a key factor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-81b6237c84f002117fbfe7575d9cdd6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e</data>
