  <data key="d2">Entomoremediation is the use of insects, such as Tenebrio molitor, for biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Entomoremediation is a subtype of bioremediation that involves the use of insects to degrade plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Entomoremediation is the process of using insects to degrade and remediate plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Entomoremediation is a novel in-situ bioremediation approach using insects for environmental remediation.</data>
