<node id="Perryman, M.">
  <data key="d0">Perryman, M.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Perryman, M. is a researcher recognized for co-authoring the influential scientific article *“Plastic waste inputs from land into the ocean,”* published in *Science* in 2015. This study is widely cited as a foundational work in the field of environmental science, particularly in understanding the scale and pathways of plastic pollution entering marine ecosystems from terrestrial sources. As one of the contributing authors, Perryman, M. played a role in advancing knowledge on the global magnitude of plastic waste leakage into the ocean, helping to quantify the problem and highlight its environmental implications. The publication has become a key reference in research and policy discussions addressing plastic pollution and its impact on marine environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Co-author of a study on plastic waste inputs from land to the ocean.&lt;SEP&gt;Perryman, M. is an author of a referenced study on plastic waste inputs from land into the ocean.</data>
