<node id="Narayan, R.">
  <data key="d0">Narayan, R.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Narayan, R. is a researcher and author recognized for contributions to the scientific study of plastic waste and its environmental impacts. He is one of the co-authors of the influential article *“Plastic waste inputs from land into the ocean”*, published in *Science* in 2015, which quantified the scale of plastic waste entering marine environments from terrestrial sources and highlighted the global implications of plastic pollution. This widely cited study has played a pivotal role in advancing understanding of the pathways and magnitude of plastic waste leakage into oceans, shaping both scientific discourse and policy discussions on marine debris. In addition to this work, Narayan, R. has also contributed to research on biodegradable plastics, exploring their potential as sustainable alternatives to conventional plastics in addressing the growing problem of plastic waste pollution. Through these contributions, Narayan, R. has been associated with advancing knowledge on both the environmental challenges posed by plastic waste and possible material-based solutions.</data>
