  <data key="d0">Sewage Sludge</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Sewage sludge from wastewater treatment plants in China was studied for microplastic content.&lt;SEP&gt;Sewage sludge is a microbial environment where polystyrene biodegradation has been tested, showing low degradation rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Sewage sludge is mentioned as a source of bacteria used in polystyrene biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Sewage sludge is mentioned as one of the sources from which bacteria and fungi capable of degrading plastics have been isolated.&lt;SEP&gt;Sewage sludge is studied for microplastic mitigation through pyrolysis.</data>
