<node id="Pseudomonas aeruginosa">
  <data key="d0">Pseudomonas aeruginosa</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a bacterium isolated from the gut extract of superworms and studied for its ability to biodegrade plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;A bacterial species identified among isolates, known for crude oil degradation, biosurfactant production, and potential PS degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a bacterial species studied in relation to polystyrene degradation in Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a soil bacterium proven to degrade plastic waste including PS foam.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a bacterial species associated with polyethylene biodegradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382959</data>
</node>
<node id="PU">
  <data key="d0">PU</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41</data>
  <data key="d2">Zophobas morio was used in studies to test PU degradation, though efficiency was low.&lt;SEP&gt;PU refers to polyurethane, the primary material studied for biodegradation by T. molitor larvae and associated microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;PU (Polyurethane) is a type of plastic mentioned as being degraded by unclassified Enterobacteriaceae in superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Description not available in text.&lt;SEP&gt;PU refers to polyurethane, a type of plastic polymer that was used as a diet for yellow mealworms in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;PU refers to polyurethane, a type of polymerized plastic tested in the study for biodegradation by yellow mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385016</data>
</node>
