<node id="Chitin">
  <data key="d0">Chitin</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Chitin is a compound present in worm frass, potentially contributing to plant growth promotion.&lt;SEP&gt;Chitin is a compound reported to support rooting and was present in superworm frass.&lt;SEP&gt;Chitin is a biological compound estimated in insects and extracted from larvae, with applications in plant elicitor activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Chitin is a structural component of insect cuticle, detected in frass during NMR analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Chitin is a biopolymer found in the insect cuticle, identified in the fecula through resonance signals.&lt;SEP&gt;Chitin is a component of melted skeletons ingested by starved mealworms.</data>
