  <data key="d0">COVID-19 Pandemic</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The COVID-19 pandemic is mentioned as a factor that worsened the problem of plastic waste due to lockdown measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The global epidemic of Coronavirus disease 2019, during which mask usage and production increased significantly.&lt;SEP&gt;The COVID-19 pandemic is mentioned as a factor that may affect projected polypropylene sales growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385234</data>
</node>
<node id="Worms">
  <data key="d0">Worms</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Worms are studied for their ability to consume polystyrene (PS), produce frass that supports plant growth, and serve as food for humans, poultry, and fish.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374069</data>
</node>
<node id="Enzymes from Plastic-Eating Worms">
  <data key="d0">Enzymes from Plastic-Eating Worms</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Enzymes isolated from bacteria in plastic-eating worms are studied for their potential in plastic degradation, though large-scale application requires optimization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374069</data>
</node>
<node id="Protein Engineering">
  <data key="d0">Protein Engineering</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Protein engineering is mentioned as a promising approach to improve enzymes for plastic degradation, though still less practical than worms at present.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374069</data>
</node>
<node id="Urban Farming">
  <data key="d0">Urban Farming</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Urban farming is mentioned as a context where worms can be used for food production, both as feed and through their frass for crops.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374069</data>
</node>
<node id="Food Sustainability">
  <data key="d0">Food Sustainability</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Food sustainability is highlighted as a global issue that worms can help address through their dual role in waste reduction and food production.</data>
