<node id="Nature">
  <data key="d0">Nature</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">**Nature** is a leading international scientific journal that serves as a prominent platform for publishing high-impact research and policy articles across a wide range of disciplines. It has been cited as the publication source for several influential works related to environmental science and plastic pollution. In 2013, *Nature* published a policy article by Rochman C. M. and colleagues titled *“Classify plastic waste as hazardous,”* which advocated for the recognition of plastic waste as a hazardous material due to its environmental and health risks. This article highlighted the urgent need for stronger regulatory frameworks to address the growing problem of plastic pollution.  

In addition to policy-focused contributions, *Nature* has also published significant scientific research on plastic degradation and recycling technologies. In 2020, the journal featured the paper *“An Engineered PET Depolymerase to Break Down and Recycle Plastic Bottles,”* which presented an innovative enzymatic approach to depolymerize polyethylene terephthalate (PET), offering a potential solution for large-scale recycling of plastic bottles. This study represented a major advancement in the development of sustainable methods for managing plastic waste.  

Further extending its coverage of plastic-related research, *Nature* published a 2021 study on the direct radiative effects of airborne microplastics. This work explored how microplastic particles suspended in the atmosphere can influence climate processes by interacting with solar radiation, thereby adding a new dimension to the understanding of plastic pollution’s global impact.  

Through these publications, *Nature* has played a critical role in disseminating both scientific discoveries and policy proposals that shape the discourse on plastic waste, recycling technologies, and environmental sustainability. The journal’s contributions underscore its importance as a central venue for advancing knowledge and fostering global dialogue on pressing environmental challenges.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-908b8bfa7e446694958cf9bd0cfbc583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933de951613fc7eadfd14dde9bd18b2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71372e333b39cee7eea0c53f89bec5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387455</data>
</node>
