<node id="Starvation">
  <data key="d0">Starvation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Starvation, in the context of experimental studies on *Tenebrio molitor* (mealworm) larvae, refers to a controlled condition in which individuals are deliberately deprived of food. It was employed as a control or comparative treatment in feeding experiments, allowing researchers to assess the effects of food absence relative to other dietary conditions. Under starvation, larvae rely on stored fat and lipid reserves to sustain basic metabolic processes, leading to measurable physiological changes. These changes include reductions in reserve density and volumetric length, while structural components are preserved and no growth occurs.  

In Dynamic Energy Budget (DEB) modeling, starvation plays a critical role in parameter estimation, as it reveals how energy is allocated under resource scarcity. Observations during starvation provide insights into energy conductance, maintenance costs, and the depletion of reserves, which are reflected in body mass loss and altered energy allocation patterns. By monitoring larvae under starvation, researchers can quantify survival rates, evaluate metabolic trade-offs, and better understand the balance between reserve utilization and structural maintenance.  

Overall, starvation serves both as an experimental condition for studying the physiological and survival responses of mealworms to food deprivation and as a methodological tool in DEB modeling to refine parameters related to energy dynamics and organismal resilience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c651f9305c4265540ed7deeb891eae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-838d20fb5f3709d303402ea916d8172f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388207</data>
</node>
