<node id="Molecular Weight Distribution (MWD)">
  <data key="d0">Molecular Weight Distribution (MWD)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">MWD refers to the distribution of molecular weights in polymers determined in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular weight distribution (MWD) describes the distribution of molecular sizes in polymer residues, which shifted towards lower molecular weights after larval ingestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular Weight Distribution (MWD) refers to the distribution of molecular weights within a polymer sample. The study analyzed changes in MWD of LDPE, LLDPE, and HDPE before and after biodegradation by Tenebrio larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular Weight Distribution (MWD) is a parameter used to assess changes in LDPE polymers after digestion by larvae.</data>
