  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">LDPE microplastics were analyzed for crystalline structure changes after being metabolized by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;LDPE microplastics decompose in one stage through chain scission, producing alkenes such as ethane, ethene, propane, propene, and butane.&lt;SEP&gt;LDPE microplastics are low-density polyethylene particles that can be degraded by gut bacteria from Lumbricus terrestris.</data>
