  <data key="d0">Cronobacter sakazakii</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Cronobacter sakazakii is identified as a candidate bacterium that may contribute to EPS degradation in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Cronobacter sakazakii is a bacterial species from the Enterobacteriaceae family, found in both groups, with 0.77% in the bran-fed group and 25.47% in the EPS-fed group. It may be involved in EPS degradation.</data>
