  <data key="d0">Paenibacillus urinalis</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Paenibacillus urinalis is a bacterial species reported in 2010 to have biodegradation capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7432cb0d6c74fd2dd80b065fbad26b4b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374565</data>
</node>
<node id="Mixed Microbial Cultures">
  <data key="d0">Mixed Microbial Cultures</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixed microbial cultures were found to grow on styrene as the sole carbon source in biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixed microbial cultures have been studied for their ability to biodegrade polystyrene into low molecular organics or CO2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7432cb0d6c74fd2dd80b065fbad26b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756383986</data>
</node>
<node id="Soil Invertebrates">
  <data key="d0">Soil Invertebrates</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Five groups of soil invertebrates were tested for their ability to biodegrade polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Soil invertebrates were tested to determine whether they could degrade PS when fed with 14C-labeled PS tracers in their diets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7432cb0d6c74fd2dd80b065fbad26b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
