<node id="Solid-state 13C-CP/MS NMR">
  <data key="d0">Solid-state 13C-CP/MS NMR</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Solid-state 13C cross-polarization/magic angle spinning nuclear magnetic resonance (13C-CP/MS NMR) is an analytical method used to study chemical changes in degraded plastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374574</data>
</node>
<node id="Liquid-state 1H-NMR">
  <data key="d0">Liquid-state 1H-NMR</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Liquid-state 1H nuclear magnetic resonance (1H-NMR) is an analytical method used to analyze chemical changes during PS degradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374575</data>
</node>
<node id="13C-labeled CO2">
  <data key="d0">13C-labeled CO2</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">13C-labeled CO2 is a marker released from mealworms fed with 13C-labeled PS, confirming biodegradation and mineralization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374575</data>
</node>
<node id="α 13C-labeled PS">
  <data key="d0">α 13C-labeled PS</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">α 13C-labeled PS is a form of isotopically labeled polystyrene used in experiments to trace biodegradation in mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374575</data>
</node>
<node id="β 13C-labeled PS">
  <data key="d0">β 13C-labeled PS</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">β 13C-labeled PS is another form of isotopically labeled polystyrene used in experiments to trace biodegradation in mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374575</data>
</node>
<node id="Enzymes">
  <data key="d0">Enzymes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Enzymes, especially extracellular enzymes, are suggested as potential agents for plastic depolymerization and future large-scale biodegradation applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes are biological catalysts studied for their role in plastic degradation and polymer hydrolysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes were detected in the residual solid fraction of larval frass, potentially contributing to PET degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes are biological catalysts mentioned as agents in the biodegradation of polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes are biological molecules mentioned in the context of their ability, or lack thereof, to degrade synthetic polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes secreted by larvae play a role in the biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes secreted in the gut of larvae facilitated the decomposition of aged MPs into smaller monomers by oxidation and depolymerization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb16cd27b6682965375050748ee77862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386220</data>
</node>
<node id="Plastic-depolymerizing Enzymes">
  <data key="d0">Plastic-depolymerizing Enzymes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Plastic-depolymerizing enzymes are proposed for future biotechnological applications to break down plastics on a large scale.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374576</data>
</node>
<node id="Future Scientific Studies">
  <data key="d0">Future Scientific Studies</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Future scientific studies are anticipated to further explore PS degradation mechanisms, microbial interactions, and biotechnological applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374576</data>
</node>
<node id="Biotechnologies">
  <data key="d0">Biotechnologies</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Biotechnologies are potential applications of PS degradation research aimed at solving the plastic pollution problem.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756374576</data>
