<node id="Appl. Microbiol. Biotechnol.">
  <data key="d0">Appl. Microbiol. Biotechnol.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">**Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology (Appl. Microbiol. Biotechnol.)** is a peer-reviewed scientific journal that publishes research in the fields of applied microbiology, biotechnology, and related disciplines. The journal has served as a platform for numerous influential studies addressing environmental challenges, particularly those related to plastic pollution and biodegradation.  

Several key studies on microbial and enzymatic approaches to mitigating plastic waste have been published in *Appl. Microbiol. Biotechnol.*. These include a 2015 study by Krueger, Harms, and Schlosser that explored microbiological solutions to plastic pollution, highlighting the potential of microbial systems in addressing environmental contamination caused by synthetic polymers. The journal also published a 2014 study on the microbial degradation of co-polymers, advancing understanding of how microorganisms can break down complex synthetic materials. In 2013, it featured research on biodegradable plastic-degrading enzymes, contributing to the development of enzymatic strategies for polymer breakdown. Additionally, the journal published a 2013 study on the role of biosurfactants in bioremediation, emphasizing their importance in enhancing microbial degradation processes.  

*Appl. Microbiol. Biotechnol.* has also been a venue for studies on specific microbial species and their role in plastic biodegradation. For example, research on *Rhodococcus ruber* and its capacity to degrade polyethylene was published in the journal, providing insights into microbial pathways for tackling one of the most persistent forms of plastic waste.  

Overall, *Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology* is recognized as a significant publication outlet for research on microbial and biotechnological solutions to environmental issues, particularly the biodegradation of plastics and the development of sustainable strategies for pollution mitigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Appl. Microbiol. Biotechnol. is the journal where the study on microbiological solutions to plastic pollution was published in 2015.&lt;SEP&gt;Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology journal where the Aspergillus oryzae enzyme study was published.&lt;SEP&gt;Applied Microbiology and Biotechnology journal where the styrene degradation study was published.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal where the 2015 study on microbiological solutions to plastic pollution was published.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aad5e97885ea1116956513db244b8fb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71372e333b39cee7eea0c53f89bec5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af93e805daf3987d95ff99ab8e891d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff1127258b5df378d8b32fff2a93eb84</data>
