<node id="UPARSE">
  <data key="d0">UPARSE</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">UPARSE is a bioinformatics software tool and method designed for clustering microbial amplicon sequences into Operational Taxonomic Units (OTUs). It is widely recognized for its ability to generate highly accurate OTU sequences by applying a sequence identity threshold of 97% (0.97), a standard cutoff used in microbial ecology to approximate species-level distinctions. First published in 2013, UPARSE introduced a robust approach to OTU clustering that improved accuracy compared to earlier methods, reducing errors such as spurious OTU inflation caused by sequencing artifacts.  

The tool has been implemented in multiple versions, including UPARSE v9.2.64 and UPARSE v11, both of which maintain the core functionality of clustering sequences at the 97% identity threshold. By processing microbial amplicon reads, UPARSE enables researchers to identify and classify OTUs with high precision, making it an essential component of microbial community analysis pipelines. Its methodological framework has contributed significantly to advancements in microbial ecology, metagenomics, and environmental microbiology by providing a reliable means of interpreting high-throughput sequencing data.  

In summary, UPARSE is a foundational bioinformatics method and software tool for OTU clustering, notable for its accuracy, use of a 97% identity threshold, and continued application across different versions since its introduction in 2013.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41af774fc28352c7dd95d8c3cb43f855&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386499</data>
</node>
