  <data key="d2">Kosakonia sp. is a microbial genus strongly associated with PE and PS degradation in T. molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;A bacterial strain associated with the biodegradation of PE in the gut microbiome of yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Kosakonia sp. is a bacterial taxon identified in the gut microbiome of mealworms, strongly associated with the degradation of both polyethylene and polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Kosakonia sp. is a bacterial genus significantly associated with plastic-fed diets (PE and PS) in the mealworm gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Kosakonia sp. is a bacterial species that was more abundant in plastic-only diets and strongly associated with both polyethylene (PE) and polystyrene (PS) degradation in the mealworm gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Kosakonia sp. is a bacterium associated with the gut microbiome of mealworms fed on PS and PE diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Kosakonia sp. is a bacterial genus associated with PE and PS degradation in T. molitor.</data>
