<node id="Negative Control">
  <data key="d0">Negative Control</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Negative controls consisted of gut microbiome supplemented with supernatant but without PS, used to compare respiration activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Negative control refers to PE mulching films cultured without bacterial inoculation, used to compare experimental results.&lt;SEP&gt;The negative control refers to PE mulching films without bacterial inoculation, used as a baseline for comparison in degradation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Negative control conditions were used in experiments, such as uninoculated flasks or Escherichia coli ATCC 25922, to ensure validity of results.&lt;SEP&gt;The negative control refers to the use of E. coli strains that did not degrade polystyrene, serving as a baseline for comparison in the experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07a91e5cf8b623163be09e14d1f4978e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386819</data>
</node>
