<node id="Antibiotic Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Antibiotic Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibiotic treatment was applied to mealworm diets (PS and bran) to test whether the gut microbiome or the mealworm itself was responsible for emulsifying activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibiotic treatment was applied to larvae for 6 days, resulting in suppression of gut microbial colonies and reduced ability to digest PS and CS feedstocks.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibiotic treatment refers to the experimental condition where larvae were exposed to antibiotics such as gentamicin to suppress gut microbiota.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c84ac252cb9ce906354bda2ad1113aba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386521</data>
</node>
<node id="Tween-80">
  <data key="d0">Tween-80</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Tween-80 is a known surfactant referenced as a comparison for the emulsification activity observed in mealworm gut supernatant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756375027</data>
</node>
