<node id="Merck">
  <data key="d0">Merck</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Merck is a German company that provided nutrient agar (NA) for bacterial isolation.&lt;SEP&gt;Merck supplied solvents (LiChrosolv®) used in the extraction process.&lt;SEP&gt;Merck is a supplier of chemicals, solvents, and reagents used in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Merck is a company based in Steinheim, Germany, that supplied chemicals for the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Merck is a supplier of LC-MS grade methanol, acetonitrile, isopropanol, methyl tert-butyl ether (MTBE), and tetrahydrofuran (THF), located in Steinheim, Germany.&lt;SEP&gt;Merck is the supplier of KBr and chloroform-D used in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462</data>
