<node id="Mealworm Biodegradation Experiment">
  <data key="d0">Mealworm Biodegradation Experiment</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The experiment studied the ability of T. molitor larvae and imagines to digest different types of polystyrene and bioplastics, and analyzed gut microbiome changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756375241</data>
</node>
<node id="PSr">
  <data key="d0">PSr</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PSr refers to processed polystyrene obtained through extrusion, injection molding, and grinding, used in the experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;PSr is a polystyrene variant processed by press molding before consumption tests.&lt;SEP&gt;A variant of polystyrene material studied for its susceptibility to mealworm chewing and biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;PSr is a raw form of polystyrene used in the feeding experiments, leading to strong declines in carbohydrate levels in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;PSr is a type of polystyrene material tested in the experiment. It showed high hardness and gloss values, moderate mass loss (5.75%), and was associated with low lipid and sugar content in mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326aabc25dd967951a7845ea221532ac</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756379491</data>
</node>
<node id="PSP">
  <data key="d0">PSP</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PSP refers to commercially available polystyrene packaging material fed to larvae in the experiment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756375242</data>
</node>
<node id="I">
  <data key="d0">I</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">I refers to the control group of larvae fed with oatmeal ad libitum.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756375242</data>
</node>
