</node>
<node id="Fatty acids">
  <data key="d0">Fatty acids</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Fatty acids are oxidized during starvation in insects to provide energy.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioactive molecules identified in the polar fraction of frass during the biodegradation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Fatty acids are biochemical compounds measured in larvae, analyzed in relation to diets in PCA analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Fatty acids are biochemical compounds analyzed in mealworms under different diets, with variations in quality and quantity depending on diet type.&lt;SEP&gt;Fatty acids were observed to undergo transformation in larvae under different dietary conditions, supporting microbial metabolism and biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Whole-cell fatty acids were extracted from strain BIT-26T and analyzed to determine its chemotaxonomic profile.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381810</data>
</node>
