<node id="High-Density Polyethylene (HDPE)">
  <data key="d0">High-Density Polyethylene (HDPE)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">High-Density Polyethylene (HDPE) is a type of polyethylene plastic characterized by its long linear molecular chains, minimal branching, and high crystallinity. These structural features give HDPE notable physical properties, including high tensile strength, rigidity, elasticity, and relatively high melting points. Due to its crystalline structure and stability, HDPE is generally resistant to biodegradation and has long been considered a persistent plastic in the environment.  

Despite this resistance, recent studies have investigated the potential for biological degradation of HDPE by various organisms. Research has shown that HDPE can be partially degraded by certain insect larvae and microorganisms. For example, the lesser waxworm has been observed to degrade HDPE under experimental conditions, while mealworms have been reported to create visible marks and holes in HDPE bags, suggesting some level of consumption and breakdown. Additionally, bacterial strains such as *Bacillus sp. PELW2042* have demonstrated the ability to degrade HDPE, further indicating that microbial activity may play a role in its decomposition.  

Overall, High-Density Polyethylene (HDPE) is a widely used, durable plastic polymer with high crystallinity and low branching that makes it resistant to natural degradation. However, emerging studies highlight that certain insects and microbial species may contribute to its biodegradation, offering potential pathways for addressing plastic waste challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;HDPE is a type of polyethylene plastic that can be depolymerized by Achroia grissella.&lt;SEP&gt;High-density polyethylene microplastics (&lt;80 μm) were observed to be internalized in the digestive system of blue mussels and translocated to the bloodstream.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d575c206eb616c4c970fd48fe3349247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387073</data>
</node>
