<node id="GC-MS">
  <data key="d0">GC-MS</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">GC-MS (Gas Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry) is an analytical method used to analyze intestinal feces and PVC composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Gas Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry was used to detect intermediates of CS and PS metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;GC-MS refers to gas chromatography–mass spectrometry, used for metabolomic analysis of intermediates in larvae samples.&lt;SEP&gt;GC-MS analysis detected long-chain fatty acids as intermediates of PS/CS degradation in larval gut or frass samples.&lt;SEP&gt;GC-MS analysis was used to determine fatty acid content of exposure groups. It refers to Gas Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry as an analytical method.&lt;SEP&gt;GC-MS (Gas Chromatography-Mass Spectrometry) is the analytical technique used to identify degradation products of PE and PS microplastics after digestion by larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb00229bf45a3bd9b8a17e10a1c93d9</data>
