<node id="Yellow Mealworm (Tenebrio molitor)">
  <data key="d0">Yellow Mealworm (Tenebrio molitor)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Yellow Mealworm (Tenebrio molitor) is studied for its gut microbiome response to diet shifts during polystyrene and polyethylene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworm (Tenebrio molitor) is an insect species studied for its ability to biodegrade plastics such as polyurethane, polystyrene, polyethylene, and PVC, and its gut microbiome response to these diets.&lt;SEP&gt;An insect larvae used in the study to test ingestion and biodegradation of disposable surgical masks.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworm (Tenebrio molitor) is an insect whose gut microbiome responds to diet shifts during polystyrene and polyethylene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;A species of mealworm larvae studied for its ability to biodegrade polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are studied for their gut microbiome response to diet shifts during polyethylene biodegradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4da90774e2e5cb1fea30fd5aa390760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce368b44455642f4b9a1dacc4cdf0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3745cb01a4209e2eae28914dde3b52</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756383211</data>
</node>
<node id="Plastic-eating mealworms">
  <data key="d0">Plastic-eating mealworms</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Plastic-eating mealworms are studied for their ability to biodegrade and mineralize polystyrene with the help of gut microorganisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms capable of biodegrading and mineralizing polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms that are capable of biodegrading and mineralizing polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms studied for their ability to biodegrade and mineralize polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic-eating mealworms are studied for their ability to biodegrade and mineralize polystyrene, with focus on chemical, physical, and microbial aspects.&lt;SEP&gt;Organisms studied for their ability to biodegrade and mineralize polystyrene.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db0003a7244c51697d0129eb84b8e28e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce368b44455642f4b9a1dacc4cdf0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0</data>
