  <data key="d0">Indian meal moths (Plodia interpunctella)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Indian meal moths are insects studied for their ability to degrade polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Indian meal moths, scientifically known as Plodia interpunctella, are reported to consume plastics, with their gut microbes contributing to plastic digestion.</data>
