<node id="Gut microbes">
  <data key="d0">Gut microbes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Gut microbes are microorganisms living in the digestive systems of insects and animals, demonstrated to be essential for plastic digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microbes is a journal that published research on gut-associated microbes of Drosophila melanogaster.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microbes are microorganisms in the larvae's digestive system, studied for their role in PET biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Microorganisms in the mealworm gut that play a role in breaking down long-chain polystyrene molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microbes refer to the microbial communities in Tenebrio molitor larvae that play a role in the biodegradation of microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microbes are microorganisms in insect larvae that play a role in plastic biodegradation through depolymerization processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
