  <data key="d2">Laccase is a lignin-degrading enzyme reported to have low activity on polyethylene plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Laccase is an enzyme enriched in PP-fed larvae, contributing to PP oxidation and degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Laccase is an enzyme capable of degrading lignin.&lt;SEP&gt;Laccase is an oxidative enzyme known to decompose PE and aromatic compounds, observed to be activated in PET-fed larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Laccase is an enzyme detected in some bacterial isolates, involved in oxidative degradation processes.</data>
