  <data key="d0">PE Mulching Films</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PE mulching films are polyethylene-based agricultural films used in experiments to study degradation by bacterial strains.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene (PE) mulching films are agricultural plastic films used in soil, which are a major source of plastic pollution. They were the subject of biodegradation experiments in this study.&lt;SEP&gt;PE mulching films are agricultural films made of polyethylene, used in farming practices. They are highly resistant to biodegradation and require microbial or pretreatment methods for breakdown.</data>
