  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Aspergillus niger is a fungus used in mixed culture for biodegradation of low-density polyethylene (LDPE) in soil.&lt;SEP&gt;Aspergillus niger is a soil fungus proven to degrade plastic waste including PS foam.&lt;SEP&gt;Aspergillus niger is a fungal species associated with polyethylene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Aspergillus niger is a fungus studied for its ability to biodegrade thermally treated low density polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;A fungus studied for its ability to degrade thermally oxidized high-density polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;A fungus studied for biodegradation of low density polyethylene.</data>
