</node>
<node id="Bioremediation">
  <data key="d0">Bioremediation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The use of biological organisms to treat or remove pollutants, mentioned as a potential but unlikely application for larvae-based plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioremediation refers to the use of biological organisms, such as bacteria, to degrade pollutants like nanoplastics in ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioremediation is the process of using organisms to degrade pollutants, mentioned as a potential application of polystyrene biodegradation research.&lt;SEP&gt;Bioremediation refers to the use of biological organisms, such as bacteria, to degrade pollutants like plastics and microplastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa64e5cd2c08637934509262e56ab363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385661</data>
</node>
<node id="Waste plastics">
  <data key="d0">Waste plastics</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Waste plastics are the target material considered for biodegradation and recycling technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;Waste plastics are disposed of mainly in landfills (72%), with the remainder incinerated or recycled.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756379485</data>
</node>
<node id="Food waste composting/digestion">
  <data key="d0">Food waste composting/digestion</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Food waste composting/digestion is mentioned as a process where plastic anomalies could potentially be mitigated by understanding degradation mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756375865</data>
</node>
<node id="Cassone et al. (2020)">
  <data key="d0">Cassone et al. (2020)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Cassone et al. (2020) studied the intestinal microbiome of greater wax moth larvae fed on polyethylene and identified microorganisms, particularly Acinetobacter, as likely contributors to biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cassone et al. (2020) questioned the ubiquity of earlier published work on LDPE degradation by insects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756375865</data>
</node>
<node id="Kundungal et al. (2019)">
  <data key="d0">Kundungal et al. (2019)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Kundungal et al. (2019) demonstrated that larvae of the lesser waxworm (Achroia grisella) can degrade high-density polyethylene under various conditions, though a complete mass balance was not achieved.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756375865</data>
</node>
<node id="Yang et al. (2019)">
  <data key="d0">Yang et al. (2019)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Yang et al. (2019) expanded on their earlier work, showing that superworms (Zophobas atratus) mineralize polystyrene at higher rates, supported by respiratory tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Yang et al. (2019) showed that prior treatment of mealworm specimens with antibiotics affected their behavior in LDPE degradation experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756375866</data>
</node>
<node id="Amphibia hobby shop">
  <data key="d0">Amphibia hobby shop</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Amphibia hobby shop in Kontich, Belgium, supplied live larvae specimens used in the experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756375867</data>
</node>
