  <data key="d0">Bacillus subtilis</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Bacillus subtilis is a bacterium identified in the mealworm gut that contributes to the biodegradation of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus subtilis is a bacterial species mentioned in relation to surfactants that improve the efficiency of PE degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacterial species studied for polyethylene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus subtilis is a soil bacterium proven to degrade plastic waste including PS foam.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus subtilis is a bacterial species reported to degrade polyethylene.</data>
