<node id="Low-density polyethylene">
  <data key="d0">Low-density polyethylene</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Low-density polyethylene is a type of plastic that mealworms can biodegrade more effectively compared to high-density polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Low-density polyethylene is a type of plastic that bacteria of the genus Pantoea have the capacity to degrade.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic polymer studied for biodegradation in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Type of polyethylene studied for biodegradation and its effects on organisms such as earthworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Low-density polyethylene studied for biodegradation by mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
