<node id="Plastic waste">
  <data key="d0">Plastic waste</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Plastic waste refers to materials such as Styrofoam, carry bags, and plastic bottles that were tested for biodegradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste refers to discarded plastic materials that contribute to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste, including disposable surgical masks, is studied for biodegradation by insect larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste is referenced as a target material for degradation and up-recycling into cell proteins through microbial processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386000</data>
</node>
<node id="Environmental parameters">
  <data key="d0">Environmental parameters</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Environmental parameters such as temperature, humidity, and light intensity influence the intake capacity and growth of mealworms during biodegradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756376087</data>
</node>
<node id="Aspect Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Aspect Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Aspect Ratio (10^-3 to 10^-6) is a measurement used in the bacterial culture preparation from crushed bacteria in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756376088</data>
</node>
