  <data key="d0">Bacillus sp. PELW2042</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A Bacillus bacterial strain isolated from the gut contents of Tenebrio molitor larvae, capable of degrading high-density polyethylene (HDPE).&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. PELW2042 is the identified species of strain PELW2042, confirmed through Calmodulin gene sequence analysis and phylogenetic tree comparison. It is capable of degrading HDPE and altering its surface morphology and hydrophobicity.</data>
