<node id="PELW2042">
  <data key="d0">PELW2042</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">PELW2042 is the name given to a pure bacterial colony isolated from the gut of yellow mealworms, identified as a Gram-positive bacterium with HDPE-degrading ability.&lt;SEP&gt;PELW2042 is a bacterial strain isolated, cultured, and purified. It is Gram-positive, grows optimally at 35 °C and pH 7, forms round colonies with clear edges and yellowish color, and has elliptical rod-shaped cells. Identified as Bacillus sp. PELW2042, it can degrade HDPE by forming biofilms and secreting surfactants.&lt;SEP&gt;PELW2042 is a microbial strain studied for its ability to biodegrade HDPE (high-density polyethylene) films, causing structural, chemical, and molecular changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
