<node id="HDPE (High-Density Polyethylene)">
  <data key="d0">HDPE (High-Density Polyethylene)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">HDPE is a type of plastic with high environmental durability and resistance to microbial degradation due to its physicochemical properties such as high molecular weight, lack of functional groups, and hydrophobicity. It is the main target of biodegradation studies in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;HDPE is a type of polyethylene studied for its biodegradation by larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;HDPE is a minority component in commercial PE products, mentioned in the context of biodegradation differences.&lt;SEP&gt;HDPE (High-Density Polyethylene) is one of the five plastic types tested for mealworm consumption. It showed lower consumption levels compared to PS and PP.&lt;SEP&gt;HDPE (High-Density Polyethylene) is a type of plastic tested for consumption by mealworms. Consumption rates were recorded across different time intervals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-31b2c5f608adabba1cc6986356e96598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21d8b17fc7993bee31f7e07e4db97cfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475b22fe6100b14cced604f739663fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756383527</data>
</node>
