<node id="Enterobacter hormaechei">
  <data key="d0">Enterobacter hormaechei</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Enterobacter hormaechei is a bacterial species previously isolated from Tenebrio molitor and associated with polystyrene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter hormaechei is a microorganism isolated from Tenebrio molitor, tested on NPS and PS film for 15 days, studied in microbiome context.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter hormaechei is a bacterial species studied in relation to polystyrene degradation in Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;A gut bacterium from mealworms studied for polystyrene biodegradation under anaerobic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter hormaechei is the bacterial species to which strain LG3 belongs, confirmed through genome sequence analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter hormaechei is an opportunistic pathogen mentioned in relation to lipid A, a toxic endotoxin component.&lt;SEP&gt;A bacterial species collected from wastewater treatment plants, studied for heterotrophic denitrification.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167</data>
