<node id="Polystyrene biodegradation">
  <data key="d0">Polystyrene biodegradation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Polystyrene biodegradation refers to the experimental process of testing mealworms and their gut bacteria for the ability to degrade polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene biodegradation is the subject of studies on solutions to plastic waste pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene biodegradation refers to the process of breaking down polystyrene by microbial and enzymatic activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene biodegradation refers to the process of breaking down polystyrene by organisms such as mealworms and superworms, as studied in multiple referenced works.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene biodegradation refers to the microbial and biological processes studied for breaking down polystyrene waste.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44e006d8af33633a06dac6789334329d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40</data>
