<node id="Paula M. Peña-Pascagaza">
  <data key="d0">Paula M. Peña-Pascagaza</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Paula M. Peña-Pascagaza is one of the authors of the study on Tenebrio molitor and its gut bacteria growth in polystyrene presence as the sole carbon source.&lt;SEP&gt;Paula M. Peña-Pascagaza is an environmental engineer with expertise in bioprocesses, microbiology, geographic information systems, environmental study and monitoring. She provides accompaniment and advice in environmental areas such as research development, guidelines, legislation management, processing before environmental authorities, and software application. She is described as adaptable, resourceful, results-oriented, and analytical.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
