<node id="Miguel A. Ballen-Segura">
  <data key="d0">Miguel A. Ballen-Segura</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Miguel A. Ballen-Segura is one of the authors of the study on Tenebrio molitor and its gut bacteria growth in polystyrene presence as the sole carbon source.&lt;SEP&gt;Miguel A. Ballen-Segura holds a Ph.D. and MSc with emphasis in fundamental and applied ecology. He works at the School of Exact Sciences and Engineering, Sergio Arboleda University as a professor and researcher, focusing on projects involving microorganisms as remediation tools and their role in high mountain aquatic systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377438</data>
</node>
