<node id="Tenebrio">
  <data key="d0">Tenebrio</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Tenebrio is a beetle mentioned in the context of gastrointestinal bacteria capable of forming biofilms on polystyrene surfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio, the mealworm, is the host organism from which strain BIT-26T (Mixta tenebrionis) was isolated.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio is the genus to which both T. obscurus and T. molitor belong, studied for their gut microbiome and PS biodegradation capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio is a genus of darkling beetles whose members, including T. obscurus and T. molitor, are studied for their plastic-degrading abilities.&lt;SEP&gt;A genus of beetles, including species such as Tenebrio molitor, Tenebrio obscurus, and Tenebrio opacus.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio is an insect genus previously studied for microbial plastic degradation in its gut.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384791</data>
</node>
<node id="Bactérias do trato gastrointestinal">
  <data key="d0">Bactérias do trato gastrointestinal</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Bacteria from the gastrointestinal tract of Tenebrio are described as having the ability to generate biofilms on polystyrene surfaces, causing structural changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377491</data>
</node>
<node id="Poliestireno (PS)">
  <data key="d0">Poliestireno (PS)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Polystyrene (PS) is a material used as a surface for bacterial biofilm formation and is indicated as a possible carbon source for bacterial growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377492</data>
</node>
<node id="Microscopia eletrônica de varredura (SEM)">
  <data key="d0">Microscopia eletrônica de varredura (SEM)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Scanning Electron Microscopy (SEM) is the technique used to observe the changes caused by bacterial biofilms on polystyrene surfaces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377492</data>
