<node id="Sustainable Demolition Process">
  <data key="d0">Sustainable Demolition Process</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The sustainable demolition process refers to the proposed method of using Tenebrio molitor mealworms to remove EPS from brickwork debris.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f0582a5d7e55961a1ce4d971d3e4a8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377614</data>
</node>
<node id="Traditional Demolition Process">
  <data key="d0">Traditional Demolition Process</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The traditional demolition process for brick-and-mortar buildings involves using ordinary diggers to destroy walls, producing mixed debris that is difficult to recycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e3f0582a5d7e55961a1ce4d971d3e4a8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377614</data>
