<node id="White EPS">
  <data key="d0">White EPS</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">White EPS is a type of expanded polystyrene tested in the study, which left some residue on mortar surfaces and had stronger effects on larvae mortality.&lt;SEP&gt;White EPS is a type of expanded polystyrene foam tested in the biodegradation process using Tenebrio molitor larvae. It has higher material density and showed slightly weaker consumption dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399</data>
