<node id="Grey EPS">
  <data key="d0">Grey EPS</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Grey EPS is a type of expanded polystyrene tested in the study, which was fully removed by larvae and produced frass with higher phosphorus content and more chemical modifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Grey EPS is a type of expanded polystyrene foam with graphite content, tested in the biodegradation process using Tenebrio molitor larvae. It showed faster consumption compared to white EPS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399</data>
