<node id="Mortality">
  <data key="d0">Mortality</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mortality refers to the death rate of Tenebrio molitor larvae during the experiment, measured and analyzed as part of the results.&lt;SEP&gt;Mortality refers to the death rate of Tenebrio molitor larvae during the EPS biodegradation process, inversely correlated with larvae weight and chemical modifications of frass.&lt;SEP&gt;Mortality is a biological parameter measured in the study, with higher mortality observed in larvae fed with non-optimal feeds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9</data>
