<node id="Polyethylene Regranulate (PE-reg)">
  <data key="d0">Polyethylene Regranulate (PE-reg)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Polyethylene regranulate, referred to as PE-reg, was a polyethylene-based diet that supported rapid development of mealworm larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377807</data>
</node>
<node id="Cardboard Diet">
  <data key="d0">Cardboard Diet</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The cardboard diet consisted of shredded packaging cardboard with a density of approximately 0.36 g/cm³.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-246606838d14d58d03d733b6250a0460</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377807</data>
</node>
<node id="Polyethylene Diets (PE-oxo, PE-reg)">
  <data key="d0">Polyethylene Diets (PE-oxo, PE-reg)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The polyethylene diets consisted of polyethylene with a density of approximately 0.92 g/cm³. PE-oxo contained ~1% starch as an additive, while PE-reg contained ~2% CaO and CaCO₃-based pigments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-246606838d14d58d03d733b6250a0460</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377807</data>
</node>
<node id="Polystyrene Diet (PS)">
  <data key="d0">Polystyrene Diet (PS)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The polystyrene diet consisted of shredded white styrofoam used for packaging, with a density of approximately 0.02 g/cm³.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-246606838d14d58d03d733b6250a0460</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377808</data>
