  <data key="d0">Benzene molecules</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Benzene molecules are chemical structures within polystyrene whose double bond stretching was affected during digestion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377852</data>
</node>
<node id="Engel et al. (2013)">
  <data key="d0">Engel et al. (2013)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Engel et al. are cited researchers who reviewed the digestive system microbiome and nitrogen cycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377852</data>
</node>
<node id="Bar-Shmuel et al. (2020)">
  <data key="d0">Bar-Shmuel et al. (2020)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Bar-Shmuel et al. are cited researchers who contributed to the review of gut microbiome in insects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377853</data>
</node>
<node id="Delmont et al. (2018)">
  <data key="d0">Delmont et al. (2018)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Delmont et al. are cited researchers who described mechanisms of N-fixation and ammonia oxidation in Planctomycetes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377853</data>
</node>
<node id="Lücker et al. (2010)">
  <data key="d0">Lücker et al. (2010)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lücker et al. are cited researchers who studied Nitrosira, suggesting a mixotrophic lifestyle with CO2 assimilation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377853</data>
</node>
<node id="CEL group">
  <data key="d0">CEL group</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">CEL group is a diet group characterized by high levels of urease subunit alpha (ureC), MUFAs, SFAs, fatty acids, and unique features such as C4 esterase activity, acetoin production, and adipic acid take-up.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377853</data>
</node>
<node id="OAT group">
  <data key="d0">OAT group</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">OAT group is a diet group with high levels of urease subunit alpha (ureC), MUFAs, SFAs, and fatty acids, especially MUFAs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377853</data>
</node>
<node id="PS group">
  <data key="d0">PS group</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PS group is a polystyrene-based diet group associated with high amoA abundance, increased nitrification, higher protein content, lower larval mass, and microbiome features such as Nitrosomonadales, Nitrospirales, Planctomycetes, and α-linoleic acid.&lt;SEP&gt;PS is one of the experimental groups analyzed in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;The PS group refers to mealworms fed with plastic (PS) diet, used to study gut microbiota and gene expression changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ac5b96e63e6f5e34fe841f690d9f78ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756379127</data>
</node>
<node id="PE diets">
  <data key="d0">PE diets</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PE diets are polyethylene-based diet groups characterized by high nifH and nirS gene abundance, high fractions of Entomoplasmatales, Enterobacteriales, Rhizobiales, and unique metabolic capacities such as phenylacetic acid and D-sorbitol consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;PE diets refer to polyethylene-based diets tested in the study, which varied in their effects on T. molitor development.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377853</data>
</node>
<node id="Plastic-based diets">
  <data key="d0">Plastic-based diets</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Plastic-based diets include PS and PE diets, characterized by high content of fungi, bacteria, nosZ, protozoa, Lactobacillus spp., PUFAs, and shared metabolic traits such as tryptophan deaminase activity and glucose uptake.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377853</data>
</node>
<node id="Lactobacillus spp.">
  <data key="d0">Lactobacillus spp.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Lactobacillus spp. are bacteria found in plastic-based diets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377854</data>
</node>
<node id="Nitrosira (N. defluvii)">
  <data key="d0">Nitrosira (N. defluvii)</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitrosira (N. defluvii) is a bacterium found in T. molitor gut, associated with mixotrophic lifestyle and CO2 assimilation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377855</data>
</node>
<node id="ureC gene">
  <data key="d0">ureC gene</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The ureC gene encodes urease subunit alpha and was found in high levels in CEL and OAT groups, indicating bacteria capable of decomposing urea.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377855</data>
</node>
<node id="nosZ gene">
  <data key="d0">nosZ gene</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The nosZ gene encodes nitrous oxide reductase, associated with denitrification and found in high abundance in plastic-based diets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377855</data>
</node>
<node id="nifH gene">
  <data key="d0">nifH gene</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The nifH gene encodes nitrogenase reductase, found in high abundance in polyethylene-based diets.&lt;SEP&gt;The nifH gene encodes dinitrogen reductase and is genetically conserved, used as a marker for detecting nitrogen-fixing bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;The nifH gene is a genetic marker used to confirm nitrogen-fixing ability in bacterial isolates from mealworm guts.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385966</data>
</node>
<node id="nirS gene">
  <data key="d0">nirS gene</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The nirS gene encodes nitrite reductase, found in high abundance in PE-reg and PE-oxo diets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377856</data>
</node>
<node id="nifS gene">
  <data key="d0">nifS gene</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The nifS gene is associated with nitrogen metabolism and was found in polyethylene-based diets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377856</data>
</node>
<node id="GC-TOF-MS method">
  <data key="d0">GC-TOF-MS method</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">GC-TOF-MS is an analytical method used to analyze lipophilic and polar fractions in frass to determine polystyrene degradation potential.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377856</data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-traits group">
  <data key="d0">Multi-traits group</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A group of multi-traits characterized by high abundance of Nitrosomonadales, Nitrospirales, Planctomycetales, and α-linoleic acid, linked to the PS diet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377856</data>
</node>
