<node id="PS variant">
  <data key="d0">PS variant</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The PS variant is a diet strategy where T. molitor maintained body mass and prolonged generation length.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377861</data>
</node>
<node id="Control variant">
  <data key="d0">Control variant</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The control variant diet preserved the reproductive cycle of T. molitor, allowing rapid pupation under conditions closest to the natural environment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377861</data>
</node>
<node id="PE-reg substrate">
  <data key="d0">PE-reg substrate</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The PE-reg substrate is a polyethylene-based diet variant where a significant number of T. molitor pupae formed, focusing on producing the next generation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377861</data>
</node>
<node id="Oxo-degradable polyethylene">
  <data key="d0">Oxo-degradable polyethylene</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Oxo-degradable polyethylene is a polymer structure that, when degraded in the insect digestive system, may form toxic compounds.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756377861</data>
</node>
<node id="Insect bioindicators">
