<node id="Digestive Enzymes">
  <data key="d0">Digestive Enzymes</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Digestive enzymes in Tenebrio molitor larvae that were up-regulated after feeding on polypropylene depending on molecular weight.&lt;SEP&gt;Digestive enzymes in larvae contribute to polymer depolymerization, working synergistically with gut microbes.&lt;SEP&gt;Digestive enzymes are biological molecules required for breaking down nutrients, and their production in mealworms is negatively affected by a plastic-only diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Digestive enzymes in mealworms aid in the biodegradation of ingested plastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173</data>
