  <data key="d2">Lachnatalea sp. is a bacterial genus dominant in all PP-fed groups and has potential for degrading natural organic polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Lachnatalea sp. is a bacterial genus found in PET-fed groups of T. molitor larvae, showing high abundance and potential for polymer degradation.</data>
