  <data key="d2">Cronobacter sp. is a bacterial genus associated with plastic degradation or nitrogen fixation in T. molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Cronobacter sp. is a bacterial genus dominant in the control group gut microbiota of T. molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Cronobacter sp. is a bacterial genus identified as a majority member of the mealworm gut microbiome across all diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Cronobacter sp. is a bacterial species from the Gammaproteobacteria class identified as overrepresented in PS samples.</data>
