  <data key="d1">organism</data>
  <data key="d2">Pediococcus sp. was correlated with PP-H-fed larvae and is associated with organic acid production during fermentation, potentially linked to PP degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Pediococcus sp. is a bacterial genus associated with the production of organic acids from water-soluble carbohydrates during the fermentation of whole-plant corn silage and is correlated with PP degradation intermediates.</data>
