<node id="Waxworms (Galleria mellonella)">
  <data key="d0">Waxworms (Galleria mellonella)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Waxworms, larvae of the wax moth Galleria mellonella, are studied for their ability to biodegrade polystyrene and polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Waxworms are insects reported to be capable of degrading PS, with their gut microbiome contributing to plastic biodegradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93</data>
