<node id="Polyethylene Biodegradation">
  <data key="d0">Polyethylene Biodegradation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Polyethylene biodegradation is studied in insect larvae such as mealworms and waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene biodegradation is the process of breaking down polyethylene by biological organisms.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of polyethylene breakdown by mealworms via gut microbe-independent depolymerization.</data>
