<node id="Nitrogen Fixation">
  <data key="d0">Nitrogen Fixation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Nitrogen fixation is a biological process studied in insects and microbial communities.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen fixation is a microbial function that was diminished in larvae gut flora when LDPE foam was supplemented with traditional diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen fixation functions were stimulated in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio larvae during polyethylene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen fixation is the process of converting atmospheric nitrogen into biologically usable forms, demonstrated within plastic-eating mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen fixation is a biological process studied in the context of mealworm gut microbiota.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc</data>
