<node id="Lipases">
  <data key="d0">Lipases</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Lipases are enzymes used for sustainable synthesis and degradation of polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipases are enzymes investigated for their ability to degrade polyurethane bonds.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipases are enzymes measured in the gut of mealworms that can break down specific bonds in polyurethane molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipases are enzymes measured in the mealworm gut, associated with PU hydrolysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrolase enzymes identified in transcriptomic analysis, related to lignocellulose and PS degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipases are extracellular enzymes tested for activity against NPS-grown bacteria using Tween 80 as substrate.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipases are enzymes produced by Achromobacter species, involved in hydrolyzing fats.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01bf9080cbf55e62c0b26d0e054bd1fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26138366e1d9310732edc569ba338bfe</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381121</data>
</node>
