  <data key="d2">Wood-feeding beetles rely on nitrogen-fixing bacteria to supplement nitrogen supply when feeding on low-nitrogen diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen-fixing bacteria are microorganisms in the gut of larvae that provide nitrogen through nitrogen fixation, though the amount is limited compared to normal feed.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen-fixing bacteria are microbes capable of fixing atmospheric nitrogen, found in the gut of Styrofoam-eating mealworms.</data>
