<node id="Bacterial Consortium">
  <data key="d0">Bacterial Consortium</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A group of bacteria isolated from soil capable of degrading polyurethane.&lt;SEP&gt;A bacterial consortium is a group of bacteria that collectively degraded low molecular weight PE wax with a mass reduction of 31.5% in 21 days.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of bacteria enriched from the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae, studied for degradation of polyvinyl chloride.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
