<node id="Tenebrio molitor larvae (yellow mealworms)">
  <data key="d0">Tenebrio molitor larvae (yellow mealworms)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Tenebrio molitor larvae, also known as yellow mealworms, belong to the darkling beetle family (Coleoptera: Tenebrionidae). They are commercially available as animal feed and are capable of biodegrading a wide variety of petroleum-based plastics (PS, PE, PVC, PUR) and biodegradable polymers (PLA, PBAT). They are used as a model insect species for investigating plastic biodegradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756378846</data>
