  <data key="d0">PBAT</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Poly(butylene adipate-co-terephthalate) (PBAT) is a biodegradable polymer that Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade and assimilate for energy.&lt;SEP&gt;PBAT (polybutylene adipate terephthalate) was mentioned as a biodegradable polymer suggested for future testing.&lt;SEP&gt;PBAT (polybutylene adipate terephthalate) is a biodegradable plastic studied for its effects on bacterial communities in soil.&lt;SEP&gt;PBAT is a degradable plastic mentioned as a subject for future biodegradation research.</data>
