<node id="Residual Polymers">
  <data key="d0">Residual Polymers</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Residual polymers refer to the remaining plastic particles in larvae frass after biodegradation, with size distribution measured.&lt;SEP&gt;Residual polymers are the remaining plastic materials after mealworm digestion, analyzed for chemical modifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Residual polymers refer to the remaining polymer material found in the frass of larvae after partial depolymerization and biodegradation of plastics such as LLDPE, HDPE, and LDPE.&lt;SEP&gt;Residual polymers are the remaining plastic materials after digestion by yellow mealworms, analyzed to assess biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Residual polymers with heterogeneous molecular weight distribution are the final products after depolymerization.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7a93f0b3dbebad30b6aeabec429a40</data>
