<node id="Dysbiosis">
  <data key="d0">Dysbiosis</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Dysbiosis was observed in PVC-fed larvae, indicating microbial imbalance associated with oxidative stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756378869</data>
</node>
<node id="Biomass depletion">
  <data key="d0">Biomass depletion</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Biomass depletion was one of the negative physiological responses in Tenebrio molitor larvae after ingestion of microplastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756378869</data>
</node>
<node id="Weight loss">
  <data key="d0">Weight loss</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Weight loss was observed in Tenebrio molitor larvae as a negative physiological response to microplastic ingestion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756378870</data>
</node>
<node id="Decreased survival rates">
  <data key="d0">Decreased survival rates</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Decreased survival rates were observed in Tenebrio molitor larvae fed with microplastics, varying with polymer biodegradability.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756378870</data>
</node>
<node id="Biofragmentation">
  <data key="d0">Biofragmentation</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Biofragmentation of ingested microplastics occurred in larvae, but residual particles remained at micrometer size.&lt;SEP&gt;Biofragmentation refers to the biological process of breaking down plastics into smaller fragments, often studied in macroinvertebrates.&lt;SEP&gt;Biofragmentation refers to the process by which organisms break down plastic waste into smaller particles, such as micro- and nano-plastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387401</data>
</node>
<node id="Circular approach for PLA waste management">
