  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Serratia sp. is a bacterial genus identified in the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor larvae, associated with degradation of polystyrene and corn straw.&lt;SEP&gt;Serratia sp. is a bacterial strain studied in relation to polystyrene degradation in Tenebrio molitor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
