<node id="CS">
  <data key="d0">CS</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">CS was one of the feedstocks provided to larvae, both antibiotic-treated and untreated.&lt;SEP&gt;CS refers to another plastic material tested for degradation in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;CS is another plastic material studied for degradation by larvae, with different degradation characteristics compared to PS.&lt;SEP&gt;CS refers to a type of diet or polymer fed to larvae, associated with cellulose or lignocellulose degradation metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;CS (cellulose/lignocellulose) is a polymer whose degradation involves lignin, hemicellulose, and cellulose breakdown into glucose or xylose.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5b96e63e6f5e34fe841f690d9f78ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756379116</data>
</node>
