<node id="Lac640">
  <data key="d0">Lac640</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Lac640 is a laccase enzyme identified as highly upregulated in PS- and CS-fed groups, expressed in E. coli Rosetta (DE3), and tested for its ability to degrade plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Lac640 is a treatment applied to PS/CS samples, and its effects on surface morphology and functional groups were analyzed using FTIR and SEM.&lt;SEP&gt;An enzyme whose expression was upregulated in PS- and CS-fed groups, two times higher than other enzymes, involved in oxidation of PS and lignin.&lt;SEP&gt;Lac640 is a gene encoding LMCOs (laccase-like multicopper oxidases), highly upregulated in PS- and CS-fed larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Lac640 is a protein analyzed in the study, including phylogenetic tree, SDS-PAGE, enzyme activity, and kinetic analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5b96e63e6f5e34fe841f690d9f78ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756379124</data>
</node>
