<node id="Yellow mealworm">
  <data key="d0">Yellow mealworm</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Larvae of Tenebrio molitor Linnaeus, studied for biodegradation of plastics and production of biochar from frass.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworm is an insect whose gut hosts microorganisms, including WJ2020 and WJ2025, that can degrade PS films. It can feed on EPS but does not gain sufficient nutrients from it.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworm (Tenebrio molitor L.) is studied for microbial community changes in artificial ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworm, the larva of Tenebrio molitor Linnaeus 1758, is a macroinvertebrate with high plastic-degrading ability, capable of ingesting and biodegrading various petroleum-based plastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-db579d338d8f90574e3ac67a3ae9938d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aac53ba8b358857c4dcd3b6cd9e8991&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3</data>
