<node id="Landfill">
  <data key="d0">Landfill</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Landfill is the primary disposal method for waste plastics, accounting for 72% of disposal.&lt;SEP&gt;Landfill is mentioned as an environmental source where microorganisms have been studied for their ability to biodegrade polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Landfill is a traditional disposal method for plastic waste, contributing to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Landfill is an environmental source containing microbial communities used in PE biodegradation research.&lt;SEP&gt;Landfill is a traditional method of disposing of waste plastic, but it cannot fundamentally solve environmental pollution.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568</data>
