<node id="Pyralidae">
  <data key="d0">Pyralidae</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pyralidae is a family of pyralid moths, discovered since 2015 to be capable of biodegrading plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Pyralidae is a moth family that includes species such as Galleria mellonella, which are studied for plastic biodegradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf</data>
