<node id="PET (Polyethylene Terephthalate)">
  <data key="d0">PET (Polyethylene Terephthalate)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PET is a type of plastic polymer studied for biodegradation by insects such as T. molitor. Different molecular weights (low, medium, high) were tested.&lt;SEP&gt;PET (polyethylene terephthalate) is a common plastic mentioned as a potential target for future biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene terephthalate (PET) is a plastic that has been more extensively studied for biodegradation compared to PP.&lt;SEP&gt;PET is a plastic polymer hypothesized to be degradable by Tenebrio genus beetles.&lt;SEP&gt;PET is a type of plastic mentioned as a potential target for future biodegradation studies with Tenebrio obscurus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8c5ce99d234a2ac272a8b4b8135e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748</data>
