  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibiotic suppression refers to the experimental condition where gut microbes are inhibited, affecting the biodegradation of plastics such as PS and PVC.&lt;SEP&gt;Antibiotic suppression refers to the inhibition of gut microbes using antibiotics, which reduced PP depolymerization in the larvae.</data>
