<node id="PS foam">
  <data key="d0">PS foam</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PS foam (polystyrene foam) is another type of plastic mentioned as feed for larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;PS foam (polystyrene foam) is used as feed for mealworms in the study, but it results in lower growth, development, and reproduction compared to standard diets.&lt;SEP&gt;PS foam refers to polystyrene foam, a type of plastic tested in both pristine and aged conditions for ingestion by T. molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;PS foam (polystyrene foam) is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by insect larvae such as T. molitor and T. obscurus.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene (PS) foam was one of the plastics ingested by mealworms in the experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69</data>
