<node id="Lepidoptera">
  <data key="d0">Lepidoptera</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Lepidoptera is an insect order that includes Pyralidae moths, which are studied for their ability to biodegrade polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Lepidoptera is one of the insect orders represented in the study, with Greater Wax Moth (WM) as its candidate species.&lt;SEP&gt;Lepidoptera is an order of insects whose larvae have been studied for their ability to degrade polystyrene styrofoam with the help of gut microorganisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Lepidoptera is an order of insects whose larvae have been reported to feed on EPS.&lt;SEP&gt;Lepidoptera is an insect order, some species of which have been identified as capable of degrading polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Lepidoptera are insects observed to consume plastics and decompose them in vivo.&lt;SEP&gt;Lepidoptera are insects observed consuming and decomposing plastics in vivo.</data>
