  <data key="d0">Carbonyl Index (CI)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Carbonyl Index (CI) is a measurement used to characterize the oxidative degradation of polyethylene polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonyl Index (CI) values were measured from FTIR spectra peaks of PE and frass samples to quantify chemical modifications and biodegradation levels.&lt;SEP&gt;The Carbonyl Index (CI) is an aging index representing oxygen-containing groups on aged MPs, correlated with microbial growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonyl Index (CI) is an abbreviation used in the study as a measure related to microplastic aging.</data>
