  <data key="d2">WCA refers to water contact angles, one of the variables analyzed.&lt;SEP&gt;WCA refers to water contact angle measurement, an analytical method used to study PS film surface changes after inoculation with bacterial strains.&lt;SEP&gt;WCA (Water Contact Angle) is a measurement used to assess hydrophobicity of polyethylene microplastics before and after digestion by Tenebrio species.&lt;SEP&gt;WCA is an analytical method mentioned as part of the tests confirming oxidation and biodegradation of PP in larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385289</data>
</node>
