<node id="PE-MPs">
  <data key="d0">PE-MPs</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PE-MPs (Polyethylene Microplastics) are microplastic particles of polyethylene used as a diet for mealworm larvae, influencing gut microbiome diversity and niche width.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene microplastics (PE-MPs) were tested for their physicochemical properties (PCPs) and their impact on gut microbiomes.&lt;SEP&gt;PE-MPs (Polyethylene Microplastics) are a form of plastic powder fed to Tenebrio larvae for 21 days to study oxidative stress and degradation effects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc</data>
