<node id="Beetle">
  <data key="d0">Beetle</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The adult stage of Tenebrio molitor, which consumes EPS at a much slower rate compared to mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Beetles are organisms tested for EPS consumption. They showed negligible EPS consumption and degradation, focusing mainly on the hard outer layer of EPS cups.&lt;SEP&gt;Beetles were included in some co-culture experiments with mealworms to study EPS consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Beetles were tested for EPS consumption but were shown to be ineffective compared to mealworms.</data>
