<node id="Eggs">
  <data key="d0">Eggs</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Eggs were harvested from the beetle stock bin every 30 days and later hatched into mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Eggs were produced by larvae in the control group and in some EPS diet groups, indicating reproductive outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Eggs laid by female moths on folded wax paper, later collected and transferred to containers for hatchling development.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertilized eggs laid by female beetles, which fell through the sieve mat to the lower floor for hatching and juvenile development.&lt;SEP&gt;Eggs are the reproductive output of T. molitor, produced during the imago stage and influenced by energy allocation.</data>
