<node id="Strain YT2">
  <data key="d0">Strain YT2</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Strain YT2 is an isolated bacterial strain used in PS biodegradation assays.&lt;SEP&gt;Strain YT2 is a bacterial strain capable of forming biofilm and degrading polystyrene (PS) film, leading to surface deterioration and chemical changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Strain YT2 is a bacterial strain capable of attacking or oxidizing the PS (polystyrene) structure to produce more polar derivatives and cause weight and molecular weight loss in PS samples.</data>
