<node id="Black Soldier Fly (BSF)">
  <data key="d0">Black Soldier Fly (BSF)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Black Soldier Fly larvae were used as one of the insect models in the study to test plastic metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;BSF is an insect species studied for its potential in plastic biodegradation. It is cosmopolitan, used to upcycle organic substrates, and has limited ability to chew plastic, focusing degradation potential on enzymes.&lt;SEP&gt;Black Soldier Fly (BSF) is one of the insect species used in the plastic-insect exposure study.&lt;SEP&gt;Black Soldier Fly (BSF) is an insect model used in experiments to study metabolic responses to plastic substrates and supplements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756380842</data>
</node>
<node id="Mealworm (MW)">
  <data key="d0">Mealworm (MW)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mealworm larvae were used as one of the insect models in the study to test plastic metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;MW is an insect species widely investigated as a larval model for plastic biodegradation and micro- and nanoplastic toxicity. Its frass has potential as an organic fertilizer in sustainable agriculture.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworm (MW) is one of the insect species used in the plastic-insect exposure study, reared on wheat bran, carrot, and sweet potato.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworm (MW) is an insect model used in experiments to study metabolic responses to plastic substrates and supplements.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
