<node id="Central Carbon Metabolism (CCM)">
  <data key="d0">Central Carbon Metabolism (CCM)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Central Carbon Metabolism refers to the suite of compounds and pathways analyzed in the study to measure insect metabolic responses to plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;CCM refers to a suite of metabolites and pathways central to cellular metabolism, involved in biosynthetic and metabolic processes, nutrient availability, and physiological requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;CCM refers to the metabolic pathways studied in insect larvae to assess the impact of plastic exposure.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
