<node id="Pseudomonas sp M7">
  <data key="d0">Pseudomonas sp M7</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Pseudomonas sp M7 is a bacterial isolate characterized by rough, wrinkled, creamy colonies. It showed enzymatic activity including cellulase, esterase, catalase, and oxidase.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas sp M7 (PP12656) is a microbial strain identified as a potential NPS degrader, showing 5% reduction in PS film weight.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas sp M7 is a bacterial strain isolated from yellow mealworms and identified as capable of degrading polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas sp M7 is a bacterial strain isolated from the intestines of yellow mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3196d2d200ebf060e966a565b5eb26de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26138366e1d9310732edc569ba338bfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381134</data>
</node>
