  <data key="d0">Achromobacter sp. HZ01</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Achromobacter sp. HZ01 is a bacterial strain isolated from crude oil-contaminated seawater. It demonstrated high degradability of total n-alkanes (up to 96.6%) and could utilize polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs) as its sole carbon source.&lt;SEP&gt;A novel hydrocarbon-degrading bacterium isolated from crude oil-contaminated seawater.</data>
