<node id="Pseudomonas nitroreducens">
  <data key="d0">Pseudomonas nitroreducens</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Pseudomonas nitroreducens is a microorganism isolated from Tenebrio molitor, tested on NPS and PS film for 60 days, showing 6.93% biodegradation/weight loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas nitroreducens is one of the bacterial species isolated from mealworms that can degrade polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas nitroreducens is a bacterial strain, with 7 strains identified, 1 of which was tested for EPS degradation. Growth was lower in LB medium compared to TYE medium, indicating salt sensitivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041</data>
