<node id="Masilia sp. FS1903">
  <data key="d0">Masilia sp. FS1903</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Masilia sp. FS1903 is a microorganism isolated from Tenebrio molitor, tested on PS film for 15 days under anaerobic conditions, showing 2.76% biodegradation/weight loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Masilia sp. FS1903 is a PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the intestines of the greater wax moth larvae (Galleria mellonella), capable of degrading PS by 12.97% after 30 days.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfcb17715cb4e5148b33061c1b6cbf1c</data>
