<node id="E. coli K12">
  <data key="d0">E. coli K12</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">E. coli K12 is a bacterial strain used as a control in the experiments to test whether observed chemical modifications in plastics were due to microbial contamination. No new peaks were observed in plastics incubated with E. coli K12.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381388</data>
</node>
<node id="Putative Gas Fraction (PGF)">
  <data key="d0">Putative Gas Fraction (PGF)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Putative Gas Fraction (PGF) represents the fraction of mass balance unaccounted for in the solid and biomass outputs, suggesting mineralization of plastics into gaseous products.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381388</data>
</node>
<node id="32-day Experiment">
  <data key="d0">32-day Experiment</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The 32-day experiment involved feeding mealworms with plastics (PE, PS) and bran, measuring depolymerization, chemical modifications, biomass changes, and putative gas fraction.&lt;SEP&gt;An experiment lasting 32 days tested mealworm viability and plastic consumption with PS and bran diets.&lt;SEP&gt;The 32-day experiment measured survival rates, PS consumption, and weight gain of mealworms under different feeding and temperature conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756383770</data>
</node>
<node id="NMR Analysis">
  <data key="d0">NMR Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">NMR analysis was used to examine chemical modifications in residual polymers, revealing new peaks associated with alkene bonds and oxygen incorporation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381388</data>
</node>
<node id="Control PE">
  <data key="d0">Control PE</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Control PE refers to polyethylene samples not fed to mealworms, used as a baseline for comparison in chemical analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381389</data>
</node>
<node id="Frass-fed Mealworms">
  <data key="d0">Frass-fed Mealworms</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mealworms fed only bran produced frass that was analyzed as a control to confirm that observed peaks were not due to contamination.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381389</data>
</node>
<node id="Mass Balance">
  <data key="d0">Mass Balance</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mass balance was used to measure system inputs, outputs, and biomass changes in mealworms to assess mineralization of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass balance was used to monitor the removal and digestion of PS and PE plastics by mealworms, based on frass and residual plastic contents.&lt;SEP&gt;Mass balance refers to the estimation of PS removal based on the mass of ingested PS, egested frass, and extracted fractions (Cw, Ce, Cc).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387679</data>
</node>
