  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Indian mealmoth is an insect species from which Enterobacter absuriae YTI was isolated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381390</data>
</node>
<node id="Article">
  <data key="d0">Article</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The scientific article published in Environmental Science &amp; Technology reporting on mealworm plastic degradation and gut microbiome analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;The article presents experimental results on the physiological response of mealworms to polystyrene microplastics and their biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The published research article in Environmental Science &amp; Technology reporting on the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e</data>
