<node id="Benzene Ring">
  <data key="d0">Benzene Ring</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The benzene ring is a chemical structure in polystyrene that was observed to be cleaved during degradation in larvae guts.&lt;SEP&gt;The benzene ring structure of PS showed dampened peaks in FTIR analysis, suggesting ring cleavage during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The benzene ring is a chemical structure in polystyrene that was destroyed by yellow mealworm gut microbes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa</data>
