<node id="Mixta tenebrionis sp. nov.">
  <data key="d0">Mixta tenebrionis sp. nov.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixta tenebrionis sp. nov. is a newly proposed bacterial species isolated from the gut of the plastic-eating mealworm Tenebrio molitor L. The type strain is BIT-26T (=CGMCC 1.17041T = KCTC 72449T).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381784</data>
</node>
<node id="BIT-26T">
  <data key="d0">BIT-26T</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">BIT-26T is the type strain of Mixta tenebrionis sp. nov., isolated from the gut of a plastic-eating mealworm in Beijing, PR China.&lt;SEP&gt;BIT-26T is a bacterial strain studied for its genome, fatty acid composition, and physiological properties. It was confirmed to represent a novel species in the genus Mixta.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381784</data>
</node>
<node id="Beijing, PR China">
  <data key="d0">Beijing, PR China</data>
  <data key="d1">geo</data>
  <data key="d2">Beijing, PR China is the location where the plastic-eating mealworm from which strain BIT-26T was isolated was found.&lt;SEP&gt;Beijing, PR China is the location where the mealworm strain BIT-26T was studied.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381784</data>
</node>
