<node id="Mixta">
  <data key="d0">Mixta</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixta is a bacterial genus within the family Erwiniaeae, established in 2018 by reclassifying four species from the genus Pantoea. It includes species such as Mixta calida, Mixta gaviniae, Mixta intestinalis, and Mixta theicola.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixta is a bacterial genus. Strain BIT-26T was compared with species in this genus and confirmed as a novel species within it.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixta is a bacterial genus. Strain BIT-26T corresponds to this genus and is compared with other Mixta species.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixta is a newly proposed bacterial genus within the family Erwiniaeae.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixta is a bacterial genus identified as a nitrogen-fixing gut bacterium in mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385994</data>
</node>
<node id="Erwiniaeae">
  <data key="d0">Erwiniaeae</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Erwiniaeae is a bacterial family within the order Enterobacteriales, containing 14 genera including Mixta.&lt;SEP&gt;Erwiniaeae is a newly proposed bacterial family within the order Enterobacteriales.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
