<node id="Strain BIT-26T">
  <data key="d0">Strain BIT-26T</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Strain BIT-26T is a bacterial strain isolated from mealworm in Beijing, PR China, characterized through a polyphasic taxonomic study and proposed as a novel species of the genus Mixta.&lt;SEP&gt;Strain BIT-26T is a Gram-stain-negative, facultatively anaerobic, motile rod-shaped bacterium with peritrichous flagella. It grows at 12–41 °C, pH 4.5–9.0, and tolerates 0–7.5% NaCl. It has unique biochemical and fatty acid characteristics that distinguish it from related species.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756381793</data>
</node>
