<node id="Mixta tenebrionis">
  <data key="d0">Mixta tenebrionis</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixta tenebrionis is a species of the genus Mixta, represented by strain BIT-26, included in phylogenetic analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixta tenebrionis is the proposed novel species name for strain BIT-26T, isolated from the mealworm Tenebrio.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixta tenebrionis is a bacterial species. It is Gram-stain-negative, facultatively anaerobic, motile with peritrichous flagella, and forms yellow colonies on LB agar. It grows in a wide range of temperatures, pH, and salt concentrations, and has specific biochemical characteristics including catalase activity and sugar utilization profiles. The type strain is BIT-26T.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4</data>
