  <data key="d0">Acid Production from Carbohydrates</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Acid production from carbohydrates refers to the ability of bacterial strains to metabolize sugars such as d-sorbitol, amygdalin, salicin, cellobiose, lactose, sucrose, raffinose, d-arabinol, d-fucose, gluconate, 2-keto-gluconate, and 5-keto-gluconate.</data>
