  <data key="d0">Standard Diet (fermented cassava yeasts)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The standard diet used in the experiment consisted of fermented cassava yeasts, serving as the control feed for mealworms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382395</data>
</node>
<node id="Larval Stage">
  <data key="d0">Larval Stage</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The larval stage refers to the developmental phase of mealworms before entering the prepupal stage. It was measured for growth and survival in the experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;The larval stage is the developmental stage of the waxworm where it prefers to eat and is the focus of feeding experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2303f3680e9313daac77bb7e27e7da</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382975</data>
</node>
<node id="Prepupal Period">
  <data key="d0">Prepupal Period</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The prepupal period is defined as the nonfeeding-wandering stage of mealworms before pupation. It was measured as part of the experiment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382395</data>
</node>
<node id="Pupation Period">
  <data key="d0">Pupation Period</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The pupation period is defined as the stage when the prepupa becomes immobile and encloses itself in a pupal case. It was measured in the experiment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382395</data>
</node>
<node id="Pupal Weight">
  <data key="d0">Pupal Weight</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Pupal weight refers to the measured weight of mealworms during the pupal stage, used as a growth parameter in the experiment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382395</data>
</node>
<node id="Imago Weight">
  <data key="d0">Imago Weight</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Imago weight refers to the measured weight of newly emerged adult beetles (imago) from pupae, used as a parameter in the experiment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382395</data>
</node>
<node id="Fecundity">
  <data key="d0">Fecundity</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Fecundity refers to the reproductive capacity of mealworms, measured by the number of eggs laid by females after mating.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382395</data>
</node>
<node id="Egg Production">
  <data key="d0">Egg Production</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Egg production refers to the number of eggs laid by female mealworms within ten days after mating, measured as part of fecundity.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382395</data>
