<node id="XPS foam">
  <data key="d0">XPS foam</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">XPS foam is another type of polystyrene foam feed given to mealworms, showing the worst results in terms of larval, pupal, and imago weight.&lt;SEP&gt;XPS foam is a type of polystyrene foam that provides less productivity in mealworms compared to EPS foam.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382397</data>
</node>
<node id="Yeast">
  <data key="d0">Yeast</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Yeast is used as a standard diet for mealworms, providing essential nutrients such as B vitamins, proteins, trace metals, amino acids, and nitrogen, resulting in better growth and reproduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Yeast is identified as the factor mediating attraction, oviposition, and development in Drosophila melanogaster.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382398</data>
</node>
