  <data key="d0">Polystyrene Foam</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Polystyrene foam is the specific form of polystyrene fed to mealworms during experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene foam was tested as a feed for Tenebrio molitor larvae, leading to high larval mortality but demonstrating biodegradation potential.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene foam is a type of feed used in the experiment to rear Tenebrio molitor larvae, also linked to biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene foam was used as a feed in the experiment, resulting in high mortality of mealworms due to its almost zero nutritional value.</data>
