  <data key="d0">Lesser Waxworm</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The lesser waxworm is the larval organism studied for its ability to degrade polyethylene (PE) and survive on different diets.&lt;SEP&gt;The lesser waxworm is the larval stage insect studied for its ability to consume and degrade polyethylene (PE) and waxcomb (WC).&lt;SEP&gt;The lesser waxworm, identified as Achroia grisella, was used in experiments to test its ability to degrade polyethylene (PE) and waxcomb (WC).</data>
