<node id="A. grisella larvae">
  <data key="d0">A. grisella larvae</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">A. grisella larvae are organisms that naturally evolved to eat and digest beeswax, which has chemical bonds similar to polyethylene (PE). They may also possess PE-degrading gut bacteria or unique extracellular enzymes that contribute to plastic digestion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382983</data>
</node>
<node id="Indian meal moth larvae">
  <data key="d0">Indian meal moth larvae</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">The larvae of the Indian meal moth are reported to contain PE-degrading bacteria in their digestive tract.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382983</data>
</node>
<node id="Lesser waxworms">
  <data key="d0">Lesser waxworms</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Lesser waxworms are insects that can feed on both waxcomb (WC) and polyethylene (PE), completing their life cycle under both diets, though with differences in growth, biomass gain, and survival rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382984</data>
</node>
<node id="Honey bees">
  <data key="d0">Honey bees</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Honey bees produce beeswax to construct waxcomb for raising larvae and storing honey and pollen.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382984</data>
</node>
<node id="Cannibalism in waxworms">
  <data key="d0">Cannibalism in waxworms</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">Cannibalism was observed among PE-fed lesser waxworms when there was a shortage of food or essential nutrients, contributing to reduced survival rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756382984</data>
</node>
