</node>
<node id="Lesser Waxworms">
  <data key="d0">Lesser Waxworms</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Lesser waxworms are larvae studied for their ability to consume and biodegrade polyethylene (PE) and waxcomb (WC). They were fed different diets including PE, WC, and PE-WC co-feed, and their frass and life cycle were analyzed.&lt;SEP&gt;Lesser waxworms are insects studied for their ability to consume and degrade polyethylene (PE). They were fed PE and PE with additional nutrition (WC) to assess survival and biodegradation rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26</data>
