<node id="Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor L.)">
  <data key="d0">Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor L.)</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Mealworms are studied for their growth and transcriptomic response when fed plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor L.), also known as yellow mealworms or meal moths, are insect larvae capable of ingesting and biodegrading various plastics (PE, PS, PVC, PLA, PBAT). They depolymerize, assimilate, and mineralize plastics in their gut microenvironments, making them highly efficient plastic-degrading macroinvertebrates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7768b61a3d166f2cd01d4e87ac88cd</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387401</data>
</node>
