<node id="Redundancy Analysis (RDA)">
  <data key="d0">Redundancy Analysis (RDA)</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">RDA is a statistical method used in the study to evaluate correlations between survival rate, PS consumption, and environmental factors.&lt;SEP&gt;Redundancy Analysis (RDA) was performed, indicating that PS density, Mₙ, and Mₓ explained 99.8% of the variation in PS consumption and specific consumption rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Redundancy Analysis (RDA) was used in the study to identify relationships between aging indexes and microbial communities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28</data>
