  <data key="d0">Variation Partitioning Analysis (VPA)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">VPA is a statistical method based on partial RDA used in the study to partition variation in data.&lt;SEP&gt;Variation Partitioning Analysis (VPA) based on partial RDA revealed the contributions of PS density, Mₙ, and Mₓ to PS consumption variation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28</data>
