<node id="Unfed controls">
  <data key="d0">Unfed controls</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Unfed controls are larvae groups that were not provided with any diet during the experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;Unfed controls were used as a baseline in the gut microbial community analysis of Tenebrio larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756386523</data>
</node>
<node id="Weight change">
  <data key="d0">Weight change</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Weight change refers to the percentage change in larval weight under different feeding conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384004</data>
</node>
<node id="25 °C Test Temperature">
  <data key="d0">25 °C Test Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The feeding experiments were conducted at a controlled temperature of 25 °C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384004</data>
</node>
<node id="SPCR (Specific PS Consumption Rate)">
  <data key="d0">SPCR (Specific PS Consumption Rate)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">SPCR refers to the specific rate at which larvae consume polystyrene (PS), measured over different time intervals during the 31 day test.&lt;SEP&gt;SPCR is the specific consumption rate of polystyrene by mealworms, calculated as the mass of PS ingested per 100 larvae per day.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387675</data>
</node>
<node id="TER (THF Extractable Ratio)">
  <data key="d0">TER (THF Extractable Ratio)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">TER represents the fraction of residual PS polymer in egested frass, used as an indirect measure of PS degradability in the mealworm gut.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384005</data>
</node>
<node id="Mₙ (Number Average Molecular Weight)">
  <data key="d0">Mₙ (Number Average Molecular Weight)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mₙ is a molecular weight measurement used to evaluate the extent of PS depolymerization in frass samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384006</data>
</node>
<node id="Mₓ (Weight Average Molecular Weight)">
  <data key="d0">Mₓ (Weight Average Molecular Weight)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mₓ is a molecular weight measurement used to evaluate the extent of PS depolymerization in frass samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384007</data>
</node>
<node id="Volatile Organics">
  <data key="d0">Volatile Organics</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Volatile organics are compounds classified from the decomposition of frass under 100°C, possibly including gut secretions and carboxylic acid compounds from PS biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Volatile organics are compounds detected in the decomposed frass under 100°C, including gut secretions and degradation products from PP biodegradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51f749234fed052c982d79f81b93cc29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385277</data>
</node>
<node id="Carboxylic Acid Compounds">
  <data key="d0">Carboxylic Acid Compounds</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Carboxylic acid compounds are identified as products of PS biodegradation, detected in frass decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;Carboxylic acid compounds are degradation products observed in frass samples from PP biodegradation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-51f749234fed052c982d79f81b93cc29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
