<node id="Pseudomonadaceae">
  <data key="d0">Pseudomonadaceae</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Pseudomonadaceae are bacteria reported to play a role in insect gut environments, potentially contributing to polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonadaceae is a bacterial family found to be significantly more abundant in PS samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonadaceae is a bacterial family that increased to 7.68% in PP-fed groups, associated with PP degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonadaceae is one of the bacterial families classified under Gammaproteobacteria, identified in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonadaceae is one of the bacterial families within Gammaproteobacteria identified in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonadaceae is a bacterial family that accounted for 80% of the strains identified in this study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae</data>
