<node id="PS samples">
  <data key="d0">PS samples</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">PS samples refer to experimental groups where polystyrene was used as the only food source for larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;PS samples refer to samples associated with polystyrene-fed insects, used in microbial diversity and abundance analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;PS samples refer to experimental groups of A. diaperinus larvae reared on polystyrene.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384784</data>
</node>
<node id="CT samples">
  <data key="d0">CT samples</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">CT samples refer to control groups in the experiment, used for comparison with PS samples.&lt;SEP&gt;CT samples are control samples used for comparison with PS samples in microbial diversity and abundance studies.&lt;SEP&gt;CT samples refer to control groups of A. diaperinus larvae reared on vegetable food.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384784</data>
</node>
<node id="A. diaperinus">
  <data key="d0">A. diaperinus</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A. diaperinus is an insect species tested for its ability to survive on polystyrene as the only food source.&lt;SEP&gt;A. diaperinus, also known as lesser mealworm larvae, is an insect species in which Pseudomonas has been consistently found.&lt;SEP&gt;A. diaperinus is an insect whose gut microbiome was studied for microbial and fungal communities associated with plastic consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;A. diaperinus is a species of beetle whose larvae were studied for gut microbial community differences when reared on polystyrene versus vegetable food.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59453e4c878e72ac6985a08043cdf126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384784</data>
</node>
<node id="Alpha-diversity estimates">
  <data key="d0">Alpha-diversity estimates</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Alpha-diversity estimates are used to measure microbial diversity, showing that bacterial microbiota in PS samples is impoverished compared to CT samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384785</data>
</node>
<node id="Beta-diversity">
  <data key="d0">Beta-diversity</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Beta-diversity refers to differences in microbial community composition between PS and CT samples, highlighted by PCoA plots.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756384785</data>
</node>
<node id="PCoA plots">
  <data key="d0">PCoA plots</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">PCoA plots are visualizations used to compare microbial community differences between PS and CT samples.&lt;SEP&gt;PCoA plots are used to highlight differences in beta diversity between PS and CT samples, showing separation along major axes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6</data>
