<node id="Residual PP Polymer">
  <data key="d0">Residual PP Polymer</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Residual PP polymer is the extractable fraction found in larval frass, composed of non-degraded and partially degraded polypropylene.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385273</data>
</node>
<node id="Non-extractable Fraction">
  <data key="d0">Non-extractable Fraction</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The non-extractable fraction in larval frass contains solid intermediates and other undigested residues from ingested polypropylene.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385273</data>
</node>
<node id="Broad Depolymerization">
  <data key="d0">Broad Depolymerization</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Broad depolymerization is a pattern of plastic biodegradation characterized by a decrease in both Mw and Mn simultaneously.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385273</data>
</node>
<node id="Limited Extent Depolymerization">
  <data key="d0">Limited Extent Depolymerization</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Limited extent depolymerization is a pattern of plastic biodegradation characterized by an increase in Mn or in both Mw and Mn.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385273</data>
