<node id="Enterobacter hormaechei LG3">
  <data key="d0">Enterobacter hormaechei LG3</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Enterobacter hormaechei LG3 is a facultative anaerobic bacterial strain isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae (mealworms) that can oxidize and depolymerize polystyrene under anaerobic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter hormaechei LG3 is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of mealworms, capable of degrading PS under both anaerobic and aerobic conditions, showing biofilm formation and upregulation of degradative enzyme genes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385597</data>
</node>
<node id="Bacillus amyloliquefaciens SCGB1">
  <data key="d0">Bacillus amyloliquefaciens SCGB1</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Bacillus amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 is a bacterial strain used for comparison in polystyrene biodegradation studies under anaerobic and aerobic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 is a facultative gut bacterium used in experiments to confirm PS degradation by Enterobacter hormaechei LG3. It is known for its influence on gut health and ability to degrade PS and PE.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 is a bacterial strain isolated from traditional Korean soybean-fermented foods, capable of affecting intestinal health in mice and growing under anaerobic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 is another bacterial strain compared with LG3 in PS degradation experiments. It was less effective in depolymerizing PS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385599</data>
</node>
<node id="Exiguobacterium YT2">
  <data key="d0">Exiguobacterium YT2</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Exiguobacterium YT2 is a PS-degrading gut bacterium isolated in previous studies under aerobic conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385599</data>
</node>
<node id="Pseudomonas strain DSM 50071">
  <data key="d0">Pseudomonas strain DSM 50071</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Pseudomonas strain DSM 50071 is a PS-degrading bacterium isolated from the gut of Superworms (Zophobas atratus) larvae under aerobic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas strain DSM 50071 is a bacterial strain referenced in relation to PS biodegradation, with its effectiveness not yet determined.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385599</data>
</node>
<node id="Korean government">
  <data key="d0">Korean government</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Korean government banned the use of EPS buoys in territorial waters due to their role in producing polystyrene microplastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385600</data>
</node>
