  <data key="d0">LG3</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">LG3 is one of the bacterial strains isolated from mealworms and sequenced for 16 S rRNA analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;LG3 is a bacterial strain used for whole genome sequence analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;LG3 is a bacterial strain that showed effective depolymerization of oxidized polystyrene (PS) under anaerobic conditions. It was later identified as Enterobacter hormaechei and demonstrated the ability to degrade PS under both anaerobic and aerobic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;LG3 is a PS-degradable bacterium studied for its ability to biodegrade polystyrene (PS) under anaerobic conditions. It exhibits upregulation of specific enzymes, changes in physiological characteristics, and production of CO2 as an end product. It also shows biofilm formation and lipid metabolism changes when treated with Mi-PS.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-237dcdbb783e27ec19d2ebc6b854b744&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756385622</data>
</node>
