  <data key="d2">A. tumefaciens MA92 is a bacterial strain with a longer doubling time of 106.8 minutes compared to E. coli.&lt;SEP&gt;A. tumefaciens MA92 is a bacterial strain that adhered to polystyrene film.&lt;SEP&gt;A. tumefaciens MA92 is a bacterial strain tested for polystyrene degradation but changes were unclear due to excessive bacterial growth.&lt;SEP&gt;A. tumefaciens MA92 is a bacterial strain considered capable of degrading polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;A. tumefaciens MA92 is a bacterial strain isolated from the intestine of mealworms and tested for polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;A. tumefaciens MA92 is a bacterium identified as capable of degrading polystyrene.</data>
