  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">P. nitroreducens MA77 is a bacterial strain sensitive to salt and with a longer doubling time of 113.4 minutes compared to E. coli.&lt;SEP&gt;P. nitroreducens MA77 is a bacterial strain that adhered to polystyrene film.&lt;SEP&gt;P. nitroreducens MA77 is a bacterial strain that reduced the size and sharpness of polystyrene particles.&lt;SEP&gt;P. nitroreducens MA77 is a bacterial strain that consistently exhibited polystyrene degrading activity.&lt;SEP&gt;P. nitroreducens MA77 is a bacterial strain whose growth was influenced by salt concentration and was tested for polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;P. nitroreducens MA77 is a bacterium identified as capable of degrading polystyrene.</data>
