<node id="Digestive Biofragmentation Model">
  <data key="d0">Digestive Biofragmentation Model</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A model developed to predict and unveil the fragmentation process of ingested plastics during biodegradation in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;The digestive biofragmentation model is a simulation tool based on enzymatic surface degradation, used to predict the size-reduction process of plastic particles in the intestinal tract.&lt;SEP&gt;The digestive biofragmentation model is a simulation framework used to estimate the size-reduction process and removal time of ingested PS and PE plastic particles in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;The digestive biofragmentation model is a scientific model used to predict the biodegradation and removal rates of PS and PE particles in insect larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387071</data>
</node>
