  <data key="d0">Mariculture Polystyrene Floats</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Polystyrene floats used in mariculture were fragmented by burrowing invertebrates, leading to the formation of microplastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387073</data>
</node>
<node id="Burrowing Invertebrates">
  <data key="d0">Burrowing Invertebrates</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Burrowing invertebrates induce fragmentation of mariculture polystyrene floats, producing microplastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387074</data>
</node>
<node id="Pyrolyzer-Gas Chromatography Mass Spectrometry (Py-GCMS)">
  <data key="d0">Pyrolyzer-Gas Chromatography Mass Spectrometry (Py-GCMS)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Py-GCMS is an analytical method used in the study to detect microplastics and nanoplastics during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Py-GCMS is an analytical method used in the study to assess the size distribution and mass content of residual plastic particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387074</data>
</node>
<node id="Laser Light Scattering Sizer">
  <data key="d0">Laser Light Scattering Sizer</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">A laser light scattering sizer was used in the study to attempt detection of nanoplastics, with a detection limit of 10 nm.&lt;SEP&gt;The laser light scattering sizer is an analytical method used to measure the size distribution of residual plastic particles.&lt;SEP&gt;A highly sensitive detection method used to analyze nanosized plastic particles in biodegradation studies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387074</data>
</node>
<node id="δ13C Signature">
  <data key="d0">δ13C Signature</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The δ13C signature was used to verify biodegradation of plastics by detecting changes in residual plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;δ13C signature is an isotopic measurement used to confirm biodegradation of plastics by comparing residual plastics in frass with original plastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387074</data>
</node>
<node id="Animal-Based Traditional Medicinal Materials">
  <data key="d0">Animal-Based Traditional Medicinal Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Traditional medicinal materials of animal origin were found to contain PET, PE, PP, and PVC microplastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
