<node id="Superoxide Dismutase (SOD)">
  <data key="d0">Superoxide Dismutase (SOD)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Superoxide Dismutase (SOD) is an enzyme measured as an indicator of oxidative stress in mealworms exposed to microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;SOD activity levels in mealworms were measured to evaluate antioxidant performance.&lt;SEP&gt;SOD is an antioxidant enzyme measured in mealworms, with higher concentrations in plastic-fed groups, particularly PVC-fed mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Superoxide dismutase (SOD) is measured in U/g fresh weight to evaluate antioxidant enzyme activity in mealworms exposed to microplastics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387403</data>
</node>
<node id="Laser Direct Infrared Spectrometry (LDIR)">
  <data key="d0">Laser Direct Infrared Spectrometry (LDIR)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Laser Direct Infrared Spectrometry (LDIR) is a method used to determine the number and depuration time of microplastics in mealworms' intestines.&lt;SEP&gt;Laser direct infrared spectrometry (Agilent 8700 LDIR) was used to identify residual microplastics with a detection limit of 20 μm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756387403</data>
</node>
