<node id="Steps 1-5">
  <data key="d0">Steps 1-5</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Steps 1-5 refer to the sequential stages of DEB model growth curve fitting used in the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388223</data>
</node>
<node id="Volumetric Length">
  <data key="d0">Volumetric Length</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Volumetric length is a measurement used to assess larval growth in the experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;Volumetric length is a measured parameter in larvae that decreases under starvation or insufficient diet conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388223</data>
</node>
<node id="Droppings and Moult Residues">
  <data key="d0">Droppings and Moult Residues</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Droppings and moult residues are a food source tested in the Starvation 2 group, but they were insufficient to maintain life in larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388223</data>
</node>
<node id="Reserve Density (e)">
  <data key="d0">Reserve Density (e)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Reserve density (e) refers to the energy reserves in larvae, which decrease during starvation or insufficient diet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388224</data>
</node>
<node id="Food Availability (f)">
  <data key="d0">Food Availability (f)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Food availability (f) is a modeled parameter representing the accessibility of food for larvae, assumed to be zero in starvation and PS groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388224</data>
</node>
<node id="Energy Conductance (ν)">
  <data key="d0">Energy Conductance (ν)</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Energy conductance (ν) is a fixed parameter estimated from Starvation 1 and used in further modeling steps.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388224</data>
</node>
<node id="DEB Model Parameters">
  <data key="d0">DEB Model Parameters</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">DEB model parameters include $k_M$, $g$, $\hat{r}_B$, $L_{\text{Im}}$, and $\hat{R}$, which describe physiological responses of larvae under different diets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388224</data>
</node>
<node id="$k_M$">
  <data key="d0">$k_M$</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">$k_M$ is a DEB model parameter that decreases under starvation, inhibiting growth of larval structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388224</data>
</node>
<node id="$g$">
  <data key="d0">$g$</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">$g$ is a DEB model parameter that decreases under starvation, contributing to inhibited growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388224</data>
</node>
<node id="$\hat{r}_B$">
  <data key="d0">$\hat{r}_B$</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">$\hat{r}_B$ is a DEB model parameter representing growth rate, which decreases under insufficient diets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388225</data>
</node>
<node id="$L_{\text{Im}}$">
  <data key="d0">$L_{\text{Im}}$</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">$L_{\text{Im}}$ is a DEB model parameter representing maximum volumetric length, which decreases under starvation and insufficient diets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388225</data>
</node>
<node id="$\hat{R}$">
  <data key="d0">$\hat{R}$</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">$\hat{R}$ is a DEB model parameter related to reproduction, which decreases in PS + oat. and PS + oat. + vit. groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388225</data>
</node>
<node id="$L_{\text{S0}}$">
  <data key="d0">$L_{\text{S0}}$</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">$L_{\text{S0}}$ is the structural volume of larvae built before starvation, reached after reserves are depleted.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388225</data>
</node>
<node id="$L_{\text{V0}}$">
  <data key="d0">$L_{\text{V0}}$</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">$L_{\text{V0}}$ is a parameter listed in Table 2, related to larval volume before starvation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388226</data>
</node>
<node id="$L_{\text{Em}}$">
  <data key="d0">$L_{\text{Em}}$</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">$L_{\text{Em}}$ is a parameter listed in Table S4, related to larval energy reserves.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388226</data>
</node>
<node id="$u_V$">
  <data key="d0">$u_V$</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">$u_V$ is a parameter indicating accumulated reserves before starvation, with small differences between groups.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388226</data>
</node>
<node id="Mode 1">
  <data key="d0">Mode 1</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mode 1 is a physiological response pattern where reserve density decreases, explaining reduced growth and reproduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Mode 1 refers to a decrease in reserve density as a mechanism affecting larvae development under PS feeding conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388227</data>
</node>
<node id="Modes 4 or 5">
  <data key="d0">Modes 4 or 5</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Modes 4 or 5 are physiological response patterns associated with decreased DEB parameters $k_M$ and $g$ under starvation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388227</data>
</node>
<node id="Alphitobius diaperinus Panzer">
  <data key="d0">Alphitobius diaperinus Panzer</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Alphitobius diaperinus Panzer is an insect species belonging to the same family (Tenebrionidae) as T. molitor, studied for metabolic responses to food deprivation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388227</data>
</node>
<node id="Starvation Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Starvation Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Starvation conditions refer to experimental feeding scenarios where larvae had insufficient food supply, including PS-only diets.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388228</data>
</node>
<node id="Step 1, Step 2, Step 3, Step 4, Step 5">
  <data key="d0">Step 1, Step 2, Step 3, Step 4, Step 5</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">These steps refer to different stages or conditions of the experimental design, including control, starvation, and PS-based feeding conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388228</data>
</node>
<node id="Mode 2">
  <data key="d0">Mode 2</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mode 2 refers to an increase in somatic maintenance $[\hat{p}_M]$, which was considered but eliminated as it would increase $\hat{r}_B$ and $\hat{R}$.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388228</data>
</node>
<node id="Mode 3">
  <data key="d0">Mode 3</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mode 3 refers to changes in $[E_C]$, which were considered unlikely due to strong homeostasis and minimal incorporation of PS into biomass.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388228</data>
</node>
<node id="Mode 4">
  <data key="d0">Mode 4</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mode 4 refers to a physiological reaction to starvation that could decrease $\hat{r}_B$ and $\hat{R}$.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388229</data>
</node>
<node id="Mode 5">
  <data key="d0">Mode 5</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Mode 5 refers to another physiological reaction to starvation that could decrease $\hat{r}_B$ and $\hat{R}$.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388229</data>
</node>
<node id="Aliphatic hydrocarbons">
  <data key="d0">Aliphatic hydrocarbons</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Aliphatic hydrocarbons are metabolites or degradation products of PS that can occur in faeces of larvae.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1756388229</data>
</node>
