</edge>
<edge source="Yellow Mealworms" target="Gut Microbiome">
  <data key="d6">27.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The gut microbiome of yellow mealworms changed significantly when they were fed a polyether-PU diet.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiome of yellow mealworms was analyzed to study microbial contributions to plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiome of yellow mealworms was analyzed to study bacterial richness and diversity under different diets.</data>
  <data key="d8">diet impact,digestion,gut health,microbial community,microbial ecology</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16c2c8ec44f02a1180cfb4b9e4fb90f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1756385052</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yellow Mealworms" target="Bran">
  <data key="d6">44.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Mealworms fed bran showed high survival rates, serving as a control diet for comparison with polyether-PU foam.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran was used as a food source for yellow mealworms in the study, compared with PVC.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms were fed with bran as a control diet in the experiment.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms fed with bran showed the highest survival and weight gain, serving as the control group.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran was used as a control diet for yellow mealworms in the study.</data>
  <data key="d8">control diet,control group,diet,diet comparison,experimental comparison,growth support,nutrition</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42540a18795e5e2ad9054b7a0edfc3</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1756385050</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yellow Mealworms" target="Unfed Control">
  <data key="d6">8.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Mealworms in the unfed control group had lower survival rates compared to those fed bran or polyether-PU.</data>
  <data key="d8">diet,survival comparison</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-ae42540a18795e5e2ad9054b7a0edfc3</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1756370700</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yellow Mealworms" target="PS (Polystyrene)">
  <data key="d6">26.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Previous studies showed mealworms could consume polystyrene, similar to polyether-PU.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms consumed PS foam and showed extensive biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms were fed with PS to measure survival rates and growth effects.</data>
  <data key="d8">biodegradation,comparative study,diet experiment,diet impact,plastic degradation,survival analysis</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42540a18795e5e2ad9054b7a0edfc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbb6f13dbe3de759712fa3a0c9780470</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1756381662</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yellow Mealworms" target="Polyether-PU Foam">
  <data key="d6">10.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Mealworms fed polyether-PU foam showed high survival rates and consumed the material, indicating its biodegradation potential.</data>
  <data key="d8">biodegradation,diet</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-ae42540a18795e5e2ad9054b7a0edfc3</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1756370701</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Yellow Mealworms" target="PE (Polyethylene)">
  <data key="d6">24.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Previous studies showed mealworms could consume polyethylene, similar to polyether-PU.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms consumed PE foam and showed extensive biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms are mentioned as another species capable of PE biodegradation, possibly through gut microbes.</data>
  <data key="d8">biodegradation,comparative study,diet impact,plastic degradation</data>
