  <data key="d6">60.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Mealworms are capable of consuming and degrading polystyrene as a carbon food source.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms ingest and biodegrade polystyrene, converting it into CO2 and degraded polymer residues.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms were used to biodegrade polystyrene in the experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms were found to consume polystyrene at the highest rates among tested plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms were studied for their ability to degrade polystyrene materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms were fed polystyrene of different molecular weights to study biodegradation.</data>
  <data key="d8">biodegradation,consumption,environmental research,experimental organism,experimental study,plastic breakdown,plastic degradation,waste management</data>
