<edge source="Polyethylene (PE)" target="Mealworm larvae">
  <data key="d6">59.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Mealworm larvae ingest and biodegrade polyethylene, which triggers oxidative stress and metabolic dysbiosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworm larvae ingest and biodegrade PE microplastics, which negatively affect their growth, survival, and physiology.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworm larvae demonstrated the ability to remove and biodegrade polyethylene (PE).&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworm larvae were shown to degrade polyethylene substrates.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms fed with PE showed elevated ROS, SOD, and MDA levels, indicating oxidative stress.</data>
  <data key="d8">biodegradation,environmental impact,experimental substrate,organism impact,oxidative stress,plastic biodegradation,plastic ingestion</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f8516b10110f884279870c2ef887f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
