<edge source="Mealworms" target="PVC">
  <data key="d6">45.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Mealworms metabolized PVC differently depending on the region: Tai'an and Shenzhen showed structural changes, while Guangzhou did not.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms consuming PVC showed little mass change at 10 and 20 days but significant mass reduction at 30 days due to release of organic compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms were fed PVC plastic, which showed similar metabolic effects as HDPE.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms fed with PVC showed the highest oxidative stress and damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms were fed polyvinyl chloride (PVC), which was difficult to chew and led to significant mass loss and low carbohydrate/protein levels.</data>
  <data key="d8">biodegradation,diet,experimental condition,metabolism,oxidative stress,plastic consumption,plastic degradation,plastic digestion,regional variation,toxicity</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff201df58dec460c49cd31920c29f11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63</data>
