  <data key="d11">1756387532</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PS" target="Gentamicin">
  <data key="d6">34.0</data>
  <data key="d7">Gentamicin was tested for its effect on depolymerization of PS during larval experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Gentamicin inhibited depolymerization of PS in Tenebrio molitor larvae according to cited studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Gentamicin suppressed gut microbes in T. molitor larvae, which completely inhibited PS depolymerization.&lt;SEP&gt;Gentamicin treatment inhibited or stopped PS depolymerization in larvae, unlike LDPE.</data>
  <data key="d8">antibiotic effect,biodegradation,depolymerization inhibition,microbial dependence,polymer inhibition</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b</data>
