<edge source="Frass" target="PS (Polystyrene)">
  <data key="d6">72.0</data>
  <data key="d7">The relation **“Frass, PS (Polystyrene)”** refers to the connection between insect frass, particularly that produced by larvae such as mealworms, and the presence of polystyrene (PS) residues or degradation products within it. Frass generated after larvae consume PS foam has been extensively studied to evaluate the extent and mechanisms of PS biodegradation. Analyses of this frass consistently reveal residual PS particles, oligomers, and chemically modified compounds, indicating that ingestion leads to partial depolymerization and transformation of the polymer.  

Chemical characterization of frass has shown evidence of oxidative processes, aromatic ring cleavage, and the formation of specific degradation products, including compounds such as 1,3-di-tert-butyl-2,5-dimethylbenzene. These findings suggest that the digestive activity of larvae induces structural changes in PS, resulting in both residual polymer fragments and newly formed low-molecular-weight substances. In addition to chemical modifications, thermal and solvent-extraction analyses of frass samples have been used to detect changes in PS properties, further confirming biodegradation pathways.  

Overall, the relation highlights that frass serves as a key indicator of PS biodegradation, containing both unaltered polymer residues and chemically transformed products. By examining frass composition, researchers can assess the degree of PS breakdown, identify degradation intermediates, and better understand the biological and chemical processes involved in larval-mediated depolymerization of polystyrene.</data>
  <data key="d8">biodegradation,biodegradation evidence,biodegradation products,chemical transformation,degradation,digestion output,excrement,experimental output,polymer degradation,polymer residues,residual analysis,residual plastics,residue,waste analysis</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6b858a4eb57553f5b1ae041e1c7160</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1756387230</data>
</edge>
