<edge source="T. molitor larvae" target="PET">
  <data key="d6">66.0</data>
  <data key="d7">T. molitor larvae were fed PET, which sustained survival but did not provide adequate nutrition or minerals.&lt;SEP&gt;PET is consumed and biodegraded by T. molitor larvae with higher efficiency compared to other plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae ingest PET as part of their ability to consume various plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae consumed and biodegraded PET, showing significant mass reduction and isotopic enrichment.&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae were able to depolymerize and biodegrade PET independently of gut microbes.&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae were fed PET polymers to study gut microbial responses and biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae are fed PET, and their ability to degrade it is studied.</data>
  <data key="d8">biodegradation,consumption,experimental feeding,feeding,plastic breakdown,plastic consumption,plastic degradation,plastic digestion,plastic ingestion,survival</data>
  <data key="d9">chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f</data>
  <data key="d10">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d11">1756379858</data>
</edge>
<edge source="T. molitor larvae" target="PLA">
  <data key="d6">39.0</data>
  <data key="d7">T. molitor larvae consumed PLA powder with measurable consumption rates.&lt;SEP&gt;PLA is mentioned as more biodegradable than PET, providing a comparison to T. molitor larvae degradation efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae ingest PLA as part of their ability to consume various plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;PLA is degraded by T. molitor larvae, supporting better growth and nutrient retention compared to PS and PVC.&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae fed with PLA MPs showed increased ROS and antioxidant enzyme activity.</data>
  <data key="d8">biodegradation,biodegradation comparison,larval physiology,oxidative stress,plastic degradation,plastic digestion,plastic ingestion</data>
